(window.__pvQ=window.__pvQ||[]).push({"n":0,"of":3,"total":405,"d":[{"u":"pune/pmc-bars-extra-fsi-tdr-builders-until-road-widening-completed.html","h":"PMC bars extra FSI, TDR for builders until road widening is actually completed","s":"No extra FSI or TDR may be granted on the strength of proposed road widening until the road is widened along its entire length, under a circular from the Pune Municipal Commissioner.","k":"PMC, FSI and TDR","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-28T13:50:48+05:30","g":["PMC","FSI","TDR","Road widening","Pune"],"b":"In a circular issued on November 27, Pune Municipal Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram has ordered that no additional Floor Space Index (FSI) or Transferable Development Rights (TDR) benefits be given on the strength of proposed road widening until the road is actually widened along its entire length.\nThe new directive applies to fresh, revised and subsequent construction proposals.\nSeveral construction projects in Pune have been granted premium FSI and TDR benefits based on proposed road widths, even though the roads remain narrow on the ground. Such approvals have placed an additional burden on existing roads and civic infrastructure. The commissioner has specifically highlighted this issue in the circular.\nUnder Section 210 of the Maharashtra Municipal Corporations Act, road-widening proposals are approved with the consent of the Standing Committee. Builders have, however, been receiving additional construction benefits under the Unified Development Control and Promotion Regulations (UDCPR) 2020 even though the proposed widening was not physically completed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-cctv-captures-powerful-blast-trimurti-pharma-kurkumbh-midc.html","h":"CCTV captures powerful blast at Trimurti Pharma in Kurkumbh MIDC","s":"Officials have yet to confirm whether anyone was hurt in the Kurkumbh MIDC explosion, and its cause is unclear.","k":"Kurkumbh MIDC","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-28T13:15:35+05:30","g":["Kurkumbh MIDC","Trimurti Pharma","Daund taluka"],"b":"A powerful explosion at Trimurti Pharma in Kurkumbh MIDC, an industrial area in Pune district’s Daund taluka, was captured by CCTV cameras. Thick plumes of smoke spread across the company premises and into the surrounding area.\nThe cause of the blast remains unclear.\nOfficials have yet to confirm whether anyone was injured or killed, or how much damage the explosion caused.","i":"","a":["Kurkumbh","Daund","Daund taluka","Dound"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fire-mulchand-sons-godown-tulshibagh-market-cause-not-yet-known.html","h":"Fire at Mulchand Sons godown in Pune’s Tulshibagh market, cause not yet known","s":"Shopkeepers and shoppers in the crowded area of a Pune market were alarmed by a godown fire, and its cause and any injuries are yet to be confirmed.","k":"Tulshibagh market","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-27T17:25:29+05:30","g":["Tulshibagh market","Pune","Mulchand Sons","godown fire"],"b":"A fire broke out at the Mulchand Sons godown in Pune’s Tulshibagh market, where Pune Municipal Corporation fire engines and firefighters were at the spot.\nShopkeepers and shoppers in the crowded area were alarmed.\nEarly indications point to a possible electrical short circuit. The cause, the status of the fire and any injuries are yet to be confirmed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/lulla-nagar-uncovered-dumper-hauls-stones-everett-site-traffic.html","h":"Lulla Nagar: uncovered dumper hauls stones from The Everett site through traffic","s":"A person filming an uncovered dumper that came out from the side of The Everett in Lulla Nagar asks when the police and the PMC will act.","k":"Lulla Nagar","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-27T16:52:05+05:30","g":["Lulla Nagar","The Everett","Dumper","PMC"],"b":"An uncovered dumper loaded with excavated stones comes out from the side of The Everett, a Tribeca project in Lulla Nagar, and moves through traffic, a video recorded on the road shows.\nThe dumper hauls the stones from The Everett construction site with nothing covering its load. Two-wheelers and four-wheelers pass close behind and around it.\nThe person filming says that if even one stone falls in such a crowd it could be dangerous, and asks when the police and the PMC will act on it.","i":"","a":["Lulla Nagar"]},{"u":"pune/malthan-youth-alleges-toxic-fairness-cream-pushed-him-to-death-door.html","h":"Malthan youth alleges toxic fairness cream pushed him to death’s door","s":"A Malthan youth says mercury traces from a fairness cream spread through his body and that his treatment cost ₹10 to 12 lakh; his account has not been independently confirmed.","k":"Malthan","c":"City","t":"2026-11-27T15:48:40+05:30","g":["Malthan","Shirur taluka","Fairness cream","Food and Drug Administration","Manipal Hospital"],"b":"A youth from Malthan in Shirur taluka alleges that a toxic fairness cream he ordered online left him fighting for his life and needing treatment in the intensive care unit of Manipal Hospital, Kharadi, Pune.\nHis account has not been independently confirmed, and the cream has not been tested.\nHe says his health turned serious after he used a face-brightening night cream he ordered after seeing advertisements promising a brighter face, and that traces of mercury from the cream spread through his body.\nDoctors saved his life, but he says the treatment cost him ₹10 to 12 lakh.\nHe says he will seek redress against the company before the consumer commission and other competent authorities.\nA demand has been raised that the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) urgently test samples of the cream at an approved laboratory for mercury or other harmful substances, and inquire into its manufacture, sale and permissions.\nHe has urged young people not to fall for attractive advertisements and online claims, and not to use any chemical product on the face without checking its ingredients and safety.","i":"illustration-f3cb303d1b","a":["Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-deccan-remove-commissioner-banners-demand-amitesh-kumar-transfer.html","h":"‘Remove Commissioner’ banners in Deccan, Pune demand Amitesh Kumar’s transfer","s":"Banners in Deccan reading ‘Remove Commissioner’ come amid growing concern over rising crime and a recent machete attack outside the Shivajinagar court.","k":"Deccan, Pune","c":"City","t":"2026-11-27T15:17:07+05:30","g":["Pune","Deccan","Amitesh Kumar","Shivajinagar court"],"b":"Banners reading ‘Remove Commissioner’ have surfaced in Pune’s Deccan area amid growing concern over rising crime in the city, demanding the transfer of Police Commissioner Amitesh Kumar.\nThey have also surfaced amid the recent machete attack outside the Shivajinagar court.\nA series of machete attacks and other criminal incidents across Pune has raised serious concerns over public safety.","i":"","a":["Deccan Gymkhana","Deccan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-man-12-year-old-nephew-drown-farm-pond-moshi.html","h":"Man and 12-year-old nephew drown in farm pond at Moshi","s":"Locals brought a 21-year-old man and his 12-year-old nephew out of the water of a farm pond at Moshi, and doctors at a hospital declared them dead.","k":"Moshi","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-27T14:12:22+05:30","g":["Moshi","Farm pond","Bhosari MIDC police","Accidental death"],"b":"Two residents of Bankar Vasti in Moshi drowned in a farm pond at Moshi on Wednesday night: a 21-year-old man and his 12-year-old nephew.\nThey had gone swimming in a farm pond near their locality on Wednesday evening. Locals brought them out of the water and sent them to a hospital. Doctors there declared them dead.\nInspector Bhojraj Misal of Bhosari MIDC police said the two drowned during the swim. The police have registered a case of accidental death.","i":"illustration-c06690c62e","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-murder-victim-kin-hired-men-kill-accused-says-cp.html","h":"Murder victim’s kin hired men to kill accused outside Pune court, says CP","s":"Six people have been arrested for an attack on a suspect in a Katraj murder, who was shot and severely injured.","k":"Pune court attack","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-27T13:38:04+05:30","g":["Pune","Katraj","Sassoon General Hospital","Pune Commissioner of Police"],"b":"The Pune Commissioner of Police said relatives of a man murdered in Katraj hired the men who attacked the accused in that murder outside a Pune court.\nThe Katraj murder was over a land dispute. The murder victim’s relatives recently tried to have the suspect in that murder killed at the court.\nThe suspect was shot and severely injured, and remains in critical condition at Sassoon General Hospital. The attackers fled shouting that they had avenged the killing.\nSix people have been arrested for the attack. Investigations are under way to uncover the larger conspiracy and the involvement of financiers.","i":"illustration-5bb091c526","a":["Katraj"]},{"u":"pune/pune-shivajinagar-court-attack-reel-taunts-police-claims-group-runs-katraj.html","h":"Shivajinagar court attack: reel taunts Pune police, claims group ‘runs Katraj’","s":"Police suspect the 25 November assault on a man outside the Shivajinagar court was retaliation.","k":"Shivajinagar court attack","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-27T11:32:28+05:30","g":["Shivajinagar court attack","Katraj","Pune police","Pune"],"b":"An Instagram reel posted under the name ‘SC Company Pune City’ taunted Pune police after the 25 November attack outside the Shivajinagar District and Sessions Court.\nThe reel carried a ‘Miss you’ message and a claim that the group ‘runs Katraj’. Whether one of the accused posted it is not verified.\nWitnesses said the attackers made a similar boast as they fled after assaulting a man with koytas outside the court on 25 November.\nThe man had come to court for a hearing in a 2025 murder case in Katraj, in which he was out on bail. Police suspect the assault was retaliation.","i":"","a":["Katraj"]},{"u":"pune/salman-khan-film-shoot-blamed-pune-camp-traffic-chaos.html","h":"Salman Khan film shoot blamed for traffic chaos in Pune's Camp area","s":"Commuters and residents in Camp were left frustrated, and an angry citizen confronted a film crew over traffic restrictions.","k":"Camp traffic","c":"City","t":"2026-11-26T17:31:26+05:30","g":["Pune","Camp","Salman Khan","Traffic"],"b":"A film shoot featuring Salman Khan has been blamed for traffic chaos in Pune's Camp area. Commuters and residents in Camp were left frustrated.\nOver the traffic restrictions, an angry citizen confronted the film crew, leading to a heated exchange.","i":"","a":["Pune Camp","Camp","Pune Cantonment area"]},{"u":"pune/kondhwa-lodge-woman-gang-raped-two-friends-police-say-both-accused-arrested.html","h":"Kondhwa lodge: woman gang-raped by two friends, police say; both accused arrested","s":"Yerawada police have registered a case and arrested two men, and Senior Police Inspector Umesh Gite is investigating further.","k":"Kondhwa","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T17:02:48+05:30","g":["Kondhwa","Yerawada police"],"b":"Police say two of a woman's friends gang-raped her at a lodge in Kondhwa; both accused were arrested after she approached Yerawada police on Tuesday and lodged a complaint.\nThe two men lured her to the lodge about three days before the complaint was filed, and both sexually assaulted her. They then threatened her and warned her not to tell anyone about the incident.\nPolice registered a case. Senior Police Inspector Umesh Gite is conducting further investigation.","i":"illustration-58b4789b61","a":["Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-seize-cannabis-shirur-two-arrested.html","h":"Pune Police seize ₹1.25 crore cannabis in Shirur, two arrested","s":"A Shirur cannabis raid by Pune City Police's Anti-Narcotics Cell, carried out under the guidance of Deputy Commissioner of Police (Crime Branch) Gauhar Hasan, has a total seizure worth about ₹1.51 crore, including an SUV and mobile phones.","k":"Shirur","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T16:28:15+05:30","g":["Pune","Shirur","Cannabis","Anti-Narcotics Cell","Pune Rural"],"b":"Pune City Police's Anti-Narcotics Cell seized about 250 kg of cannabis worth ₹1.25 crore in a raid on the SBI Colony area of Shirur, in Pune Rural, and arrested two people from Amravati.\nThe total seizure, including an SUV and mobile phones, is worth about ₹1.51 crore. The team acted on specific intelligence.\nAccording to preliminary information, police say the two belonged to a drug supply network operating across the state and supplied cannabis to various parts of Maharashtra.\nDeputy Commissioner of Police (Crime Branch) Gauhar Hasan guided the operation. Further investigation is under way to identify others involved in the network and to trace the source of the seized cannabis.","i":"","a":["Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-shivajinagar-court-three-bomb-threat-emails-after-daylight-murder.html","h":"Bomb threat emails again target Shivajinagar court a day after daylight murder","s":"After three bomb threat emails, Pune's Shivajinagar District Court, which has seen serious incidents in 2004, 2012, 2013, 2016, 2018 and 2026, faces the question of why it continues to face such threats and who is behind the emails.","k":"Shivajinagar court","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-26T15:56:30+05:30","g":["Shivajinagar","Bomb threat emails","Court security","Pune"],"b":"While a session related to the case was under way, three bomb threat emails reached Pune's Shivajinagar District Court a day after a daylight murder near its Gate No. 4.\nQuestions are now being raised about CCTV surveillance, boundary walls and security arrangements at the court, especially after a damaged boundary wall was demolished but not rebuilt.\nThe court has seen serious incidents in 2004, 2012, 2013, 2016, 2018 and 2026.\nThe repeated threats have raised a larger question: despite multiple incidents and security measures, why does the court continue to face such threats, and who is behind the emails?","i":"","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/baramati-thar-driver-rams-traffic-policeman-flees-samyak-chowk.html","h":"Thar driver's high-handedness in Baramati: rams traffic policeman at Samyak Chowk, then flees","s":"After hitting a traffic policeman at Samyak Chowk in Baramati, a Thar driver fled, causing a stir in the area.","k":"Baramati","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-26T15:24:53+05:30","g":["Baramati","Thar","CCTV","Samyak Chowk"],"b":"A Thar driver rammed a traffic policeman with force at Samyak Chowk in Baramati and fled the spot, a display of high-handedness.\nCCTV cameras captured the whole incident.\nThe driver's escape after hitting a traffic policeman has caused a stir in the area.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-zp-teachers-suspended-fake-disability-claims-more-cases-may-emerge.html","h":"Five Pune ZP teachers suspended over fake disability claims; more cases may emerge","s":"Five Pune Zilla Parishad teachers' suspensions are part of a wider verification exercise in which 46 of 176 certificates examined in the first phase were found to be fake.","k":"Pune ZP teachers","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-26T14:52:15+05:30","g":["Pune Zilla Parishad","Disability certificates","Teacher suspensions"],"b":"Medical re-checks found the disability of five Pune Zilla Parishad teachers from Shirur, Khed, Ambegaon and Haveli talukas far below their certificates, and the teachers have been suspended.\nPune ZP chief executive officer Gajanan Patil confirmed the action on Wednesday, saying all five teachers had been suspended after their disability levels were found to be below the prescribed 40% benchmark. Under the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016, a person must have at least 40% of a specified disability to qualify as a person with benchmark disability and access the associated statutory benefits.\nThe assessments put the five teachers' disability levels at between 0% and 10%, against the 18% to 60% recorded in their disability certificates. In one case, an assessment fell from 52% to zero.\nThe suspensions over fake disability claims are part of a wider verification exercise begun after complaints that some teachers had submitted questionable disability certificates to secure transfers under the differently-abled category.\nIn Pune district, as many as 409 teachers submitted disability certificates during the ZP teacher transfer process. In the first phase, 176 certificates were examined and 46 were found to be fake. More cases may emerge.","i":"illustration-7b4d6560fe","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-court-attack-killed-man-brother-alleged-mastermind.html","h":"Billhook attack outside Pune court: brother of man killed in Katraj alleged mastermind","s":"A murder accused attacked with billhooks outside the Pune district court on Wednesday is in critical condition, Sassoon General Hospital medical superintendent Yallappa Jadhav said.","k":"Court attack","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T13:50:02+05:30","g":["Pune","Shivajinagar","Court attack","Pune Police"],"b":"Assailants chased down a murder accused and struck him with billhooks outside the district and sessions court in Shivajinagar around 1pm on Wednesday afternoon, as he stepped out of Gate 4.\nThe attack took place close to the Civil Court Metro station. The man, released on bail from Yerawada Central Prison about four days earlier, had come to court in connection with a murder case.\nHis hands were almost chopped off near the wrists and he suffered a skull fracture. He was taken to Sassoon General Hospital, where medical superintendent Yallappa Jadhav said his condition is critical.\nPolice detained the assailants near Daund after a nearly three-hour chase, and Pune crime branch officers found two pistols at the spot.\nPolice investigations show the brother of a man killed in Katraj last year was the alleged mastermind behind the attack. The injured man is an accused in that murder.\nJoint commissioner of police Sanjay Darade said, “Prima facie, the attack outside the court was the fallout of a murder in Katraj last year.”\nPune Bar Association secretary Samrat Jambhulkar said everyone entering the court premises should be thoroughly checked and CCTV cameras installed.","i":"illustration-ad5381dca5","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/shivajinagar-court-attack-six-in-police-custody-including-minor.html","h":"Shivajinagar court attack: six in Pune Police custody, including a minor","s":"Five adults and a child in conflict with law are among six people in custody in the attempt-to-murder investigation into an attack near Pune District Court.","k":"Shivajinagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T13:17:11+05:30","g":["Shivajinagar","Pune District Court","Pune Police","attempt to murder"],"b":"Pune Police have taken six people, including a minor, into custody over an attack near Gate 4 of Pune District Court in Shivajinagar, close to the Metro station, around 1 pm on November 25.\nFour persons attacked a man with sharp weapons. He suffered serious injuries, including an injury that left his wrist severed, and was shifted to a hospital for treatment.\nTwo firearms were recovered from the scene. Police said no firearm injuries were noticed prima facie, based on feedback from the treating doctors.\nFive of the six in custody are adults; the sixth is a child in conflict with law. They have been taken into custody as part of the attempt-to-murder investigation, and police are working to establish their individual roles.\nDCP (Crime Branch) Gauhar Hasan confirmed the development on November 26. Further investigation is under way.","i":"illustration-95991b170b","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-bopdev-ghat-tempo-ploughs-into-engineering-students-three-killed.html","h":"Pune: Tempo ploughs into engineering students at Bopdev Ghat bus stop, three killed, two critical","s":"Five students were injured at a Bopdev Ghat bus stop and three of them died during treatment; police have arrested a tempo driver.","k":"Bopdev Ghat","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-26T12:44:58+05:30","g":["Pune","Bopdev Ghat","engineering students","Yewalewadi police"],"b":"A tempo ploughed into engineering students waiting at a bus stop outside their college in front of KJ Education Institute in Bopdev Ghat around 2.30 pm on Wednesday, killing three and critically injuring two.\nFive students were injured and rushed to different hospitals. Three of them, including a girl, died during treatment; the other two are undergoing treatment. Police have arrested the tempo driver.\nInspector Maruti Patil of Yewalewadi police station said, as per a preliminary probe, the tempo was coming down the road sloping from Bopdev Ghat when it rammed into a car travelling ahead of it, and the driver then lost control and ploughed into the students.\nThe institute's Executive Director said the students were in their second or third year of engineering and were returning after their exams. They were standing at the PMPML bus stop, which students use regularly, and not on the road, he said.\nHe added that no such incident had happened in the last 20 years, and that authorities should look for a solution to overspeeding and rash driving.","i":"illustration-75c6bf542f","a":["Yewalewadi","Yevalewadi"]},{"u":"pune/ambegaon-budruk-couple-booked-allegedly-cheating-investors-gold-scheme.html","h":"Ambegaon Budruk couple booked for allegedly cheating investors of ₹31.68 lakh in gold investment scheme","s":"According to a complaint by a 38-year-old private-sector employee from Ambegaon Khurd, investors in a gold investment scheme handed over cash, online payments and gold ornaments.","k":"Ambegaon Budruk","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T11:41:23+05:30","g":["Pune","Ambegaon","Gold investment scheme","Ambegaon police"],"b":"An Ambegaon Budruk couple has been booked over a gold investment scheme in which they allegedly cheated investors of ₹31.68 lakh. Ambegaon police registered the case on November 24.\nThe couple allegedly ran the scheme as “government-approved” and promised attractive returns.\nThe complaint was filed by a 38-year-old private-sector employee from Ambegaon Khurd. According to the complaint, investors handed over cash, online payments and gold ornaments, including old jewellery promised in exchange for new pieces.\nThe couple allegedly withheld 965.65 grams of gold jewellery. The investors allegedly got neither their money nor their gold back despite repeated demands.\nThe case is under Sections 316(2), 316(5), 318(4) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and Sections 3 and 4 of the Maharashtra Protection of Interest of Depositors (MPID) Act, 1999. Police are investigating the scheme and the whereabouts of the assets.","i":"illustration-b2d252cbfc","a":["Ambegaon Budruk","Ambegaon Bk"]},{"u":"pune/vishrambag-man-23-attacked-near-sm-joshi-bridge-alleged-investment-dispute.html","h":"Vishrambag: man, 23, attacked near S.M. Joshi Bridge in alleged investment dispute","s":"A 23-year-old man injured in an attack in Vishrambag has alleged that four youths were sent to take his life by two men angered by his repeated demands to return money given for investment.","k":"Vishrambag","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-26T10:41:40+05:30","g":["Pune","Vishrambag","S.M. Joshi Bridge"],"b":"A 23-year-old man was attacked with an iron weapon by four unidentified youths aged 18 to 22 at 4:15 am on 24 November 2026, near the S.M. Joshi Bridge crematorium in Vishrambag, Pune.\nThe 23-year-old suffered injuries to his head and both arms.\nHe has alleged that two men, aged 25 and around 50, angered by his repeated demands to return money given for investment, called him to the spot and sent the four youths to take his life.\nA case has been registered at Vishrambag Police Station, and police are investigating.","i":"illustration-ade69f6fa6","a":[]},{"u":"pune/loud-late-night-film-shoot-sopan-baug-disturbing-societies.html","h":"Loud late-night film shoot in Sopan Baug disturbs societies, keeps area awake","s":"Housing societies across Sopan Baug are affected by the sound of a film shoot at an hour when the area should be quiet.","k":"Sopan Baug","c":"City","t":"2026-11-25T23:20:42+05:30","g":["Pune","Sopan Baug","Film shoot","Housing societies"],"b":"Housing societies across Sopan Baug are being disturbed late at night by the loud sound of a film shoot that is going on in the area.\nThe disturbance is not confined to one building: societies across Sopan Baug in general are affected. The sound has been really disturbing the housing societies in the area.\nIt comes at an hour when the area should be quiet. The shoot keeps Sopan Baug awake, and the societies are angry.","i":"","a":["Sopan Baug"]},{"u":"pune/bopdev-ghat-eicher-tempo-rammed-students-bus-stop-two-die.html","h":"Bopdev Ghat bus stop: Eicher tempo rammed into students, two die, three seriously injured","s":"Police have reached the scene where an Eicher tempo hit students waiting at a Bopdev Ghat bus stop, and further details are awaited.","k":"Bopdev Ghat","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-25T18:15:06+05:30","g":["Pune","Bopdev Ghat","Eicher tempo","Students"],"b":"Two students died on the spot and three others were seriously injured as an Eicher tempo rammed into a group of students who were waiting at a bus stop in Bopdev Ghat, Pune.\nPolice reached the scene, and the investigation is under way. Further details are awaited.","i":"illustration-28868b1d05","a":[]},{"u":"pune/shivajinagar-sessions-court-man-shot-at-attacked-koyta-police-detain-suspect.html","h":"Shivajinagar sessions court: man shot at, attacked with koyta; police detain one suspect","s":"Preliminary information is that a man shot at and attacked with a koyta at the Shivajinagar sessions court in Pune is an accused in a murder case who came out on bail only four days earlier.","k":"Shivajinagar sessions court","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T17:05:14+05:30","g":["Pune","Shivajinagar","Sessions court","Pune police","Sassoon Hospital"],"b":"A gang of six opened fire on a man in the premises of the Shivajinagar sessions court in Pune, then struck him with a koyta and fled the spot. One suspect has been taken into custody.\nPreliminary information is that the man is an accused in a murder case registered at Ambegaon police station. Preliminary information is also that he came out on bail only four days earlier and had come to the court premises for some court work.\nThe injured man was admitted to Sassoon Hospital, where he is undergoing treatment. Pune police and a crime branch team rushed to the spot.\nPune police said initial information was that three to four people carried out the attack, but the exact number of attackers and their identity are not yet clear.\nAsked about a possible link to a murder in Katraj last year, police said the identity of the attackers, the motive and any link to last year's incident are all under investigation.\nPune has seen three attacks on court premises since 2017, and this is not the first.","i":"illustration-56217d6b7b","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-metro-line-3-to-open-two-more-stations-from-november-25.html","h":"Pune Metro Line 3 to open two more stations from November 25","s":"Pune Metro Line 3's two new stations will keep the same operating hours as the route's other stations.","k":"Pune Metro","c":"City","t":"2026-11-25T16:33:14+05:30","g":["Pune Metro","Metro Line 3","Balewadi Phata","Balewadi High Street","Balewadi"],"b":"Pune Metro Line 3 will open two more stations, Balewadi Phata and Balewadi High Street, to passengers on Wednesday, November 25, 2026, becoming operational at 3:30 pm.\nBoth stations will become operational following authorisation from the Commissioner of Metro Rail Safety (CMRS). Pune Metro's passenger advisory sets out the opening time.\nOperating hours at the two stations will be the same as those of the other stations on the route. The new stations are expected to improve connectivity for residents, office-goers and visitors travelling to and from the Balewadi area.","i":"illustration-3d5fec3afc","a":["Balewadi"]},{"u":"pune/pimpalgaon-joga-leopard-attacks-women-harvesting-paddy-junnar-one-dies.html","h":"Leopard attacks women harvesting paddy at Pimpalgaon Joga in Junnar; one dies, the other injured","s":"Fear has spread through the Pimpalgaon Joga area of Junnar taluka, where a leopard attacked two women, and a forest department team has left for the spot.","k":"Pimpalgaon Joga","c":"City","t":"2026-11-25T16:01:55+05:30","g":["Junnar","Leopard attack","Pimpalgaon Joga","Pune"],"b":"At about 1:45 pm on Wednesday, 25 November, according to preliminary information, a leopard attacked two women in the Bhoirwadi area of Pimpalgaon Joga, Junnar taluka. The women were harvesting paddy in a field when the leopard suddenly attacked them.\nOne woman died and the other was injured.\nFarmers and residents are worried, and the attack has spread fear in the Pimpalgaon Joga area. A forest department team has left for the spot.","i":"illustration-3e9894eb55","a":["Junnar","Junnar taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-four-attackers-cut-off-youth-hand-sickles-shivajinagar-court.html","h":"Pune: four attackers try to fire at youth, cut off his hand with sickles outside Shivajinagar court","s":"Deputy Commissioner of Police (Crime), Pune City, Gauhar Hasan said that suspects in an attack on a youth outside the Shivajinagar district court have been identified and will be arrested soon.","k":"Shivajinagar court","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T14:58:38+05:30","g":["Shivajinagar court","Katraj","Santoshnagar","Gauhar Hasan"],"b":"Four attackers tried to fire at a youth from two pistols outside the Shivajinagar district court in Pune at about 1.15 pm on Wednesday, 25 November, then cut off one of his hands at the wrist with sickles when the bullets did not go off.\nThey had surrounded him outside chamber no. 63 of the court. The sickles were ones they had brought, and all four fled the spot.\nThe youth, a resident of the Katraj area, is being treated in a hospital’s intensive care unit. A preliminary medical examination found that he had not been hit by a bullet.\nAccording to preliminary police information, he was the main accused in a murder at Santoshnagar, Katraj, on 20 April 2025 over a land and money dispute, and had come out on bail only four days earlier. He had come to the court for court proceedings on Wednesday.\nPolice drew up a panchnama at the spot and seized two pistols. The preliminary assessment is that the attack was carried out over past enmity, to avenge the earlier murder.\nGauhar Hasan, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Crime), Pune City, said the suspects have been identified and several police teams have been sent to trace them, and that they will be arrested soon.","i":"illustration-b8eec95e50","a":["Katraj"]},{"u":"pune/pune-daylight-gunfire-outside-shivajinagar-court-sickle-attack-two-pistols-found.html","h":"Daylight gunfire outside Shivajinagar Court in Pune: sickle attack, two pistols found","s":"A forensic team and senior police officials reached the scene of the firing outside Shivajinagar Court in Pune, where two pistols were recovered, according to preliminary information.","k":"Shivajinagar Court","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T14:24:51+05:30","g":["Pune","Shivajinagar Court","Sickle attack","Firing"],"b":"Gunfire broke out in broad daylight outside Shivajinagar Court in Pune, near Gate No. 4, and, according to preliminary information, a person who tried to flee towards the Family Court after the firing was attacked with a sickle and seriously injured.\nHe was rushed to Sassoon General Hospital for treatment. Two pistols were recovered from the spot, according to preliminary information.\nSenior police officials and a forensic team reached the scene to investigate and collect evidence. The exact circumstances behind the firing and the attack are yet to be established.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-encroachment-drive-online-war-on-x-ram-vs-zagade.html","h":"Pune encroachment drive sparks online war on X: PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram vs Mahesh Zagade","s":"Ankush Kakade said Mahesh Zagade, who had served as PMC, PMRDA and Food and Drugs commissioner, had not taken up the encroachment issue in his tenure.","k":"Encroachment drive","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-25T13:52:13+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Naval Kishore Ram","Mahesh Zagade","Encroachment drive"],"b":"PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram and Mahesh Zagade, a former IAS officer, are in an online war on X that Pune’s encroachment drive has sparked.\nRam questioned, in a post on his official X account, what Zagade had done during his own tenure.\nAnkush Kakade, asked about the war of words, said that when one points a finger at someone, four fingers point back. He said Zagade had served as PMC commissioner, PMRDA commissioner and Food and Drugs commissioner and must have done some work in his tenure, but had not taken up the encroachment issue then.\nKakade said encroachment has now come to the fore, and the commissioner’s ego appeared hurt after members of some parties took him to task in the house and used unwanted words.\nHe said it was not for a worker like him to advise two IAS officers or step into their dispute. He said Zagade, also a Punekar, should meet Ram and discuss what help he could offer, and that Ram should take his advice if he found it appropriate and necessary.\n“Ultimately, both of them should look at what is in the interest of Punekars,” Kakade said.","i":"illustration-50a3689d6c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/shivajinagar-pmc-razes-illegal-shed-fountain-hotel.html","h":"Shivajinagar: PMC razes illegal shed at Fountain Hotel; residents question ‘open bar’","s":"Several hotels and bars in Shivajinagar face complaints over dining tables in parking areas and alleged breaches of Food and Drug Administration (FDA) norms and late-night operating hours.","k":"Shivajinagar","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-25T13:20:19+05:30","g":["Shivajinagar","Fountain Hotel","PMC","Pune"],"b":"In Shivajinagar, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) encroachment department has razed an unauthorised shed at Fountain Hotel, and residents question how an open bar allegedly ran under the illegal structure without notice from the State Excise Department.\nLocals have also alleged that action against neighbouring eateries was merely tokenistic. They are asking who is shielding the establishments whose spillover parking causes severe traffic congestion on surrounding roads.\nComplaints have also surfaced against several hotels and bars in Shivajinagar for placing dining tables in designated parking areas, forcing patrons to park on the streets and obstructing public movement. The complaints also include alleged violations of Food and Drug Administration (FDA) norms and late-night operating hours.\nCitizens are now asking whether the Municipal Commissioner, the State Excise Superintendent, the FDA Commissioner and the Police Commissioner will take decisive action against the violators.","i":"","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-koyta-wielding-rival-gangs-clash-keshavnagar-manjari-road-society.html","h":"Panic as koyta-wielding rival gangs clash at Keshavnagar-Manjari Road housing society","s":"Residents of a housing society on Keshavnagar-Manjari Road await strict police action against those involved in a clash between rival koyta-wielding gangs.","k":"Keshavnagar-Manjari Road","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T12:39:10+05:30","g":["Keshavnagar-Manjari Road","Koyta-wielding gangs","CCTV"],"b":"Rival koyta-wielding gangs clashed over dominance at a housing society on Pune’s Keshavnagar-Manjari Road, causing panic, and the whole incident was captured on CCTV.\nGang members allegedly entered the society armed with koytas and tried to attack members of the rival group, leaving residents in fear.\nResidents are awaiting strict police action against those involved.","i":"","a":["Keshav Nagar"]},{"u":"pune/talegaon-dabhade-police-arrest-employee-accomplice-allegedly-hacking-senior.html","h":"Talegaon Dabhade police arrest employee, accomplice for allegedly hacking senior colleague to death","s":"Police say a 23-year-old employee plotted to kill a 36-year-old senior colleague who had slapped him during an argument about a month ago.","k":"Talegaon Dabhade","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T12:07:10+05:30","g":["Talegaon Dabhade","Maval","Shirgaon police","Ozarde"],"b":"The body of a 36-year-old man from Somatane Phata in Talegaon Dabhade was found in Ozarde around 10am on Monday. Talegaon Dabhade police have arrested a 23-year-old employee and his accomplice for allegedly hacking his senior colleague to death.\nHe left home around 7pm on Sunday to get kharwas (colostrum pudding) for his son. His wife approached Talegaon Dabhade police when he did not return, and a case of abduction was registered. A case of murder was registered with Shirgaon police.\nPolice say the accused, the victim's colleague from Sadvali village in Maval taluka, called him to Urse village on the pretext of giving him kharwas. The accused then took him on his motorcycle to a secluded spot near Ozarde, where the two allegedly hacked him to death with a billhook.\nPolice traced and detained the employee, who confessed during questioning. They then arrested his 26-year-old accomplice.\nPolice say the victim, the accused's senior at the company, had slapped him during an argument about a month ago, after which the accused plotted to kill him.\nSenior Police Inspector Devendra Chavan of Shirgaon police gave the details. Both have been handed over to Talegaon Dabhade police for further investigation.","i":"illustration-c18b60697d","a":["Talegaon Dabhade","Talegaon","Maval","Mawal","Maval taluka"]},{"u":"pune/fda-cancels-drug-licences-of-jejuri-inducare-again-nine-medicines-fail.html","h":"FDA cancels drug licences of Jejuri's Inducare again as nine medicines fail quality tests","s":"Government analysts declared nine medicines of Inducare Pharmaceutical and Research Foundation, located in Additional MIDC, Jejuri, substandard, misbranded or spurious.","k":"Jejuri","c":"City","t":"2026-11-25T10:57:34+05:30","g":["FDA","Inducare Pharmaceutical","Jejuri","Drug quality"],"b":"Inducare Pharmaceutical and Research Foundation, located in Additional MIDC, Jejuri, in Pune district, has had its drug manufacturing licences cancelled once again by the Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The action follows the finding that the company manufactured and sold nine medicines without obtaining mandatory product permissions.\nGovernment analysts declared all nine substandard, misbranded or spurious.\nLaboratory tests found that two of the medicines lacked their essential active ingredients. Ibucare Plus tablets had no Ibuprofen, and Carevita-M tablets had none of nine specified vitamins and other ingredients. Both were declared spurious.\nAmong the other findings, Carezinc had only 72.73% of its Vitamin C content, Carepanta D2 only 40.90% of its Pantoprazole and I-Sartan M only 62.28% of its Metoprolol Succinate.\nLDLR-5, DomiCare and Caremide failed dissolution tests. They carried misbranding, incorrect labelling or incorrect ingredient details.","i":"illustration-2927c99349","a":["Jejuri"]},{"u":"pune/model-colony-youths-create-ruckus-police-barricades-dhotre-chowk.html","h":"Model Colony: youths create ruckus with police barricades at Dhotre Chowk","s":"Youths with police barricades in Pune's Model Colony feature in a video that has surfaced on social media.","k":"Model Colony","c":"City","t":"2026-11-25T10:24:03+05:30","g":["Pune","Model Colony","Dhotre Chowk","Police barricades"],"b":"At around 10:40 pm on 23 November, youths who came on Bullet motorcycles handled police barricades and created chaos at Dhotre Chowk in Pune's Model Colony.\nA video of the youths' ruckus with the police barricades has surfaced on social media.","i":"","a":["Model Colony"]},{"u":"pune/pune-bibwewadi-bungalow-gold-silver-cash-stolen.html","h":"Bibwewadi bungalow: gold, silver and cash worth ₹20.5 lakh stolen","s":"Jewellery and cash worth an estimated ₹20.5 lakh were stolen from a Dhavalagiri Society bungalow in Bibwewadi, an area that has seen other recent theft-related incidents.","k":"Bibwewadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-25T07:35:00+05:30","g":["Bibwewadi","Theft","Dhavalagiri Society","Pune"],"b":"A bungalow in Pune's Bibwewadi, No. 26/A in Dhavalagiri Society, has lost gold and silver jewellery and cash worth an estimated ₹20.5 lakh to theft.\nThis is not the first recent theft-related incident in the area. On November 8, gold jewellery and cash worth ₹3.28 lakh were stolen from a home in Sukhsagarnagar, Bibwewadi.\nEarlier, on November 2, an alert 62-year-old resident noticed three suspicious men entering the building and foiled a burglary attempt on Kondhwa-Bibwewadi Road.\nConcerns are growing among residents over repeated incidents in and around Bibwewadi.","i":"illustration-8e7775c279","a":["Bibwewadi","Bibvewadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-special-mcoca-court-rejects-amit-kangude-bail-plea.html","h":"Pune: Special MCOCA court rejects Amit Kangude’s bail plea in Sharad Mohol murder","s":"A Special MCOCA court in Pune has rejected Amit Maruti Kangude’s bail plea and directed that the trial be expedited, as Kangude has been in judicial custody for more than two years.","k":"Sharad Mohol murder","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-25T05:34:02+05:30","g":["Sharad Mohol","Amit Kangude","MCOCA","bail plea"],"b":"In an order passed on November 23, Special MCOCA Judge HM Bhosale rejected the bail application of Amit Maruti Kangude, who is accused in the Sharad Mohol murder and allegedly took part in the shooting that killed gangster Sharad Mohol, at the Special Maharashtra Control of Organised Crime Act (MCOCA) Court in Pune.\nSpecial Public Prosecutor Pradeepsingh Rajput strongly opposed the bail plea. The advocates for the Mohol family also argued against it.\nThe prosecution cited eyewitness statements, Kangude’s identification during the identification parade, CCTV footage and audio recordings of conversations with co-accused. It also told the court that a country-made pistol and live cartridges were recovered on information given by Kangude.\nThe court took serious note of two eyewitnesses identifying Kangude in the identification parade, along with the CCTV footage and the weapon seizure. Considering these and the stringent bail conditions under Section 21(4) of MCOCA, it rejected the application.\nAs Kangude has been in judicial custody for more than two years, the court directed that the trial be expedited. It ordered all the accused to be produced before it to complete the framing of charges. It also directed the Special Public Prosecutor to submit draft charges and argue on them.","i":"illustration-519e5e0e4b","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-syed-nagar-tension-stones-allegedly-pelted-jcb-pmc-encroachment-drive.html","h":"Syed Nagar tension: stones allegedly pelted at JCB during PMC encroachment drive","s":"Tension erupted near Ganga Village on Handewadi Road in Hadapsar while officials were removing illegal encroachments.","k":"Syed Nagar","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-24T15:32:32+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Syed Nagar","Hadapsar","encroachment drive"],"b":"Tension erupted at Syed Nagar in Hadapsar after stones were allegedly pelted at a JCB machine during the Pune Municipal Corporation's (PMC) encroachment drive.\nOfficials were removing illegal encroachments at the time. Syed Nagar is near Ganga Village on Handewadi Road, Hadapsar.\nThe Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) continued its anti-encroachment drive across the city for the sixth consecutive day.","i":"","a":["Hadapsar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-navale-bridge-truck-overturns-multi-vehicle-crash-injured.html","h":"Pune’s Navale Bridge: truck overturns in multi-vehicle crash, 5–6 injured","s":"A truck overturned on Pune’s Navale Bridge in a crash involving three trucks and a four-wheeler, and no one was killed.","k":"Navale Bridge","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-24T14:59:16+05:30","g":["Navale Bridge","Truck accident","Pune"],"b":"Five to six people were injured in a multi-vehicle crash involving three trucks and a four-wheeler near the Swaminarayan Temple on Pune’s Navale Bridge at around 2 am.\nOne of the trucks overturned, apparently after its driver lost control. The vehicles involved were badly damaged, but no one was killed.\nPolice reached the spot and have started investigating what led to the collision.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-solapur-road-traffic-cop-allegedly-demands-money-motorist.html","h":"Pune–Solapur Road: traffic cop allegedly demands money from motorist, then gestures for more","s":"A traffic cop on Pune–Solapur Road allegedly gestured for more after a motorist handed over two to three ₹100 notes, in an incident recorded on camera.","k":"Pune–Solapur Road","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-24T13:57:19+05:30","g":["Pune","Pune–Solapur Road","Traffic police","e-challan"],"b":"On Pune–Solapur Road, a uniformed traffic cop allegedly demanded money from a motorist after stopping the vehicle, in an incident recorded on camera.\nThe motorist handed over two to three ₹100 notes. The traffic cop allegedly appeared dissatisfied with the amount and gestured for more money.\nThe incident has sparked controversy on social media. It has raised questions about roadside cash collections and whether traffic violations are being addressed through the official e-challan system.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-hinjawadi-software-engineer-found-dead-pg-after-alleged-row-boyfriend.html","h":"Hinjawadi software engineer, 27, found dead at PG after alleged row with boyfriend","s":"The boyfriend of a 27-year-old software engineer found dead in Hinjawadi is in custody, and a case has been registered at Hinjawadi Police Station.","k":"Hinjawadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-24T13:35:43+05:30","g":["Hinjawadi","Software engineer","Hinjawadi Police Station"],"b":"A 27-year-old software engineer was found dead at her paying guest accommodation in Hinjawadi in the early hours of Monday, after an alleged 3 am row with her boyfriend, whom police have arrested.\nThe woman, a native of Wardha, worked with Wipro. Her boyfriend is an Infosys employee from Buldhana. Her paying guest accommodation is in Sakore Vasti.\nPolice say the couple had been in a relationship for more than three years and their families had agreed to their marriage. Police say tensions had allegedly developed after she suspected him of being involved with another woman.\nPolice say the 3 am row was over the relationship.\nAccording to police, an argument broke out around 3 am after the two returned from a hotel visit. It allegedly turned into a physical confrontation, in which he is accused of assaulting her with his hands. Police said no weapon was involved.\nThe boyfriend allegedly stayed beside her body through the night and called the 112 emergency helpline the next morning after finding her unresponsive. Doctors declared her dead on arrival at hospital.\nDeputy Commissioner of Police (Zone 2) Pradeep Jadhav said the initial investigation pointed to a dispute between the couple. A case has been registered at Hinjawadi Police Station and the accused is in custody.\nSenior Police Inspector Balaji Pandhare is investigating. The post-mortem findings will be key to knowing the cause of death.","i":"illustration-da3d02af65","a":["Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-pcmc-seek-data-private-hospitals-after-gbs-linked-death.html","h":"PMC, PCMC to seek data from private hospitals after GBS-linked death","s":"PCMC health chief Dr Laxman Gophane said Guillain-Barré Syndrome (GBS) cases have seen no unusual surge, but sporadic cases are possible.","k":"GBS","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-24T13:13:30+05:30","g":["GBS","PMC","PCMC","Private hospitals","Kalewadi"],"b":"After a 36-year-old teacher from Kalewadi died of Guillain-Barré Syndrome (GBS) at Yashwantrao Chavan Memorial Hospital (YCMH) on November 22, PMC and PCMC will seek details of all GBS patients treated at private hospitals.\nOfficials said she had first gone to a private hospital with weakness in her legs and, as her condition worsened, was admitted to the ICU at the civic-run New Thergaon Hospital and then shifted to YCMH.\nThe exercise aims to identify unusual trends in GBS cases and deaths that may go unreported to civic health departments. GBS is not a notifiable disease, so hospitals are not routinely required to report every case to the government.\nYCMH dean Dr Rajendra Wabale said the hospital is also collecting the numbers of GBS patients it treated in the past three months, and that the teacher was clinically a confirmed GBS patient.\nPCMC health chief Dr Laxman Gophane said YCMH doctors have been asked to check whether nerve conduction tests were done on the teacher.\n“There is a possibility of sporadic cases, but there has been no unusual surge in GBS cases,”\nGophane said\nGophane added that PCMC will write to all private hospitals for details of GBS patients reported this year. PMC health chief Dr Nina Borade said the PMC would issue instructions to collect data from private hospitals.\nThe PMC reported 141 suspected GBS cases from January 9 last year, 120 of them confirmed, particularly in Nande Gaon, Nanded, Dhayari, Kirkitwadi and Khadakwasla. That was the largest cluster in the country. Borade said that outbreak was waterborne and linked to Norovirus and Campylobacter jejuni.\nAdditional Municipal Commissioner Pavneet Kaur said the PMC has secured approval for an ₹890-crore water supply project covering 12 villages affected during the outbreak, and that the chlorination system has since been automated.","i":"illustration-694beb8eaa","a":["Kalewadi"]},{"u":"pune/pimpri-chinchwad-water-supply-shut-citywide-november-26.html","h":"Pimpri-Chinchwad water supply to remain shut citywide on November 26","s":"Pimpri-Chinchwad residents have been advised to store water in advance for the citywide shutdown on Thursday, November 26.","k":"Pimpri-Chinchwad","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-24T12:47:50+05:30","g":["Pimpri-Chinchwad","Water supply","Nigdi"],"b":"Water supply will remain shut across Pimpri-Chinchwad on Thursday, November 26, and is expected to resume on Friday, November 27.\nThe citywide shutdown is due to maintenance and repair work at the water treatment plant and the water distribution system in Nigdi Sector 23.\nOn resumption, residents may see low pressure and an irregular supply during the morning.\nCitizens have been advised to store sufficient water in advance and use it carefully to avoid inconvenience.","i":"illustration-169be4a1da","a":["Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-fails-to-explain-why-it-permitted-47-nullah-diversions.html","h":"PMC fails to explain why it permitted 47 nullah diversions","s":"Senior Congress corporator Arvind Shinde’s questions on nullah diversions drew no reasons or case-wise details from PMC officials, who confirmed 47 diversions had been permitted.","k":"Nullah diversions","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-24T12:23:56+05:30","g":["PMC","Nullah diversions","Arvind Shinde","Aniruddha Pawaskar","UDCPR"],"b":"At the civic general body meeting on Friday, senior Congress corporator Arvind Shinde sought details of nullah diversions, but PMC, which has permitted 47 of them, could not explain why the natural drainage channels were allowed to be diverted.\nShinde wanted to know how many nullahs were diverted over the past four to five years, the reasons behind each approval, and how many permissions were linked to construction and development proposals. The civic administration initially failed to provide even the basic figures.\nOfficials later confirmed that 47 diversions had been permitted, but could not furnish the reasons or case-wise details justifying the clearances.\nPMC City Engineer Aniruddha Pawaskar said, “Nullah diversions are permitted as per the norms and provisions of the UDCPR. The rules allow such diversions while maintaining the same inlet and outlet levels and ensuring that the alignment is not altered in a manner that affects the natural flow of water.”\nPawaskar added that such provisions had existed in development control regulations since 1987. The explanation did not address Shinde’s demand for details of individual permissions.\nShinde also questioned the changes the PMC proposed to the UDCPR between 2022 and 2026. Pawaskar assured the general body that the information would be submitted by Monday.\nFor the provision allowing plots on 6-metre-wide roads to avail FSI and TDR benefits based on a nearby 9-metre-wide road, officials could give only a preliminary estimate of around 100 such cases across Pune, without verified figures.","i":"illustration-e7364c74e8","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-baner-auto-driver-allegedly-intimidated-plying-statewide-strike.html","h":"Baner auto driver allegedly intimidated by fellow drivers for plying during statewide strike","s":"Auto unions across Maharashtra announced a statewide auto-rickshaw strike against bike-taxi and aggregator services such as Rapido.","k":"Statewide auto strike","c":"City","t":"2026-11-24T11:59:00+05:30","g":["Baner","Auto strike","Auto-rickshaw","Rapido"],"b":"Fellow drivers allegedly intimidated an auto-rickshaw driver in Pune’s Baner area for plying his vehicle during the statewide auto-rickshaw bandh called on Monday.\nThe unions announced the strike in protest, claiming bike-taxi and aggregator services such as Rapido are adversely impacting the livelihood of traditional auto drivers.\nThe Baner incident has highlighted growing friction among drivers on the ground during the agitation.","i":"","a":["Baner"]},{"u":"pune/pune-law-college-road-wadeshwar-cafe-pmc-anti-encroachment-action.html","h":"Law College Road: Wadeshwar Cafe faces PMC anti-encroachment action","s":"Wadeshwar Cafe is under a demolition drive of the Pune Municipal Corporation, as Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram's administration steps up action against alleged unauthorised encroachments.","k":"Law College Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-24T11:08:27+05:30","g":["Pune","Wadeshwar Cafe","Law College Road","PMC","Anti-encroachment drive"],"b":"Wadeshwar Cafe on Law College Road faces anti-encroachment action by the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC), which has brought it under its demolition drive.\nThis comes as Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram's administration intensifies action against alleged unauthorised encroachments across the city.\nPune's anti-encroachment drive continues to gather momentum.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/police-raid-four-kharadi-hotels-illegal-liquor-consumption.html","h":"Police raid four Kharadi hotels over illegal liquor consumption; 58 customers found","s":"Alcohol bottles were seized, and 58 customers were found consuming liquor, in an operation by Pune Police's Anti-Narcotics Cell at four Kharadi hotels.","k":"Kharadi hotels","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T17:59:31+05:30","g":["Kharadi","Pune Police","Liquor licence","Hotels"],"b":"Four Kharadi hotels, Rajmudra, Nivant, Farmaish and Tandoor Tukka, were raided by Pune Police's Anti-Narcotics Cell, which found 58 customers consuming liquor.\nThe raid was over the hotels allegedly allowing customers to consume liquor without the required licence. The customers were 20 at Rajmudra, nine at Nivant and 29 at Farmaish and Tandoor Tukka. Alcohol bottles were seized during the operation.\nCases have been registered against the hotel owners and waiters at Kharadi Police Station for allegedly allowing liquor consumption without the necessary permission.","i":"illustration-959a1b9869","a":["Kharadi"]},{"u":"pune/katraj-water-supply-disrupted-after-metro-work-damages-pipeline.html","h":"Katraj water supply disrupted after Metro work damages underground pipeline","s":"Residents of Pune's Katraj area blame negligence by the agencies concerned and have demanded immediate repair of a damaged underground pipeline.","k":"Katraj","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-23T17:31:56+05:30","g":["Katraj","Metro construction","Water supply","Pune"],"b":"An underground water pipeline damaged during ongoing Metro construction work in Katraj has disrupted water supply in the area and caused severe inconvenience to local residents.\nThe residents alleged that adequate precautions are not being taken while Metro projects are carried out.\nBlaming negligence by the agencies concerned, residents have demanded immediate repair of the damaged pipeline to restore normal supply. They have also demanded stricter safety and monitoring measures during the ongoing construction.","i":"","a":["Katraj"]},{"u":"pune/pune-man-killed-pmpml-bus-karve-nagar-accident-or-suicide.html","h":"Man killed by PMPML bus at Karve Nagar: accident or suicide?","s":"Questions about whether a man deliberately jumped have been raised by footage of him coming in front of a moving PMPML bus beneath the Karve Nagar flyover.","k":"Karve Nagar","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-23T17:09:31+05:30","g":["Pune","PMPML","Karve Nagar"],"b":"On 22 November, a man died after coming in front of a moving PMPML bus beneath the Karve Nagar flyover in Pune.\nFootage of the incident has raised questions about whether he deliberately jumped in front of the bus.","i":"illustration-dbf351b3d0","a":["Karvenagar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-swargate-bus-depot-rape-trial-begins-after-21-months.html","h":"Swargate bus depot rape trial begins after 21 months; survivor breaks down in witness box","s":"The survivor in the Swargate bus depot rape case broke down in tears in the witness box on the first day of the trial, and the court adjourned the hearing to December 5.","k":"Swargate bus depot case","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-23T16:48:33+05:30","g":["Swargate","Swargate bus depot case","Rape trial","Pune"],"b":"The Swargate bus depot rape trial began its witness examination on Saturday before Special Judge D. S. Deshmukh, nearly 21 months after the case shook Pune on February 25, 2025.\nThe survivor became emotionally overwhelmed while recounting the sequence of events in the witness box and broke down in tears, and the first day of proceedings ended abruptly. Considering her distressed state, the court adjourned the hearing to December 5.\nPune Police filed an 892-page chargesheet within 52 days against the accused, a 37-year-old from Gunat village in Shirur. It is backed by CCTV footage, technical evidence, identification parade records and statements from 82 witnesses.\nSpecial Public Prosecutor Ajay Misar, who is leading the prosecution, is set to examine 87 witnesses.","i":"illustration-6ad719b1ef","a":["Swargate"]},{"u":"pune/bomb-threat-email-pune-district-court-names-diljit-dosanjh-mumbai-concert.html","h":"Bomb threat email to Pune District Court names Diljit Dosanjh’s Mumbai concert on 27 November","s":"A threatening email to Pune’s District Court warned of a bomb blast at the Pune Court Complex and mentioned Amitabh Bachchan and Diljit Dosanjh as potential targets.","k":"Pune District Court","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T16:27:45+05:30","g":["Diljit Dosanjh","Bomb threat","Pune District Court","Mumbai concert"],"b":"Pune’s District Court received a threatening email on 23 November that mentioned the name of Punjabi singer Diljit Dosanjh and warned of a bomb blast. His upcoming Mumbai concert has come under a security alert.\nThe email arrived at around 1:46 pm and warned of a bomb blast at the Pune Court Complex at 2:29 pm.\nIt specifically referred to Dosanjh’s 27 November concert at Mumbai’s Mahalaxmi Racecourse and mentioned both Amitabh Bachchan and Diljit Dosanjh as potential targets.\nIt carried the phrase “Bomb Dhamake - Bachan-Diljit” and referred to 27 November and 31 December. It included threatening lines about an attack, references to Khalistan slogans and an alleged bomb threat involving an iPhone at Mahalaxmi Stadium. It also contained Punjabi phrases referring to Bachchan’s event and violence.\nThe exact meaning and credibility of the threats are yet to be established, and the matter requires investigation by the authorities.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-wipro-engineer-found-dead-hinjawadi-pg-infosys-boyfriend-arrested.html","h":"Wipro engineer found dead at Hinjawadi PG; Infosys boyfriend arrested","s":"The exact cause of death of a 27-year-old Wipro software engineer found dead at a Hinjawadi PG accommodation has not yet been established, and Senior Police Inspector Balaji Pandhare of Hinjawadi Police Station is investigating.","k":"Hinjawadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T16:05:30+05:30","g":["Hinjawadi","Wipro","Infosys","Hinjawadi Police"],"b":"A 27-year-old Wipro software engineer was found dead at a PG accommodation in Hinjawadi, Pune, and her boyfriend, a software engineer working with Infosys, has been arrested in connection with the case.\nAccording to preliminary police investigations, an argument is said to have broken out between the couple, after which the woman allegedly assaulted her boyfriend. Police say she was then assaulted with bare hands.\nThe exact cause of her death has not yet been established. Senior Police Inspector Balaji Pandhare of Hinjawadi Police Station is conducting further investigations, and police are working to establish the precise circumstances of the death.","i":"illustration-d546101af0","a":["Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3"]},{"u":"pune/pune-district-court-bomb-threat-emails-security-alert-advised-to-vacate.html","h":"Bomb threat emails: security alert at Pune District Court; lawyers, staff, visitors advised to vacate","s":"The authenticity of the bomb threat at the Pune District and Sessions Court has not been established, and the Pune Bar Association has advised lawyers, court staff and visitors to leave the premises.","k":"Pune District Court","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-23T15:43:43+05:30","g":["Pune","Pune District Court","Bomb threat","Pune Bar Association"],"b":"After emails threatening a bomb attack on the premises of the Pune District and Sessions Court were said to have been received, a security alert was issued there on Monday.\nIn an urgent advisory, the Pune Bar Association advised lawyers, court staff and visitors to vacate the premises immediately and move to a safe location.\nThe association's notice said the matter was communicated by email to the Principal District and Sessions Judge, Pune. The association's president and executive committee urged advocates and everyone in the court complex to take the warning seriously and leave without delay. They also urged them to follow the directions of the authorities and cooperate with the administration and security agencies.\nIt is not yet known who sent the emails or why. The authenticity of the threat has not been established.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/wakad-corporator-sneha-kalate-assures-park-street-residents-wall-rebuilt.html","h":"Wakad: Corporator Sneha Kalate assures Park Street residents their demolished wall will be rebuilt","s":"After speaking with Additional Municipal Commissioner Kuldeep Jangam, Corporator Sneha Ranjit Kalate assured Park Street residents who protested against Pride Purple Group of a meeting at the PCMC headquarters on Monday, 23 November.","k":"Wakad","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-23T15:21:58+05:30","g":["Wakad","Park Street","Pride Purple Group","PCMC"],"b":"Park Street residents in Wakad, who protested over the demolition of their compound wall, were assured by Corporator Sneha Ranjit Kalate, after she spoke with PCMC Additional Municipal Commissioner Kuldeep Jangam, that it would be rebuilt.\nThe residents had protested against Pride Purple Group over the demolition and over the alleged illegal operation of an RMC (ready-mix concrete) plant near the residential area. Corporator Kalate intervened in the matter and spoke to the residents at the protest on 22 November.\nCorporator Kalate also assured the residents that a meeting would be held at the PCMC headquarters on Monday, 23 November, to discuss the issue.\nThe residents now expect concrete action against the alleged illegal RMC plant, and a resolution to their concerns.","i":"","a":["Wakad","Vakad"]},{"u":"pune/pune-aundh-developer-padmavati-associates-ngt-penalty.html","h":"Aundh developer Padmavati Associates hit with ₹12.45 crore NGT penalty","s":"Padmavati Associates must deposit ₹12.45 crore, equal to 10% of the estimated cost of its three projects, with the Maharashtra Pollution Control Board within two months.","k":"Aundh developer","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-23T14:58:42+05:30","g":["NGT","Aundh","Padmavati Associates","Environmental compensation"],"b":"The Western Zone Bench of the National Green Tribunal (NGT) has ordered Aundh-based developer Padmavati Associates to pay ₹12.45 crore as environmental compensation for three projects it built without clearances.\nThe compensation is ₹12,45,77,156.40 in full. It is for constructing its Pristine Prism, Pristine Royale and Pristine Privilege projects without mandatory environmental clearance, consent to establish or consent to operate.\nThe penalty is equivalent to 10% of the projects’ estimated cost. It must be deposited with the Maharashtra Pollution Control Board (MPCB) within two months.\nThe tribunal, hearing a complaint filed by an activist lawyer, also strongly pulled up the State Level Environment Impact Assessment Authority (SEIAA) for failing to initiate action despite knowing about the violations.","i":"illustration-b8c32834fe","a":["Aundh","Aundh Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/vendors-stalls-returned-salunkhe-vihar-road-hours-after-major-pmc-drive.html","h":"Vendors and stalls returned to Salunkhe Vihar Road hours after major PMC drive","s":"Handcarts, vegetable and fruit stalls and parked two-wheelers again narrowed the carriageway of busy Salunkhe Vihar Road, and local residents are questioning follow-up enforcement.","k":"Salunkhe Vihar Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-23T14:48:00+05:30","g":["Salunkhe Vihar Road","PMC","Anti-encroachment drive"],"b":"Hours after the Pune Municipal Corporation carried out a major anti-encroachment drive on Salunkhe Vihar Road on Sunday, roadside vendors and stalls had returned to occupy the cleared stretches by evening.\nHandcarts, vegetable and fruit stalls and parked two-wheelers lined the roadside of the busy corridor once again, narrowing the carriageway.\nLocal residents are raising fresh questions about follow-up enforcement and how long PMC's clearance operations last.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/baramati-extortion-firing-two-minors-detained-search-on-for-alleged-mastermind.html","h":"Baramati extortion firing: two minors detained, search on for alleged mastermind","s":"Two minors were detained within eight hours over the firing at a Baramati construction businessman’s SUV, and police have identified the alleged mastermind.","k":"Baramati","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T14:36:58+05:30","g":["Baramati","Extortion","Baramati police","Pune rural"],"b":"Two minors have been detained over the firing at a Baramati construction businessman’s SUV that took place around 6 pm on November 21 in Shivshambhu Nagar, Baramati MIDC.\nPolice say the businessman had received an extortion demand of ₹2 lakh through Instagram that afternoon. After he refused to pay, three suspects allegedly arrived on a motorcycle. One opened the bungalow’s gate while the others fired two rounds at the SUV. No one was injured.\nBaramati police and the Pune rural local crime branch formed five teams and detained the two minors within eight hours. Police say the minors admitted to their involvement during questioning. Two pistols allegedly used in the crime were seized.\nPolice have identified the alleged mastermind, who knows the businessman well, and a search for him is on. Police said the exact reason behind the firing and extortion will be known after his arrest.\n“As of now, we have detained two minors who were actually involved in firing and seized weapons, and a search for the prime accused is going on,” Police Inspector Narayan Pawar said.\nBaramati MP Supriya Sule, in a post on X, said, “The law and order situation in Baramati and its surrounding areas has become extremely serious, with criminal activities on the rise,” and asked, “What exactly are the Baramati police doing? Have criminals stopped fearing the law?”\nThe case has been registered at Baramati Taluka police station under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the Arms Act.","i":"illustration-058c26255b","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-find-19-thai-women-allegedly-overstaying-visas-deportation-underway.html","h":"Pune Police find 19 Thai women allegedly overstaying visas; deportation underway","s":"Legal proceedings have been initiated and the process to deport 19 Thai women allegedly staying in Pune after their visas expired is underway.","k":"Pune Police Special Branch","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T14:16:08+05:30","g":["Pune Police","Special Branch","Koregaon Park","Thai women","Deportation"],"b":"Special teams of the Pune Police Special Branch carried out a verification drive in Koregaon Park, Manjari and Mundhwa on November 20 and found 19 Thai women allegedly staying in Pune despite their visas having expired.\nThe Special Branch has taken action against the women. Police said the women had violated visa conditions and regulations. Legal proceedings have been initiated against them under the relevant laws, and the process to deport them from India is underway.\nPolice had received information that several foreign nationals were continuing to stay in the country after their visas expired. Pune Police Commissioner Amitesh Kumar directed the Special Branch to identify such foreign nationals and take legal action.\nThe teams worked under Deputy Commissioner of Police Dr Prashant Amrutkar and Assistant Commissioner Chandrakant Bhosale.","i":"illustration-87e2e6c1bc","a":["Koregaon Park","KP","Koregaon Park Annexe"]},{"u":"pune/pune-major-kondhwa-building-fire-guts-18-vehicles.html","h":"Major Kondhwa building fire: 18 vehicles gutted, 35 residents moved to terrace","s":"Fire brigade personnel moved about 35 residents of a residential building in Kondhwa to its terrace during a fire in its parking area; the blaze was brought under control within 20 minutes.","k":"Kondhwa fire","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-23T14:05:27+05:30","g":["Kondhwa","Bhagyoday Nagar","Fire brigade"],"b":"A major fire in the ground-floor parking area of a four-storey residential building at Lane No. 34, Bhagyoday Nagar, Kondhwa, gutted 18 vehicles. It broke out at around 3:19 am on Sunday, 22 November.\nFire brigade officials gave the details of the damage: sixteen two-wheelers, one three-wheeler and one four-wheeler were completely gutted, and the building's lift and electrical wiring were badly damaged.\nThree fire tenders from the Kondhwa Fire Station were sent to the spot. The fire had spread across the parking area and filled it with thick smoke, so fire brigade personnel moved about 35 residents to the building's terrace. Firefighters wearing breathing apparatus went in to put out the flames.\nThe blaze was brought under control within 20 minutes and did not spread to the neighbouring building. There were no injuries or casualties. The exact cause of the fire is yet to be ascertained.","i":"","a":["Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-auto-rickshaw-drivers-strike-bike-taxi-policy-traffic-hit-mukai-chowk.html","h":"Pune auto-rickshaw drivers strike over bike taxi policy; traffic hit at Mukai Chowk","s":"Auto-rickshaw drivers in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad want the Maharashtra Government to withdraw its bike taxi policy completely, fearing that bike taxi services will hurt their livelihood and employment.","k":"Mukai Chowk","c":"City","t":"2026-11-23T13:54:23+05:30","g":["Mukai Chowk","Bike taxi policy","Rickshaw strike","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"Auto-rickshaw drivers in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad have called a strike on Monday, 23 November, and from 10 am protesting drivers gathered at Mukai Chowk in Pimpri-Chinchwad, disrupting traffic in the area.\nThe protesting drivers stopped bike taxis as well as Ola and Uber auto-rickshaws.\nThe protesters are demanding that the Maharashtra Government withdraw its bike taxi policy completely.\nThe drivers fear that bike taxi services will hurt their livelihood and employment.","i":"illustration-d02009602c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-trio-fires-baramati-builder-car-2-lakh-instagram-extortion-demand.html","h":"Trio fires at Baramati builder’s car over ₹2 lakh Instagram extortion demand","s":"Police are investigating the link between an Instagram extortion call and a firing at a Baramati builder’s car in which no one was injured.","k":"Baramati","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T13:43:47+05:30","g":["Baramati","Extortion","Firing"],"b":"Around 6 pm, unidentified assailants reached near a builder’s residence, opened the gate and fired two rounds at his car in Baramati over a ₹2 lakh extortion demand made on Instagram, then fled. No one was injured.\nAccording to preliminary information, the builder, based in Baramati MIDC, received a call on Instagram on Saturday afternoon in which unidentified callers demanded ₹2 lakh.\nCCTV footage from the locality captured three unidentified suspects fleeing after the firing.\nBaramati Taluka Police and a forensic team reached the scene to collect evidence. Police are investigating the link between the Instagram extortion call and the attack.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-metro-line-2-snag-near-yerawada-commuters-walk-elevated-track.html","h":"Pune Metro Line 2 snag near Yerawada: commuters walk along elevated track","s":"Regular two-way operations resumed on Pune Metro Line 2 at 1:35 pm, and Metro officials said an inquiry into a technical fault is underway.","k":"Pune Metro","c":"City","t":"2026-11-23T13:32:36+05:30","g":["Pune Metro","Metro Line 2","Yerawada","Ramwadi"],"b":"Pune Metro Line 2 services were disrupted for nearly two hours on Sunday after a Vanaz-bound rake from Ramwadi suffered a power supply-related technical snag near Yerawada station at 11:38 am.\nIn the video, commuters on the elevated corridor walk along the narrow concrete trackside pathway between two stationary metro rakes, and climb in and out through the driver cabin’s side door.\nFrom 11:55 am, single-line services ran between RTO and Ramwadi while staff cleared the affected train from the main track. The faulty rake was parked near Ramwadi station at 1:30 pm. Regular two-way (Up and Down) operations resumed at 1:35 pm.\nMetro officials said an inquiry into the technical fault is underway and expressed regret for the inconvenience caused to passengers.","i":"","a":["Yerawada","Yerwada","Yeravda","Yerawda","Yerwda"]},{"u":"pune/marunji-cement-block-truck-overturns-man-walking-close-narrow-escape.html","h":"Cement block truck overturns near Life Republic in Marunji; man walking close by has narrow escape","s":"CCTV caught a cement block truck overturning near Life Republic in Marunji, and a man walking close by escaped; there were no casualties.","k":"Marunji","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-23T13:20:36+05:30","g":["Marunji","Life Republic","Drainage","Truck"],"b":"A truck loaded with cement blocks overturned near Life Republic in Marunji, and a man walking close to it had a narrow escape as it toppled.\nThe truck overturned after a drainage chamber is said to have collapsed. The incident was caught on CCTV, and there were no casualties.\nThe incident has raised questions about the quality of drainage infrastructure and public safety in the area.","i":"","a":["Marunji"]},{"u":"pune/wagholi-three-killed-two-injured-car-truck-collided-katkewadi.html","h":"Wagholi: three killed, two injured as car and truck collided near Katkewadi on Pune–Ahilyanagar Highway","s":"The two injured in the collision between a Volkswagen Polo and a truck on the Pune–Ahilyanagar Highway in Wagholi are undergoing treatment at I-Max Hospital.","k":"Wagholi","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-23T13:09:02+05:30","g":["Wagholi","Katkewadi","Pune–Ahilyanagar Highway","I-Max Hospital"],"b":"At around 1–1:30 am a Volkswagen Polo collided with a truck near Katkewadi in Wagholi on the Pune–Ahilyanagar Highway, killing three and injuring two.\nThree of the car's occupants died on the spot. Two others were injured. The injured were rushed to I-Max Hospital in Wagholi, where they are undergoing treatment.","i":"","a":["Wagholi"]},{"u":"pune/fake-bank-caller-allegedly-takes-over-kothrud-woman-phone-10-lakh-gone.html","h":"Fake bank caller allegedly takes over Kothrud woman’s phone, ₹10 lakh gone","s":"FIR 0459/2026 is against unidentified phone number holders and bank account holders, and Police Inspector Anil Shivaji Mane is investigating.","k":"Kothrud","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-23T11:41:04+05:30","g":["Kothrud","Bank of Maharashtra","Pune City Police","ICICI Bank"],"b":"A 78-year-old doctor living in Kothrud has complained that unidentified callers cheated him and his wife between 20 and 21 November 2026; ₹10 lakh was debited, an FIR says.\nThe complainant, Rajendra Shantaram Deo, lives in Mayur Colony, Kothrud. His wife is Vrinda Rajendra Deo, 70, and the couple live with their daughter, Pradnya Deo, 45.\nFake callers posing as Bank of Maharashtra staff allegedly took over his wife’s phone. On 20 November, around 11.30 am, a caller claiming to be a Bank of Maharashtra representative offered her a pension card and had her install an APK file sent on WhatsApp. On 21 November, around 11 am, she got a WhatsApp video call and was asked to share her screen.\nWithout any OTP being given, ₹10,00,000 was debited online from four accounts at ICICI Bank and Bank of Maharashtra, including the couple’s joint account.\nPune City Police registered the case at Kothrud police station on 22 November 2026 (FIR 0459/2026), against the unidentified phone number holders and bank account holders. It is under section 66(D) of the Information Technology Act and sections 318(4), 319(2) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. Police Inspector Anil Shivaji Mane is investigating, and Inspector Arun Dattu Ghodke registered the case.","i":"illustration-c768d48a08","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/pune-cantonment-old-grant-land-union-not-occupancy-holders-bombay-hc.html","h":"Pune Cantonment old-grant land belongs to the Union, not occupancy holders: Bombay HC","s":"A possession decree against the Union of India in a case over 0.85 acre and a bungalow at Survey No. 742, Pune Cantonment, was set aside; the Bombay HC judgment itself orders no resumption or eviction.","k":"Pune Cantonment","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-21T11:17:11+05:30","g":["Pune Cantonment","Bombay HC","Old-grant land","Survey No. 742"],"b":"On 18 November 2026, Justice Gauri Godse of the Bombay HC held that the land at Survey No. 742, Pune Cantonment “was not privately owned and it was given on an old grant basis” (para 60). The court based this on the General Land Register (Class B-3) and the old-grant record.\nJustice Godse partly allowed two second appeals filed in 1987 by the Union of India and the Military Estate Officer, Pune. The case, Union of India v. T. S. Anklesaria (a private trust), is over 0.85 acre and a bungalow at Survey No. 742, Pune Cantonment.\nThe trust claimed absolute ownership of the 0.85 acre and bungalow under a 1918 sale deed. Justice Godse found that the deed shows no source of title and that the Class B-3 entry was never challenged. The register entries, she held, raise “a strong presumption” for the Union (paras 53, 57–58, 79).\nThe judgment, quoting the Supreme Court’s 1999 Vakil ruling, traces an ‘old grant’ to colonial orders such as the Bengal Regulations of 1836. Houses could be built on cantonment ground, but “the ground continued to be the property of the State, was resumable at the pleasure of the Government”.\nResumption came on one month’s notice, with payment for authorised structures. Here, the General Land Register classes the land as Class B-3 and enters the trust as holder of occupancy rights, under a Government order of 6 January 1827 (para 54). That order, the court noted, confers no right of property in the ground.\nFollowing the Supreme Court’s 2014 ruling in Dinshaw Shapoorji Anklesari, on similar facts, she held that the Union cannot be held a tenant and the trust has only a right in the structure (para 71). So there was no tenancy to end by a Transfer of Property Act notice (para 72). Separately, the trust’s 1980 notice was invalid because the suit was filed before the lease’s six-month notice period ran out (para 75).\nThe Rent Act does not apply (para 51). The trust prayed for no declaration of title, so it is not entitled to possession as prayed in this suit (para 79).\nThe decree for possession against the Union was set aside. The decree on arrears of rent, with set-off from the compensation paid with the resumption notice of 29 January 1972, stands (paras 81–82). Any right the trust has under the lease to seek possession of the bungalow is kept open (para 80). No costs.\nAs a High Court ruling, it binds the courts below it across Maharashtra and Goa.\nFor holders of Pune Cantonment’s old-grant bungalows, the ruling restates the courts’ view that the ground remains the Government’s and the holder’s right lies in the structure. The ruling lands on a long-running Pune dispute.\nA February 2024 release by Rajendra Jagtap, Defence Estates Officer, Pune Circle, counts 202 old-grant bungalows or sites in Pune Cantonment. It says the land always belongs to the Government; a sale needs Government of India approval, and compensation on resumption is the construction cost alone.\nIn January 2024 the Defence Estates Office sealed four old-grant bungalows. It sealed one on Cross Road, the Director of Defence Estates said, on finding its sale unauthorised. In October 2025, Army authorities began the process to resume 12 bungalows.\nThe judgment itself orders no resumption or eviction. Whether the ruling will be appealed is not known.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmc-chief-will-name-and-shame-anyone-interfering-in-encroachment-drive.html","h":"PMC chief: names of those interfering in encroachment drive will be made public","s":"The Pune Municipal Corporation removed 75,540 sq ft of unauthorised structures in Thursday's drive and will carry out daily drives for the next two months.","k":"Encroachment drive","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T17:08:22+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Encroachment drive","Naval Kishore Ram"],"b":"The names of those interfering in the Pune Municipal Corporation's drive against encroachment will be made public, and no political or external interference will be tolerated, Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram has warned.\nIn Thursday's drive, the PMC removed 75,540 sq ft of unauthorised structures. The action covered 103 establishments across five ward jurisdictions.\nFor the next two months, the PMC will conduct anti-encroachment drives every day across the city, public holidays and festivals included.\nAccording to the commissioner, nearly 2.5 lakh shops in Pune have encroached upon front-margin spaces. He has urged citizens and commercial establishments to voluntarily remove unauthorised structures and encroachments from those spaces or face action.\nTo strengthen enforcement, the civic body has also proposed deploying 100 Maharashtra Security Force personnel.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-court-stays-pcmc-proposed-demolition-punawale-procedural-lapses.html","h":"Punawale: Court stays proposed PCMC demolition of 330-sq-metre structure over procedural lapses","s":"A court has ruled that a 24-hour notice alone is insufficient without mandatory safeguards, and has set aside a lower court’s refusal of interim relief to two people.","k":"Punawale","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-20T16:57:28+05:30","g":["Punawale","PCMC","Demolition","Ad-hoc District Court"],"b":"Over procedural lapses, the Ad-hoc District Court has stayed a proposed demolition by the Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) of a 330-sq-metre structure in Punawale.\nThe court ruled that a 24-hour notice alone is insufficient without following mandatory safeguards. It observed that PCMC had not submitted evidence of a spot panchnama or dated photographs documenting the alleged unauthorised construction.\nThe court also set aside the lower court’s refusal to grant interim relief to the two people who had sought it.\nUntil the civil suit is disposed of, the corporation has been restrained from acting on its February 11, 2026 notice, unless due process is followed. The court clarified that PCMC can initiate fresh proceedings in accordance with the law.","i":"illustration-02617d4c10","a":["Punawale","Punavale"]},{"u":"pune/rohit-pawar-alleges-vsr-got-over-90-percent-of-state-plane-bookings.html","h":"Rohit Pawar alleges VSR operated over 90% of aircraft booked by Maharashtra Government","s":"NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar alleged a tender initiated by Ajit Pawar was cancelled to favour VSR, and claimed the preference for the company came from influential people within the government, not from Ajit Pawar.","k":"Rohit Pawar","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-20T16:46:45+05:30","g":["Rohit Pawar","VSR","Ajit Pawar","Maharashtra Government"],"b":"NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar alleges that VSR operated over 90% of the aircraft booked by the Maharashtra Government, and that ₹168 crore was paid to the company.\nPawar claimed the preference for VSR came from influential people within the government, not from Ajit Pawar. He further alleged that a tender initiated by Ajit Pawar was cancelled to favour VSR.\nQuestioning the company’s alleged influence, Pawar asked, “Why is there so much affection for VSR? Who are VSR’s well-wishers within the government?”\nHe warned of another presentation if action against those responsible was delayed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/group-clash-cases-bibwewadi-kirkatwadi-kharadi-three-firs-one-arrest.html","h":"Group clash cases in Bibwewadi, Kirkatwadi and Kharadi: three FIRs, one arrest so far","s":"A 48-year-old man, a 19-year-old and a 21-year-old allege that groups attacked or chased them with iron objects in three Pune localities, and the only arrest is in the Kharadi case.","k":"Bibwewadi, Kirkatwadi, Kharadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T16:36:05+05:30","g":["Group clash","Bibwewadi","Kirkatwadi","Kharadi","FIRs"],"b":"Police have registered three FIRs in group clash cases in Bibwewadi, Kirkatwadi and Kharadi, with only one arrest so far.\nIn Ambika Nagar, Bibwewadi, on November 18 around 7:30 pm, six people, four of them named, attacked a 48-year-old man and his nephew with iron objects following an old dispute, the man alleged. No arrests have been made.\nNear a xerox shop in Kirkatwadi on November 16, a group of five or six people chased a 19-year-old with iron objects after an argument over their two-wheelers touching each other, the 19-year-old alleged. No arrests have been reported.\nBehind a hotel in Kharadi on November 18 around 9:15 pm, nine named men took a 21-year-old and his friend to an open ground, attacked them with sticks, iron objects and stones, and then threatened them, the 21-year-old alleged. One of the nine accused has been arrested so far.","i":"illustration-b44071f5f5","a":["Bibwewadi","Bibvewadi","Kirkatwadi","Kharadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-one-extra-s-lakh-cheques-allegedly-diverted.html","h":"Pune: One extra ‘S’, ₹26.81 lakh of customers’ cheques allegedly diverted; businessman booked","s":"Hadapsar police have registered a case under Sections 316(2) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and started an investigation.","k":"Hadapsar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T16:25:19+05:30","g":["Pune","Hadapsar","Cheques","Alleged fraud"],"b":"A 53-year-old businessman has been booked at the Hadapsar police station. One extra ‘S’ in a firm’s name allegedly helped divert ₹26.81 lakh of customers’ cheques in Pune. The alleged fraud relates to transactions between 2024 and March 5, 2026.\nHe allegedly collected customers’ cheques in the name of Olive Door Solutions and deposited them into a current account he opened as ‘Olive Door Solustions’ at AU Small Finance Bank’s Hadapsar-Magarpatta branch. Customers allegedly issued the cheques believing they were paying the original business.\nThe complaint alleges that he repeatedly assured the money would be transferred back into the firm’s account, but failed to do so, causing a loss of ₹26,81,017.\nThe case, FIR No. 621/2026, is registered under Sections 316(2) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. The complaint was registered on November 18, 2026.\nHadapsar police have registered the case and started an investigation into the diverted payments, the opening and operation of the lookalike account, and the disputed cheques.","i":"illustration-1a0ad800c5","a":["Hadapsar"]},{"u":"pune/apte-road-hotels-citizens-ask-why-no-action-after-fc-road-crackdown.html","h":"Apte Road hotels: citizens ask why no action after FC Road crackdown","s":"Citizens allege that parking for the Shreyas Hotel, Ramee Grand, Green Signal, Anna Idli and one more hotel on Apte Road causes traffic congestion, and answers from the hotels and civic authorities are awaited.","k":"FC Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T16:14:36+05:30","g":["FC Road","Apte Road","Encroachment","Pune traffic"],"b":"Some citizens are asking why hotels on nearby Apte Road, including Shreyas Hotel, Ramee Grand, Green Signal, Anna Idli and one more hotel, face no action after the FC Road encroachment crackdown.\nThe citizens allege that parking for all these hotels spills onto Apte Road and causes traffic congestion. They also ask whether hotels are even permitted in a residential zone.\nResponses from the hotels and the civic authorities are awaited.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/bombay-high-court-bars-sinhgad-trustees-from-institutions-records.html","h":"‘Nothing short of scam’: Bombay High Court bars Sinhgad trustees from institutions’ records","s":"The Bombay High Court has directed that all documents of the Sinhgad Technical Education Society’s institutions be kept in the sealed custody of government-appointed administrators, who will take charge of managing the 32 institutions to which they have been appointed.","k":"Bombay High Court","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-20T16:03:29+05:30","g":["Bombay High Court","Sinhgad Technical Education Society","STES","Pune"],"b":"A Bombay High Court division bench of Justice GS Kulkarni and Justice Neela Gokhale on Thursday barred trustees of the Sinhgad Technical Education Society (STES) from accessing or interfering with official records of its educational institutions.\nThe court directed that all documents be kept in the sealed custody of government-appointed administrators. The records will be made available to investigating agencies whenever required.\nThe bench gave the directions while hearing over 229 proceedings concerning alleged irregularities involving STES and its managing trustees. The court described the matter as “nothing short of a scam” and clarified that the CBI, the Enforcement Directorate and police are free to take action against the trustees in accordance with law.\nThe administrators, appointed to 25 technical and seven higher education institutions run by the society, will now take charge of managing the 32 institutions.\nA trustee present in court was directed to file an affidavit by 11 am on 20 November, with no further extension, disclosing every bank account held by the society and its balance. The court was informed that two trustees were currently abroad, and sought their nationalities and passport details.\nThe bench directed administrators to ensure students’ education is not disrupted. Students may be shifted to other institutions, and institutions that cannot be operated may be closed, subject to the law and pending proceedings.\nConcerned that academic activities at STES’s medical college may have remained disrupted for four to five weeks, the court made the National Medical Commission and the University of Health Sciences parties to the proceedings.\nThe matter is posted for further hearing at 11 am on 20 November.","i":"illustration-6db5dddb62","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-laxmi-road-massive-encroachment-drive-halted-traders-fatechand-ranka.html","h":"Massive Laxmi Road encroachment drive halted after Fatechand Ranka, traders intervene","s":"Nearly all establishments on the commercial stretch pulled down their shutters, and shopfront projections, metal sheds and extended signboards were torn down along Pune's Laxmi Road.","k":"Laxmi Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T15:52:40+05:30","g":["Laxmi Road","Anti-encroachment","Fatechand Ranka","Pune"],"b":"A massive anti-encroachment drive on Pune's Laxmi Road was halted after the Laxmi Road Traders' Association and veteran trader leader Fatechand Ranka intervened, with civic teams pausing the crackdown.\nNearly all establishments on the commercial stretch pulled down their shutters during the drive, which tore down extended signboards, metal sheds and shopfront projections along the road.\nAlong the closed shops on both sides of the busy market street lay dismantled signage, torn banners and damaged storefront structures.","i":"illustration-d25568998f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/missing-mbbs-student-pune-police-restarted-investigation-no-breakthrough.html","h":"Missing MBBS student: Pune Police restart investigation four months on, no breakthrough yet","s":"Investigators hope for new information within 10–15 days about a missing first-year MBBS student, with police teams sent to Goa, Bengaluru and Marathwada.","k":"Missing student","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T15:41:52+05:30","g":["Pune","Missing student","MBBS student","Pune Police"],"b":"Pune Police have restarted the investigation, four months after a first-year MBBS student from Kolhapur went missing on July 18.\nThe student studies at Byramjee Jeejeebhoy (BJ) Government Medical College. Police traced his mobile phone to the Uruli Kanchan police station jurisdiction and found that he had boarded a Solapur-bound train. The trail went cold because CCTV cameras at Daund railway station were not working.\nThere is no breakthrough yet. Police teams have also been sent to Goa, Bengaluru and Marathwada to gather information, and investigators hope to get new information within the next 10–15 days.\nThe student's father continues to seek information through social media and remains in contact with the police.\nThe case also involves allegations of campus ragging. On July 20, the father submitted a complaint to the college administration naming some students. The family has accused the college administration of delaying action and withholding inquiry findings.\nPune Police and Dr Eknath Pawar, Dean of Sassoon General Hospital, have maintained that preliminary investigations found no evidence of ragging on campus.","i":"illustration-b42e1a634a","a":[]},{"u":"pune/technical-fault-deputy-cm-shinde-helicopter-pandharpur-visit.html","h":"Technical fault in Deputy CM Shinde’s helicopter during Pandharpur visit","s":"A technical fault in Deputy Chief Minister Eknath Shinde’s helicopter during his Pandharpur visit set off talk for some time.","k":"Pandharpur","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-20T15:31:05+05:30","g":["Eknath Shinde","Pandharpur","Helicopter"],"b":"It has emerged that Deputy Chief Minister Eknath Shinde’s helicopter developed a technical fault during his visit to Pandharpur.\nThe incident set off talk for some time.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/maharera-holds-ribera-projects-liable-jhavar-flat-promise.html","h":"MahaRERA holds Ribera Projects liable for Jhavar’s ₹10 crore flat promise","s":"MahaRERA Member Ravindra Deshpande directed Ribera Projects LLP to register sale agreements within 60 days and to pay interest from March 26, 2015, for the delayed possession of two flats promised to a Pune landowning family.","k":"MahaRERA order","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-20T15:17:16+05:30","g":["Ribera Projects","Marvel Ribera","Boat Club Road","Pune"],"b":"MahaRERA has held Ribera Projects LLP liable for two flats that Vishwajeet Jhavar-led Marvel Dwellings Pvt Ltd promised a Pune landowning family in 2012, and rejected the new developer's argument that it was not responsible for the previous developer's commitments.\nThe commitment to the family was made more than 14 years ago. The family transferred a 4,167.20-square-metre plot on Boat Club Road to Marvel Dwellings for ₹65 crore, through a registered deed on September 25, 2012.\nTwo of the landowner's daughters were each entitled to ₹6.50 crore. After ₹1.50 crore each in cash, the remaining ₹5 crore each, ₹10 crore in all, was to be adjusted against flats in Marvel Ribera A Building. One was allotted Flat A-302 with four parking spaces and the other Flat A-402 with 20 parking spaces.\nPossession was promised by March 25, 2015, but the flats were never handed over within the agreed timeline. The project later changed hands after mortgage enforcement proceedings under the SARFAESI Act, and was transferred to Ribera Projects LLP on January 9, 2024.\nMahaRERA Member Ravindra Deshpande directed the developer to register sale agreements for the two flats within 60 days. Deshpande also directed it to pay interest for the delayed possession from March 26, 2015, at the State Bank of India's highest MCLR plus 2%, subject to the COVID-19 moratorium benefit.\nThe developer must also seek a project extension within 30 days. Each of the two complainants was awarded ₹20,000 towards legal costs.","i":"illustration-4e934cd974","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-book-three-allegedly-cheating-investors-1-38-crore.html","h":"Pune Police book three for allegedly cheating investors of ₹1.38 crore","s":"A case has been registered at Wanawadi police station over the alleged cheating of investors of ₹1.38 crore; police said a probe is underway.","k":"Wanawadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T14:54:15+05:30","g":["Pune Police","Wanawadi","Investors","Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar"],"b":"Pune Police have booked three residents of Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar who allegedly operated from an office in Pune and cheated several investors of ₹1.38 crore with promises of high returns.\nThe accused allegedly gained the trust of the complainant and others through three firms, persuading them to invest a total of ₹1.38 crore. The alleged fraud took place between October 2023 and October 2024.\nThe complaint said the accused initially paid returns of ₹32.73 lakh, but stopped paying from October 2024 and allegedly shut down the companies without returning the invested money.\nA case has been registered at Wanawadi police station under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the Maharashtra Protection of Interest of Depositors Act. Police said a probe is underway.","i":"illustration-054c983a4a","a":["Wanowrie","Wanawadi","Wanwadi","Wanowri","Wanavdi"]},{"u":"pune/gokul-milk-costlier-from-saturday-buffalo-cow-price-hike.html","h":"Gokul milk costlier from Saturday: buffalo up ₹6 a litre, cow up ₹4","s":"The selling price of cow milk from Gokul Milk Union goes up ₹4 a litre, and the purchase price of buffalo milk paid to producers by ₹3 a litre.","k":"Gokul milk","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-20T14:41:53+05:30","g":["Gokul Milk","Milk price hike","Gokul Milk Union"],"b":"Gokul milk is costlier from Saturday, 21 November: Gokul Milk Union has raised the selling price of buffalo milk by ₹6 a litre and of cow milk by ₹4.\nThe ₹6 rise is the biggest milk price hike in Gokul's history. The decision was taken at a meeting of the board of directors of Gokul Milk Union.\nThe board revised both purchase and selling prices, keeping in mind the condition of milk-producing farmers and of the union itself. The purchase price of buffalo milk paid to producers goes up by ₹3 a litre, and that of cow milk by ₹2.\nThe union is said to need the large increase in selling prices to make up for the financial blow it has suffered and a deficit of about ₹70 crore.\nGokul may decide on another milk price hike in January, depending on overall milk availability and market conditions.","i":"illustration-2f27a15294","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-absconding-mcoca-accused-arrested-deccan-crime-branch-unit-3.html","h":"Absconding MCOCA accused arrested from Deccan by Pune Crime Branch Unit 3","s":"A 30-year-old accused, a resident of Warje Malwadi who had been absconding since a MCOCA case was registered at Warje police station, has been handed over to the Assistant Commissioner of Police, Kothrud division.","k":"Deccan","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T14:31:00+05:30","g":["MCOCA","Deccan","Pune Crime Branch","Warje"],"b":"On Wednesday, a Pune Crime Branch Unit 3 team on crime-prevention patrol in Narhe police station limits received a tip-off from an informer that an accused absconding in a MCOCA case registered at Warje police station had come to the chowpatty area in Deccan. Pune Crime Branch Unit 3 has arrested him.\nThe 30-year-old accused is a resident of Warje Malwadi. He was caught while sitting behind Beed Anda Rice Hotel near Shelar Mama Chowk in Deccan.\nA team led by Police Inspector Prashant Annachhatre searched the area, surrounded him on all sides and took him into custody without giving him a chance to escape.\nSenior officers had told the Crime Branch to trace him. He had been absconding since the case was registered.\nCase number 177/2026 at Warje police station is registered against him and other accused under sections 118(2), 115(2), 352 and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, section 4(25) of the Arms Act, section 37(1) read with 135 of the Maharashtra Police Act, and sections 3(1)(ii) and 3(4) of the Maharashtra Control of Organised Crime Act (MCOCA).\nHe has been handed over to the Assistant Commissioner of Police, Kothrud division, for further legal action and investigation. The action was taken under the guidance of Additional Commissioner of Police (Crime) Tejaswini Satpute, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Crime) Gauhar Hasan and Assistant Commissioner of Police (Crime-1) Shailesh Sankhe.","i":"illustration-22c3c87ce6","a":["Deccan Gymkhana","Deccan","Warje","Warje Malwadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-rickshaw-unions-plan-indefinite-sit-in-outside-rto-against-bike-taxis.html","h":"Pune rickshaw unions plan indefinite sit-in outside RTO against bike taxis on 23 November","s":"Members of the Pune District Rickshaw Drivers and Owners Action Committee say bike taxis would put more two-wheelers on Pune's already congested roads and threaten rickshaw drivers' livelihoods.","k":"Bike taxis","c":"City","t":"2026-11-20T14:19:59+05:30","g":["Pune","Rickshaw unions","Bike taxis","RTO","Maharashtra"],"b":"On 23 November, rickshaw unions in Pune plan to begin an indefinite sit-in outside the Regional Transport Office (RTO) against bike taxis, organised by the Pune District Rickshaw Drivers and Owners Action Committee.\nThe unions are demanding that the state government withdraw its permission for bike taxis and that Transport Minister Pratap Sarnaik resign.\nOn the same day, the committee also plans demonstrations outside district collector offices across Maharashtra. It said rickshaw unions from Pune district and other parts of Maharashtra would join the protest.\nThe committee's convenor said the unions had protested before but the government had not addressed their concerns. The convenor said the sit-in would continue until the bike taxi decision was withdrawn or the transport minister resigned.\nCommittee members said bike taxis would add more two-wheelers to Pune's already congested roads and threaten rickshaw drivers' livelihoods. They said the policy could put drivers' families under financial strain, including the families of women rickshaw drivers who had received auto-rickshaw permits.","i":"illustration-ab0f091a99","a":[]},{"u":"pune/narhe-three-firs-attack-cases-near-zeal-college-two-arrested.html","h":"Narhe: three FIRs in attack cases near Zeal College, two arrested","s":"Two people have been arrested in one of three attack cases involving students and young men near Zeal College in Narhe; no arrests have been made in another case, and none reported in the third.","k":"Narhe attack cases","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T14:09:03+05:30","g":["Zeal College","Narhe","Narhe Police","Pune"],"b":"Narhe Police Station has registered three separate FIRs, 362/2026, 363/2026 and 364/2026, in three attack cases near Zeal College of Engineering and Research (ZCOER) in Narhe, Pune, on November 19. The three separate incidents involved students and young men.\nIn the first case, a 17-year-old boy alleged that four young men, aged 19 to 25, attacked him near a tea stall on Zeal College Lane around 2:30 PM. Two of them have been arrested.\nIn another case, around 3 PM on Zeal College Road, one of the men accused in the first case alleged that a juvenile and two others stopped his bike, attacked him with an iron object and abused him. No arrests have been made in this case.\nIn the third case, near Zeal College Chowk and Mithai Mall around 2:30 PM, an 18-year-old alleged that four people hit him on the head with a stone and also attacked his friend. No arrests have been reported.","i":"illustration-e6bfb054da","a":["Narhe","Narhe Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-arrest-katraj-man-seize-md-worth-51-98-lakh-kondhwa.html","h":"Pune Police arrest Katraj man, seize MD worth ₹51.98 lakh in Kondhwa","s":"A 42-year-old Katraj man was arrested and 73.97 grams of mephedrone seized in an operation by the Anti-Narcotics Cell (Unit II) of the Pune Crime Branch and Ambegaon police.","k":"Kondhwa","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T13:56:41+05:30","g":["Pune Police","Kondhwa","Katraj","Mephedrone"],"b":"Pune police arrested a 42-year-old Katraj man and seized MD worth ₹51.98 lakh in Kondhwa in a joint operation on November 17.\nThe seizure was 73.97 grams of mephedrone, commonly known as MD. The arrested man is a resident of Vighnaharta Colony in Santosh Nagar, Katraj.\nPolice said a patrol team noticed him behaving suspiciously in the area. He allegedly tried to flee after seeing the police vehicle, and officers stopped and searched him. Police said they recovered 73.97 grams of MD from his possession.\nThe Anti-Narcotics Cell (Unit II) of the Pune Crime Branch and Ambegaon police conducted the operation.","i":"","a":["Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk","Katraj"]},{"u":"pune/aundh-man-allegedly-attacked-by-group-near-pmt-bus-stop.html","h":"Aundh: man allegedly attacked by group near PMT bus stop; seriously injured, no arrests yet","s":"Provisions of the Arms Act are included in FIR 568/2026, registered over an alleged group attack on a man in Aundh.","k":"Aundh","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T13:43:56+05:30","g":["Aundh","Pune","Chaturshringi Police"],"b":"A man was seriously injured in an alleged group attack near the Rajiv Gandhi Bridge PMT bus stop in Aundh, Pune, at around 4:30 pm, and an FIR has been registered at Chaturshringi Police Station.\nThe complaint was filed by the man's 19-year-old friend. According to it, three named people and 10–12 others allegedly targeted him over an old dispute.\nThe accused allegedly used sticks, and one of them allegedly struck him on the head with an iron object.\nThe FIR (568/2026) also includes provisions of the Arms Act. No arrests have been made so far.","i":"illustration-25509c9b1b","a":["Aundh","Aundh Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/pune-activists-dump-dead-dog-pmc-headquarters-carcass-delay.html","h":"Activists dump dead dog at PMC headquarters over carcass delay","s":"Residents who asked the PMC veterinary department to remove the carcass of a dog hit by a two-wheeler at Zambare Chawdi in Kasba Peth were allegedly passed from one contact number to another.","k":"PMC headquarters","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T13:31:11+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Kasba Peth","Patit Pavan Sanghatana"],"b":"A group of youths and Patit Pavan Sanghatana activists brought a dead dog to the PMC headquarters around 2.15pm and dumped it at the entrance on Thursday over the delay in lifting the carcass.\nAround 10am, a two-wheeler hit the dog at Zambare Chawdi in Kasba Peth. Residents contacted the PMC veterinary department to get the carcass removed but were allegedly passed from one contact number to another without a response.\nThe protest was against the civic body’s inaction. The contractor’s staff arrived to collect the carcass only after a delay of around one-and-a-half hours, even after senior officials intervened.\nPMC veterinary officer Dr Sarika Bhosale said a show-cause notice had been issued to the contractor concerned.","i":"illustration-6b7545ca09","a":["Kasba Peth","Kasba"]},{"u":"pune/police-personnel-seen-on-video-hitting-a-person-in-lohegaon.html","h":"Police personnel seen on video hitting a person in Lohegaon, raising concerns over conduct","s":"A video from Lohegaon shows police personnel hitting a person, and a citizen has called for legal action if any wrongdoing is established.","k":"Lohegaon","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T13:20:06+05:30","g":["Lohegaon","Police conduct","Police accountability"],"b":"Police personnel are seen hitting a person in a video recorded in Lohegaon, Pune, which has raised concerns over police conduct and the use of authority.\nThe person who recorded the video claims to have witnessed the incident firsthand and has questioned the police's actions.\nThe citizen has called for an appropriate investigation and legal action if any wrongdoing is established. The incident has also raised questions about accountability and the proper conduct expected from police personnel.","i":"","a":["Lohegaon","Lohgaon"]},{"u":"pune/pune-tree-plantation-inquiry-ordered-into-alleged-irregularities.html","h":"Pune tree plantation: Forest Minister Ganesh Naik orders inquiry into alleged ₹12.5-crore irregularities","s":"Forest Minister Ganesh Naik says he will decide on further action once he has reviewed the detailed report he sought on plantation work across Pune’s 12 hills.","k":"Pune Forest Department","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T13:08:40+05:30","g":["Pune Forest Department","Ganesh Naik","Tree plantation"],"b":"Maharashtra Forest Minister Ganesh Naik has ordered an inquiry into alleged irregularities in a Pune Forest Department tree plantation programme, including claims that ₹12.5 crore, said to be for planting trees at 12 locations in Pune, was spent on saplings that were never planted.\nThe expenditure was said to be for planting 204,000 trees between January and March. The allegations include that bills were submitted retrospectively, saplings were left unplanted and later dried out, and payments totalling ₹12.5 crore were cleared in a single day. It has also been alleged that some locations already had trees but were shown as new plantation sites.\nNaik, speaking to reporters in Navi Mumbai, said officials would establish whether the Social Forestry Department or the territorial Forest Department carried out the work. He said it would be a serious matter if tenders were issued after the trees had already been planted.\nNaik said he had sought a detailed report on plantation work across Pune’s 12 hills, and would decide on further action after reviewing the findings. Officials would be questioned if existing trees had been cut to make way for the project, he added.\nThe inquiry will also examine the suspension of Forest Department superintendent Jalandhar Patil. He is said to have complained about the project and has claimed he was suspended after bringing the matter to light. Naik said the circumstances of Patil’s suspension would be investigated, adding that good officers would be protected and action taken against those found to have acted improperly.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/lonavala-fda-suspends-licences-four-hotels-expired-food-cockroaches.html","h":"Lonavala: FDA suspends licences of four hotels over expired food, cockroaches","s":"Four Lonavala hotels have had their food licences suspended by the Food and Drug Administration, Maharashtra, after inspections found multiple violations of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.","k":"Lonavala","c":"City","t":"2026-11-20T12:38:37+05:30","g":["Lonavala","FDA","Food safety"],"b":"On November 19, the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), Maharashtra, suspended the food licences of four Lonavala hotels with immediate effect, after its Pune Division carried out surprise inspections on November 18, 2026.\nThe suspended licences are those of The Orchid Hotel, Rhythm Lonavala, The Fern Hotel and Basilica Hotel. The FDA detected serious violations of food safety and hygiene regulations, and the action was taken under the ‘Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra’ campaign.\nThe inspections revealed multiple violations of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, and of the hygiene requirements under Schedule IV of the Act. The FDA found expired food products, cockroaches, pest infestations, improper storage of raw and cooked food and unhygienic kitchen conditions.\nAt The Orchid Hotel in Valvan, operated by Constellation Properties, inspectors found three expired milk packets in the kitchen and eight more in cold storage.\nAt The Orchid Hotel, raw and cooked food were stored together. Refrigerators, chopping boards and areas behind cooking ranges were unclean, water had accumulated in the kitchen and dustbins had no lids.\nStaff at The Orchid Hotel were not wearing gloves, aprons or headgear, and no consumer complaint register was kept.","i":"","a":["Lonavala","Lonavla"]},{"u":"pune/pune-kausar-baug-car-crash-witnesses-claim-driver-intoxicated.html","h":"Kausar Baug car crash: witnesses claim driver was intoxicated","s":"A video of a white car crash in Kondhwa, Pune, has gone viral on social media.","k":"Kausar Baug","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-20T12:27:01+05:30","g":["Kondhwa","Kausar Baug","Car crash","Road safety"],"b":"Eyewitnesses claimed the driver of a white car that crashed at around 5:40 am in the Kausar Baug area of Kondhwa, Pune, was intoxicated at the time.\nThe crash was allegedly due to a driving error. A video of the incident has gone viral on social media, raising concerns about road safety and responsible driving.","i":"","a":["Kausar Baug","Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fda-seizes-medicines-central-drug-store-ycm-hospital-pimpri.html","h":"FDA seizes medicines worth ₹1.72 crore from Central Drug Store at YCM Hospital, Pimpri","s":"An inspection conducted under the guidance of FDA Commissioner Tukaram Mundhe found allopathic medicines made by a company in Jejuri lacking the required manufacturing permission.","k":"YCM Hospital, Pimpri","c":"City","t":"2026-11-20T12:14:21+05:30","g":["FDA","YCM Hospital","Pimpri","Tukaram Mundhe"],"b":"Medicines worth ₹1,72,75,126 (₹1.72 crore) have been seized by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) from the Central Drug Store in the Yashwantrao Chavan Memorial (YCM) Hospital premises in Pimpri.\nOfficials found allopathic medicines manufactured by a company in Jejuri without the required manufacturing permission during the inspection. Some of the medicines also carried unverified quality claims.\nThe inspection was carried out under FDA Commissioner Tukaram Mundhe's guidance.","i":"illustration-e697f781f8","a":["Pimpri","Pimpri Camp","Pimpri Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/major-accident-near-wakad-bridge-car-fire-container-truck-overturned.html","h":"Major accident near Wakad Bridge: car catches fire, container truck overturns, no casualties reported","s":"No casualties have been reported in a car fire and a container truck accident near Wakad Bridge in Pune, where the exact cause is not yet clear and further details are awaited.","k":"Wakad Bridge","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-20T12:01:38+05:30","g":["Wakad Bridge","Car fire","Container truck","Accident"],"b":"A container truck overturned and a car caught fire in a major accident near Wakad Bridge in Pune.\nThe truck lay on its side on the road, while the vehicle that caught fire was engulfed in flames.\nThe exact cause of the incident is not yet clear. No casualties have been reported. Further details are awaited.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/man-booked-pimpri-allegedly-cheating-job-seekers-fake-pmc-letters.html","h":"Man booked at Pimpri police station for allegedly cheating job seekers of ₹1.37 crore with fake PMC letters","s":"A case over an alleged ₹1,37,44,000 fraud involving fake PMC appointment letters is registered at Pimpri police station, with the Crime Branch, led by Police Inspector Shinde, investigating.","k":"Pimpri","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T11:48:25+05:30","g":["Pimpri","PMC","Job seekers","Fake appointment letters"],"b":"A 38-year-old man from Ghorpadi, Pune, has been booked for allegedly cheating job seekers of ₹1.37 crore with fake PMC appointment letters in an alleged fraud that took place between April 28 and November 17, 2026.\nHe allegedly claimed influential contacts within the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) and offered unemployed youths municipal jobs in exchange for money. He allegedly used forged appointment letters, prepared on fake municipal letterheads and bearing counterfeit seals, to make his promises appear genuine.\nThe alleged fraud took place near Indrayani Co-operative Bank in Pimpri. Of the total of ₹1,37,44,000, the complainant, a 58-year-old resident of Vaibhavnagar, Pimpri, was allegedly cheated of ₹9,33,600, while other witnesses collectively lost ₹1,28,10,400.\nThe case was registered at Pimpri police station. The Crime Branch, led by Police Inspector Shinde, has taken up the investigation.","i":"illustration-9135fa63ff","a":["Pimpri","Pimpri Camp","Pimpri Gaon"]},{"u":"pune/pune-woman-allegedly-lured-to-dubai-job-offer-rescued.html","h":"Pune woman allegedly lured to Dubai with ₹1.25 lakh job offer rescued","s":"A Pune woman allegedly pushed towards the sex trade in Dubai was allegedly asked to pay ₹5 lakh, and Union Minister of State Murlidhar Mohol has sought a Pune Police probe.","k":"Pune woman","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-20T11:30:20+05:30","g":["Dubai","Murlidhar Mohol","Pune Police","Pune woman"],"b":"A Pune woman who was allegedly lured to Dubai with a ₹1.25 lakh job offer has been rescued with the help of Union Minister of State Murlidhar Mohol, the Ministry of External Affairs and the Indian Consulate.\nThe woman was allegedly pushed towards the sex trade in Dubai. Her passport was allegedly seized, and she was allegedly asked to pay ₹5 lakh.\nMohol has sought a probe by Pune Police into the agents’ network.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-municipal-commissioner-inspects-illegal-construction-action-kothrud.html","h":"Pune Municipal Commissioner inspects illegal construction action in Kothrud","s":"Assistant Commissioner Asmita Tambe and officials from Building Development Department Zone 6 were present for Pune Municipal Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram's inspection of action against unauthorised constructions in Kothrud.","k":"Kothrud","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-20T11:19:23+05:30","g":["Kothrud","Illegal construction","City Pride","Naval Kishore Ram"],"b":"Naval Kishore Ram, the Pune Municipal Commissioner, inspected the ongoing action against unauthorised constructions in the City Pride Kothrud area on Thursday and sought details of it from the officials concerned.\nHe reviewed the joint action against illegal structures in the front and side margins of buildings, as well as unauthorised constructions on private premises.\nPresent were Assistant Commissioner Asmita Tambe, officials from Building Development Department Zone 6 and the encroachment department of the Warje-Karvenagar ward office.\nThe PMC administration said it remains committed to enforcing construction regulations and taking action against violations.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/pcmc-moshi-waste-to-energy-plant-shut-five-months.html","h":"PCMC’s Moshi waste-to-energy plant shut for five months; 1.15 lakh tonnes of dry waste pile up","s":"The contractor of the Moshi waste-to-energy plant faces a penalty of ₹50,000 a day from the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation, yet the plant has not resumed operations.","k":"Moshi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T17:49:16+05:30","g":["Moshi","PCMC","Waste-to-energy plant","Garbage depot"],"b":"Since its chimney collapsed on June 5, 2026, the waste-to-energy plant at the Moshi garbage depot has stayed shut for more than five months, and an estimated 1,15,500 tonnes of dry waste has piled up without being processed.\nCivic officials say that, with space for fresh garbage running short, vehicles bringing daily waste to the depot are finding it increasingly difficult to unload.\nThe plant is operated by Antony Lara Renewable Energy Pvt Ltd. It began working in July 2023 and was designed to burn 700 tonnes of dry waste a day to generate 14 MW of electricity. On July 8, the contractor’s administrative building also collapsed, killing nine employees.\nThe contractor had assured the civic administration that the chimney would be rebuilt by September 30 and the plant would return to full capacity from October 1. That deadline was missed.\nSince October 1, the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation has been imposing a penalty of ₹50,000 a day on the contractor, but the plant has not resumed operations.\nPimpri-Chinchwad generates around 1,579 tonnes of waste every day, of which about 700 tonnes of dry waste was earlier processed at the plant.","i":"illustration-7c82c88f76","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/gondia-pune-airport-employee-killed-13-lakh-plot-lover-wife-four-arrested.html","h":"Gondia: Pune airport employee killed in ₹13 lakh plot; lover’s wife among four arrested","s":"Four people, including a man’s wife, have been arrested over the killing of a 35-year-old Pune airport employee he was in a relationship with, and two other suspects are still being traced.","k":"Gondia","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T17:38:19+05:30","g":["Pune airport","Gondia","Tiroda taluka","killing"],"b":"A 35-year-old Pune airport employee who worked for a private airline company was allegedly attacked in the Bondrani forest area of Gondia district between 5.30 pm and 6 pm on 14 November, and four people, including her lover’s wife, have been arrested over her killing in a ₹13 lakh plot.\nThe Bondrani forest area is under Dawaniwada police station limits in Tiroda taluka. Her body was found near the Wainganga river with multiple injuries.\nPolice allege that the wife of the man she was in a relationship with arranged the murder for ₹13 lakh, hiring contract killers with the help of a neighbour. Investigators suspect a love triangle as the motive.\nGondia Superintendent of Police Gorakh Bhamre gave details of the alleged conspiracy while briefing the media on the investigation.\nSix special police teams examined footage from around 250 to 300 CCTV cameras on routes connecting Tiroda, Khairlanji, Waraseoni and Gondia, across Gondia and Madhya Pradesh’s Balaghat district, over four consecutive days.\nA clear image of one suspected attacker led to the first detention; during questioning he allegedly disclosed another man’s involvement in arranging the killing. The four arrested include the neighbour. Two other suspects are still being traced.","i":"illustration-93ffb1cd6f","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-war-veteran-lt-gen-ashok-joshi-dies-after-accidental-fall.html","h":"Pune: War veteran Lt Gen Ashok Joshi (retd), 90, dies after accidental fall","s":"Former Director General of Military Training (DGMT) Lt Gen Ashok Joshi (retd), a decorated Army veteran who participated in the 1965 and 1971 Indo-Pak wars, has died at the age of 90.","k":"Wanowrie","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-19T17:23:11+05:30","g":["Pune","Wanowrie","Lt Gen Ashok Joshi","Army veteran","Indo-Pak wars"],"b":"War veteran Lt Gen Ashok Joshi (retd), 90, died after an accidental fall in Pune on Wednesday morning. He allegedly fell from the terrace of his residential building in Salunke Vihar, Wanowrie.\nJoshi, a decorated Army veteran and former Director General of Military Training (DGMT), participated in the 1965 and 1971 Indo-Pak wars.","i":"illustration-b4bbec80cb","a":["Wanowrie","Wanawadi","Wanwadi","Wanowri","Wanavdi"]},{"u":"pune/balewadi-forum-warns-pmc-symbolic-hunger-strike-garbage-dumping-site.html","h":"Balewadi forum warns PMC of symbolic hunger strike over garbage dumping site","s":"Two senior citizens will lead a symbolic hunger strike that a Balewadi residents’ forum has warned of if a garbage dumping site is not relocated by 27 November.","k":"Balewadi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T17:12:15+05:30","g":["Balewadi","Baner","PMC","Hunger strike"],"b":"The Baner Balewadi Nagrik Manch (BBNM), a Balewadi residents’ forum, has warned the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) of a symbolic hunger strike on 28 November over the garbage dumping site near the RK Laxman Museum in Balewadi.\nThe warning applies if the site is not relocated by 27 November. Two senior citizens will lead the protest.\nThe forum claims the dry waste segregation centre has turned into a dumping ground. It claims garbage is spilling onto roads and footpaths, causing foul odour and health concerns.\nA forum member said repeated complaints over two years had failed to bring action.","i":"","a":["Balewadi","Baner"]},{"u":"pune/pune-forest-department-tree-plantation-jain-alleges-12-5-crore-irregularities.html","h":"Pune Forest Department tree plantation: Akshay Jain alleges ₹12.5 crore irregularities","s":"Congress leader Akshay Jain's ₹12.5 crore allegations concern 12 locations, including Taljai Hill, Vetal Tekdi and Ramtekdi.","k":"Tree plantation","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T17:00:43+05:30","g":["Tree plantation","Pune Forest Department","Taljai","Vetal Tekdi"],"b":"The Pune Forest Department cleared its tree plantation bills on March 31, according to the allegations of Congress leader Akshay Jain. Work orders, however, indicate that the actual work began in May.\nJain alleges irregularities worth ₹12.5 crore in the work. According to the allegations, the department showed that 2.04 lakh trees were planted across 68 hectares between January and March. There are also claims that several planted saplings have dried up.\nThe controversy involves 12 locations, including Taljai Hill, Vetal Tekdi and Ramtekdi, where old Gliricidia trees were allegedly cut and plantation work was carried out without tenders or rate quotations.\nJain has also raised concerns that Jalandar Patil, an office superintendent who had allegedly objected to the expenditure, was suspended.","i":"","a":["Ramtekdi"]},{"u":"pune/pashan-lake-said-to-be-nearly-80-under-water-hyacinth.html","h":"Pashan Lake in Pune said to be nearly 80% under water hyacinth; PMC yet to start removal","s":"Residents are asking why the Pune Municipal Corporation waits until March to start removing water hyacinth from Pashan Lake.","k":"Pashan Lake","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T16:47:34+05:30","g":["Pashan Lake","Water hyacinth","PMC","Pune Municipal Corporation"],"b":"This November, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has not started removing water hyacinth from Pashan Lake in Pune, nearly 80% of which is said to be covered by the weed.\nResidents point out that the civic body has followed a similar schedule for years, starting the cleaning only in March or April, when the weed is said to cover just 20–30% of the lake.\nBy the time the first or second monsoon showers arrive in June, much of the remaining hyacinth is washed away.\nThe pattern has raised questions about the timing and effectiveness of the PMC's cleaning, particularly as tenders worth crores of rupees are said to be floated for the work. Residents are asking why removal cannot begin earlier, when the weed starts spreading, instead of waiting until March.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-may-face-water-cuts-two-three-days-week-mayor-nagpure.html","h":"Pune may face water cuts two to three days a week, says Mayor Nagpure","s":"No final decision on water cuts has been taken in Pune, where the civic administration has been asked to prepare a contingency plan that includes restricting supply to two or three days a week.","k":"Pune water supply","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T16:36:16+05:30","g":["Pune","Water cuts","Manjusha Nagpure","Water Resources Department"],"b":"Pune's water storage has fallen to 23.34 TMC, and a 20% water cut may become necessary in the coming weeks to ensure adequate supply until the next monsoon, Mayor Manjusha Nagpure of the Pune Municipal Corporation said on Thursday.\nThe corresponding period last year saw 28.34 TMC in storage, a decline of nearly 5 TMC.\nA final decision has not been taken.\n“We have not taken any decision on water cuts yet. However, looking at the available storage, we will have to take a decision,” Nagpure said.\nThe civic administration has been asked to draw up a contingency plan that includes limiting supply to two or three days a week and keeping a tanker water supply plan ready.\nMayor Nagpure said the civic administration is also seeking a higher water quota from the Water Resources Department, as Pune's allocation has remained at 11 TMC since 2000 despite substantial population growth.\nA meeting with the Water Resources Minister has been sought. If the allocation is not increased, the Mayor said, ensuring water supply until August 30, 2027, will become difficult.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pmc-seals-57-hong-kong-lane-stalls-jm-road-area.html","h":"PMC seals 57 Hong Kong Lane stalls, demolishes unauthorised structures in JM Road area","s":"Across all five regional zones on Wednesday, the Pune Municipal Corporation demolished 50,700 sq ft of unauthorised structures, with the largest drive, in the Hadapsar-Mundhwa ward, removing 23,000 sq ft.","k":"Hong Kong Lane","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T16:25:19+05:30","g":["Pune Municipal Corporation","Hong Kong Lane","JM Road","Anti-encroachment drive"],"b":"On Wednesday, November 18, the Pune Municipal Corporation sealed 57 stalls at Hong Kong Lane, which it had provided, for violating the stipulated terms and conditions.\nThe sealing continues the PMC's anti-encroachment drive after action on Fergusson College Road.\nUnder the Shivajinagar-Ghole Road ward office, the civic body also demolished approximately 13,000 square feet of unauthorised structures in the JM Road area, at JM Road Corner, the Junglee Maharaj Temple Khau Galli and Hong Kong Lane. It seized 15 street-vending counters, 29 gas cylinders, one additional stall and one handcart.\nThe PMC's Encroachment and Unauthorised Construction Removal Department carried out the action under the directions of the Municipal Commissioner. Deputy Commissioner Somnath Bankar of the Encroachment Department and Deputy Commissioner Avinash Sakpal of Regional Office 2 supervised it.\nThe civic body demolished a total of 50,700 sq ft of unauthorised structures on Wednesday, across all five PMC regional zones. It used 10 JCB machines, 10 gas cutters, five breakers, 80 Maharashtra Security Force personnel, 13 police officers and personnel, and 250 civic labourers.\nThe largest drive, in the Hadapsar-Mundhwa ward, removed 23,000 sq ft.\nThe PMC administration has warned that similar drives against unauthorised encroachments will continue regularly across the city.","i":"","a":["Hadapsar","Mundhwa","Mundhawa"]},{"u":"pune/bhor-three-arrested-sangvi-budruk-police-patil-murder-allegedly-land-dispute.html","h":"Bhor: three arrested for murder of Sangvi Budruk police patil, allegedly over land dispute","s":"A court has remanded three accused, aged 22, 19 and 18, in police custody until 23 November 2026 in the Sangvi Budruk police patil murder case.","k":"Bhor","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T16:14:26+05:30","g":["Bhor","Rajgad police","Sangvi Budruk","police patil"],"b":"Rajgad police have arrested three people in the murder of the police patil of Sangvi Budruk in Bhor taluka, a 50-year-old who was attacked around 6 pm on 16 November near the Lamandev temple in Sangvi Budruk.\nHe was riding home from his field on a motorcycle when the accused stopped him and struck him with a sickle on the head, near the right ear and on the right upper arm. He died of his injuries.\nThe victim was allegedly killed over a dispute about a relinquishment deed for ancestral land. A 22-year-old accused from Sangvi Budruk is said to be his nephew.\nThe nephew allegedly plotted the murder with friends over land rights. The killing is said to stem from the land dispute.\nThe three accused, aged 22, 19 and 18, were arrested on 18 November, and a court has remanded them in police custody until 23 November 2026.\nOn the victim’s son’s complaint, Rajgad police station of the Pune Rural Police registered a case under sections 103(1) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the relevant sections of the Arms Act.\nVillagers had protested outside Rajgad police station demanding the arrests, and warned that they would block the Pune–Satara highway if the accused were not caught soon.\nAssistant Police Inspector Chetan Machhale is investigating the motive and each accused’s role.","i":"illustration-5a55aea816","a":["Bhor","Bhor taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-sinhagad-fort-13-allegedly-illegal-mobile-towers-unesco-tag-concerns.html","h":"Sinhagad Fort: 13 allegedly illegal mobile towers have raised UNESCO tag concerns","s":"Sinhagad Fort's UNESCO World Heritage tag faces concerns over 13 allegedly illegal mobile towers on the fort, with an inquiry expected within 2–3 days.","k":"Sinhagad Fort","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T16:03:22+05:30","g":["Sinhagad Fort","UNESCO World Heritage tag","Mobile towers","Pune"],"b":"Concerns over Sinhagad Fort's UNESCO World Heritage tag have been raised by 13 allegedly illegal mobile towers on the fort.\nThe State Archaeology Department says no permission was granted for the towers. An inquiry is expected within 2–3 days.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-nigdi-appughar-49-trees-felled-environmentalists-demand-fir.html","h":"Nigdi Appughar: 49 trees felled, environmentalists demand FIR","s":"Environmentalists have demanded an FIR against Pushpak Amusement, the private agency that maintains Appughar, the civic-owned amusement park in Nigdi, over 49 trees cut where pruning of only 13 had been allowed.","k":"Appughar, Nigdi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T15:52:36+05:30","g":["Nigdi","Appughar","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Garden Department"],"b":"Despite permission having been granted for pruning only 13 trees, 49 mature trees were allegedly cut at Appughar, the civic-owned amusement park in Nigdi, Pimpri-Chinchwad. No FIR has been registered so far.\nThe Garden Department's inspection confirmed the felling of 49 trees. The department is said to have issued only a notice to Pushpak Amusement, the private agency that maintains the park.\nEnvironmentalists have questioned the civic administration's response. They have demanded an FIR against the agency, the suspension of officials allegedly involved, an investigation into possible collusion between officials and the contractor, and strict action against those responsible for the felling.\nResidents have also demanded accountability, alleging that the felling has damaged the area's green cover.","i":"illustration-62487cf6ec","a":["Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/pune-alka-chowk-ncp-sp-youth-wing-demands-fir-ajit-pawar-crash.html","h":"Alka Chowk protest: NCP (SP) youth wing demands FIR in Ajit Pawar plane crash","s":"An NCP (SP) youth leader in Pune criticised the BJP for targeting MLA Rohit Pawar through its workers.","k":"Alka Chowk","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T15:41:25+05:30","g":["Pune","NCP (SP)","Alka Chowk","Ajit Pawar","Rohit Pawar"],"b":"The youth wing of the Nationalist Congress Party (Sharadchandra Pawar), or NCP (SP), protested against the BJP at Alka Chowk in Pune on Wednesday, November 18, demanding an FIR in the Ajit Pawar plane crash case.\nThe protest was in support of MLA Rohit Pawar. The youth wing also demanded a thorough investigation into the plane crash involving former Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar. The protest came a day after Bharatiya Janata Yuva Morcha workers staged a demonstration against Rohit Pawar.\nAddressing the protesters, a Pune-based youth leader of the NCP (SP) said the party had been pursuing the demand for registration of a criminal case for the past 10 months, but the government had failed to act despite repeated submissions of evidence.\nHe alleged that the Maharashtra government had failed to act despite Karnataka registering a Zero FIR in connection with the matter. He also criticised the BJP for targeting Rohit Pawar through its workers, and said the NCP (SP) would continue its protest within the framework of the Constitution.\n“If the government has nothing to fear, why is it hesitating to register a case and allow the investigation to establish the truth? Let the truth come out. We want the matter investigated fairly,” he said.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/kothrud-posters-question-fir-delay-probe-report-ajit-pawar-plane-crash.html","h":"Kothrud posters question FIR delay, probe report on Ajit Pawar plane crash","s":"Posters that have surfaced in Kothrud target the BJP-led government, and NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar has raised the absence of an FIR in connection with Ajit Pawar's death.","k":"Kothrud","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T15:19:52+05:30","g":["Kothrud","Ajit Pawar","Rohit Pawar","Plane crash"],"b":"Posters have surfaced in Kothrud, a BJP stronghold in Pune, questioning the delay in an FIR and the inquiry report on the plane crash that killed deputy chief minister Ajit Pawar.\nThe posters question the state government's handling of the crash. They ask why an FIR has not been registered, where the inquiry report is and when the truth behind the crash will be made public. They were put up by an NCP (SP) worker and target the BJP-led government.\nThe posters carry questions such as, “No FIR, no concrete information on the investigation, no inquiry report and no truth about the crash before the public.” They ask why several questions remain unanswered despite considerable time having passed since the accident, and demand that the government disclose the findings to the public.\nNCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar has also raised the absence of an FIR in connection with Ajit Pawar's death, and has demanded a thorough investigation and strict action against those responsible. He has questioned the role of the airline company allegedly responsible for the crash and accused Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis of shielding the company.\nAccording to the allegations, no concrete decision has been announced on the demands for further investigation.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/shiv-sena-ubt-chetan-pawar-71000-reward-anyone-who-slaps-shaina-nc.html","h":"Shiv Sena (UBT)’s Chetan Pawar announces ₹71,000 reward for anyone who slaps Shaina NC","s":"Shiv Sena (UBT) Pimpri-Chinchwad city president Chetan Pawar announced a reward for slapping Shaina NC while claiming his party respects women’s dignity and opposes violence against women.","k":"Shiv Sena (UBT)","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T15:01:46+05:30","g":["Shiv Sena (UBT)","Chetan Pawar","Shaina NC","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"Shiv Sena (UBT)’s Chetan Pawar has announced a ₹71,000 cash reward for anyone who slaps Shaina NC, amid a political controversy over her allegedly tearing a photograph of Shiv Sena founder Balasaheb Thackeray during a protest in Mumbai.\nPawar is Shiv Sena (UBT)’s Pimpri-Chinchwad city president. Shaina NC is national spokesperson of the Eknath Shinde-led Shiv Sena.\nPawar said the party’s Mumbai unit had already announced a ₹1 lakh reward and that his Pimpri-Chinchwad unit would add ₹71,000 more. He made the announcement while claiming that his party respects women’s dignity and opposes violence against women.\nShaina NC has denied deliberately disrespecting Balasaheb Thackeray. She has apologised to his admirers if her actions hurt their sentiments.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/mohol-asks-sharad-pawar-supriya-sule-stand-rohit-pawar-childish-allegations.html","h":"Mohol asks where Sharad Pawar, Supriya Sule stand on ‘childish’ allegations by Rohit Pawar","s":"Union Minister Murlidhar Mohol asked where Sharad Pawar and MP Supriya Sule stand on ‘childish’ allegations by Rohit Pawar.","k":"Murlidhar Mohol","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T14:49:54+05:30","g":["Murlidhar Mohol","Rohit Pawar","Supriya Sule","Sharad Pawar"],"b":"Union Minister Murlidhar Mohol, speaking to reporters at the mics, called Rohit Pawar’s allegations ‘childish’ and asked where Sharad Pawar and MP Supriya Sule stand on them.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-pangare-purandar-woman-murdered-sharp-weapon-open-road.html","h":"Pangare, Purandar: woman, 47, murdered with sharp weapon on open road","s":"The exact motive behind the killing of a 47-year-old woman in Pangare village is not yet clear, and Saswad police are working to identify and catch the attacker.","k":"Pangare, Purandar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T14:39:09+05:30","g":["Pangare","Purandar","Saswad police"],"b":"A 47-year-old woman was murdered on an open road in Pangare, Purandar taluka, on Thursday morning, when an unknown attacker suddenly struck her with a sharp weapon.\nThe attack took place at about 8.30 am. She had left home for work as usual and was walking towards the bus stand. Preliminary information is that she died on the spot from severe blows to her head.\nThe killing has caused a stir in Pangare village and the surrounding area, and fear among residents.\nThe village police patil informed Saswad police at once. Police reached the spot and drew up a panchnama, and the body has been sent to Saswad Rural Hospital for a post-mortem.\nThe exact motive is not yet clear. Police are examining various possibilities: whether the attack was planned, and whether a personal dispute, a family reason or something else lay behind it.\nSaswad police are investigating the case and are working to identify and catch the attacker.","i":"","a":["Purandar","Purandar taluka","Purandhar"]},{"u":"pune/pune-customer-allegedly-finds-cockroach-lassi-wassi-bavdhan.html","h":"Customer allegedly finds cockroach in lassi at Lassi Wassi in Bavdhan","s":"Citizens have urged the Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to take stringent action against those responsible for a cockroach a customer allegedly found in a lassi in Bavdhan.","k":"Bavdhan","c":"City","t":"2026-11-19T14:27:47+05:30","g":["Bavdhan","Lassi Wassi","Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration","Pune"],"b":"At the Lassi Wassi outlet in Bavdhan, Pune, a customer is said to have found a cockroach in a glass of lassi while drinking it.\nCitizens have urged the Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to investigate the matter and take stringent action against those responsible.","i":"illustration-506412dd0c","a":["Bavdhan","Bawdhan","Bavdhan Budruk"]},{"u":"pune/khed-taluka-two-companies-lose-15-40-crore-alleged-aluminium-theft.html","h":"Khed taluka: two companies lose over ₹15.40 crore in alleged aluminium theft","s":"A case has been registered over an alleged aluminium theft from two Khed taluka companies, where the total estimated loss stands at ₹15,40,92,876.","k":"Khed taluka","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T14:06:16+05:30","g":["Khed","Vasuli","Aluminium theft"],"b":"Two companies in Khed taluka’s Vasuli industrial area have lost over ₹15.40 crore in an alleged aluminium theft that, according to the police complaint, took place between December 2018 and August 2026.\nTwo store officers working at the companies allegedly misused their positions and, in collusion with eight others, removed aluminium stock, scrap material and aluminium meant for recycling from the company premises.\nThe materials were allegedly taken outside the premises and sold to scrap dealers for financial gain. The investigation suggests the alleged involvement of contractual workers, a recruitment agency representative, transport workers and scrap dealers.\nThe total estimated loss to the two companies stands at ₹15,40,92,876. A case has been registered following the complaint.","i":"illustration-a419d69fee","a":["Khed","Khed taluka","Khed Pune"]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-removes-encroachments-outside-dagdusheth-temple-using-jcbs.html","h":"PMC removes encroachments outside Pune's Dagdusheth temple using JCBs","s":"Pune Municipal Corporation officials removed unauthorised structures and encroachments outside Pune's Shreemant Dagdusheth Halwai Ganpati Temple with JCB machines, to clear obstructions in the temple area.","k":"Dagdusheth temple","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T13:55:36+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Dagdusheth temple","Anti-encroachment drive"],"b":"Using JCBs, civic officials of the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) removed encroachments outside Pune's Shreemant Dagdusheth Halwai Ganpati Temple.\nIn the anti-encroachment drive, civic officials used JCB machines to remove unauthorised structures and encroachments from the temple premises.\nPMC took the action to clear obstructions that encroachments had caused in the temple area.","i":"illustration-8856f2a4f2","a":[]},{"u":"pune/sassoon-hospital-cardiology-opd-crowded-patients-wait-for-hours.html","h":"Sassoon Hospital cardiology OPD crowded, patients wait for hours","s":"Sassoon Hospital’s cardiology outpatient check-up is held only one day a week, and only a few of the hospital’s eight sanctioned super-specialist posts are filled.","k":"Sassoon Hospital","c":"City","t":"2026-11-19T13:44:54+05:30","g":["Sassoon Hospital","Cardiology","OPD","Pune"],"b":"Patients waited for hours on Tuesday at the cardiology OPD of Sassoon Hospital, where the queue reached right up to the entrance, leaving many standing in the sun.\nThe wait was to see a doctor, even just to find out whether patients’ heartbeats were regular or irregular. The cardiology department’s outpatient check-up runs only one day a week, so a large crowd turns up that day.\nCrowds at the case-paper and OPD windows have raised concerns about patient safety, with maintenance work under way on the ground-floor OPD building. Of the hospital’s eight sanctioned super-specialist posts, only a few have been filled.\nAccording to hospital figures, more than 6,000 patients underwent angiography, angioplasty and other cardiac treatment between 2023 and September 2026.\nA patient demanded a decentralised OPD and digital registration, so that patients come at scheduled times rather than all on one day.\nDr Rajesh Karyakarte, acting dean of Sassoon Hospital, said heart patients get free treatment or treatment at a nominal fee. He said that with heart patients rising every day, four to five patients a day are examined in depth and operated on, so the OPD for primary and regular check-ups has been planned for one day a week, with adequate staff provided for it.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-bibwewadi-restaurant-group-allegedly-attacks-man-son-in-law.html","h":"Bibwewadi restaurant: group allegedly attacks man, 54, and son-in-law","s":"A man who has difficulty walking and speaking was allegedly targeted by three named people and five to six others at a Bibwewadi restaurant; no arrests have been made so far.","k":"Bibwewadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T13:34:14+05:30","g":["Pune","Bibwewadi","Even Good Food Restaurant"],"b":"A group allegedly attacked a 54-year-old man and his son-in-law at Even Good Food Restaurant near Chandralok Chowk in Bibwewadi on November 15, between 9 pm and 11 pm.\nThree named people and five to six others allegedly targeted the man, who has difficulty walking and speaking. One of them allegedly demanded cash from the restaurant and pocket money from the complainant to settle the matter.\nNo arrests have been made so far.","i":"illustration-c2536c8bca","a":["Bibwewadi","Bibvewadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-speeding-car-hits-two-wheeler-bhosari-driver-allegedly-flees.html","h":"MIDC Bhosari: speeding car hits two-wheeler, two seriously injured; driver allegedly flees","s":"A speeding car hit a two-wheeler carrying two friends in Pimpri-Chinchwad's MIDC Bhosari area, and a driver allegedly fled the spot.","k":"MIDC Bhosari","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-19T13:23:24+05:30","g":["Speeding car","Two-wheeler","MIDC Bhosari","FIR"],"b":"Two friends aged 23 were returning to their room on a two-wheeler, which a speeding car rammed into around midnight in front of Newtech Couplings Pvt. Ltd. in Pimpri-Chinchwad's MIDC Bhosari area.\nBoth riders sustained serious injuries and are undergoing treatment at a private hospital.\nThe car driver allegedly fled the spot without helping the injured. An FIR has been registered at MIDC Bhosari Police Station, and police are searching for the absconding driver.","i":"illustration-aaf376fa4d","a":["Bhosari"]},{"u":"pune/khadakwasla-water-chhath-puja-paint-litter-raise-concerns.html","h":"Khadakwasla water: Chhath Puja paint and litter raise concerns","s":"A social activist and local resident has warned that chemicals in oil paint could enter water used for drinking in Daund and Indapur and other areas, though the extent of any contamination has not been established.","k":"Khadakwasla dam backwaters","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T13:11:50+05:30","g":["Pune","Khadakwasla","Chhath Puja","Water contamination"],"b":"Along the Khadakwasla dam backwaters, oil paint markings and uncollected garbage that remain after Chhath Puja celebrations on November 15 raise concerns of possible water contamination.\nWater flows downstream along a route that includes this stretch when the dam gates are opened.\nThe water is used for drinking in areas including Daund and Indapur, a social activist and local resident said. He warned that chemicals in oil paint could enter the water, though the extent of any contamination has not been established.\nThe activist also said the paint may persist on the banks for months. He urged officials to inspect the area, check whether permission was granted for the markings and assess any environmental impact. He has not filed a formal complaint with the irrigation department.\nResidents also criticised the litter left behind and called for organisers to clean up after public gatherings near the water. They urged authorities to monitor the dam’s surroundings and issue clear guidelines for events in the area.","i":"","a":["Khadakwasla","Khadakvasla"]},{"u":"pune/congress-ncp-corporators-protest-pmc-timber-market-fire-inquiry.html","h":"Congress, NCP corporators protest at PMC general body meeting, demand Timber Market fire inquiry","s":"Congress and NCP corporators called for an investigation into the recent Timber Market fire and sought answers from the civic administration.","k":"Timber Market fire","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T12:59:21+05:30","g":["Congress","NCP","PMC","Timber Market fire"],"b":"Opposition corporators from Congress and the NCP held a protest at a general body meeting of the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC), where they demanded an inquiry into the recent fire at Timber Market.\nInside the civic body, the opposition members raised the issue and called for an investigation into the incident. They sought answers from the civic administration.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/baramati-lawyer-claims-central-state-refused-cctv-ajit-pawar-plane-crash.html","h":"RTI: Baramati lawyer claims central and state agencies refused CCTV linked to Ajit Pawar’s fatal plane crash","s":"A Baramati advocate claims the Bureau of Civil Aviation Security turned down his appeal for Mumbai airport CCTV footage and Mumbai police refused to provide footage of Ajit Pawar’s route.","k":"Baramati RTI","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-19T12:46:48+05:30","g":["Ajit Pawar","RTI","Baramati","BCAS","Mumbai police"],"b":"Central and state agencies refused to share CCTV footage linked to Ajit Pawar’s fatal plane crash, a Baramati lawyer who sought it under the RTI Act claims.\nThe advocate is a resident of Someshwarnagar in Baramati taluka. He sought Mumbai airport CCTV footage from 6 am to 9 am on January 28, 2026, and footage of Pawar’s journey from Devgiri bungalow to Mumbai airport.\nHe filed a first appeal with the Bureau of Civil Aviation Security (BCAS) after his initial request for the airport footage was rejected. BCAS rejected the appeal, stating that the footage had been handed over to police for investigation and could not be shared with ordinary citizens.\nMumbai police refused to provide the route footage, saying it was not related to public activity or public interest, and also cited concerns over individual privacy.\nDespite BCAS confirming that the airport footage exists and was shared with investigators, the advocate questioned the refusal.\n“If there is clarity that no foul play was involved in Ajit Pawar’s death, the available footage should be made public to address the doubts in people’s minds,” the advocate said. He called on both governments to take the initiative in the interest of transparency.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/viman-nagar-woman-81-allegedly-duped-lakh-mumbai-crime-branch-officers.html","h":"Viman Nagar woman, 81, allegedly duped of ₹82.30 lakh by ‘Mumbai Crime Branch officers’","s":"Pune Cyber Police have registered a case against unidentified individuals and suspected bank account holders over an alleged ₹82.30 lakh fraud on an 81-year-old woman that allegedly began in the first week of August and came to light in November.","k":"Viman Nagar","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T12:35:32+05:30","g":["Viman Nagar","Pune Cyber Police","Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita"],"b":"Fraudsters posing as Mumbai Crime Branch officers allegedly contacted a Viman Nagar woman, 81, through WhatsApp video calls and duped her of ₹82.30 lakh. The fraud allegedly began in the first week of August and came to light in November.\nThey allegedly claimed that the Supreme Court had issued a non-bailable warrant against her. Threatening her with arrest and imprisonment, they allegedly kept her under virtual surveillance and pressured her into transferring money.\nShe allegedly broke her fixed deposits and pledged her gold jewellery to arrange the money.\nGenuine law enforcement agencies do not conduct investigations or demand money through WhatsApp video calls.\nPune Cyber Police have registered a case against unidentified individuals and the suspected bank account holders under the Information Technology Act and the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. Further investigation is underway.","i":"illustration-2877fe69fe","a":["Viman Nagar","Vimantal"]},{"u":"pune/jm-road-khau-galli-fda-orders-8-food-establishments-stop-operations.html","h":"JM Road Khau Galli: FDA orders 8 food establishments to stop operations, suspends 6 licences","s":"The Food and Drug Administration, Pune, has proposed compounding penalties totalling Rs 2.40 lakh against eight unregistered food establishments in the JM Road Khau Galli area of Shivajinagar.","k":"JM Road Khau Galli","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T12:11:22+05:30","g":["FDA","JM Road","Shivajinagar","Food safety"],"b":"The Food and Drug Administration (FDA), Pune, took action against 17 food establishments in the JM Road Khau Galli area of Shivajinagar in a special inspection drive on 18 November 2026.\nEight establishments were ordered to immediately stop operations for functioning without valid food safety registration or licences. The licences of six others were suspended with immediate effect for violating hygiene standards, and two more were served improvement notices.\nAgainst each of the eight unregistered establishments, the FDA has proposed a compounding penalty of Rs 30,000, a total of Rs 2.40 lakh.\nThe drive was conducted by the FDA’s Pune Zone-2 team at JM Road Khau Galli, near the Junglee Maharaj Temple and around the NCR Hotel area. The action was taken under the FDA’s ‘Safe Food Safe Maharashtra’ campaign, for violations of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, and the rules framed under it.\nThe eight establishments ordered to stop operations are: Shrinath Pizza and Sandwiches (near NCR Hotel, JM Road), Raj Chinese Fast Food (JM Road), Hindavi Swarajya (opposite Junglee Maharaj Temple, JM Road), Everest Momos, Jai Malhar Bhurji Centre and Shawarma Centre (JM Road Khau Galli), and Utkarsh Mandal Love Juice Point and Sai Juice, Milkshake and Sharbat Centre (opposite Junglee Maharaj Temple, Ghole Road).\nFDA Joint Commissioner (Pune Division) Shrikant Karkale said all establishments had been instructed to strictly comply with food safety regulations. Karkale warned that businesses should not resume operations until they fulfil the prescribed requirements.","i":"","a":["Shivajinagar","Shivajinagar Gaothan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-kirkatwadi-sinhagad-road-koyta-gang-allegedly-strikes-again.html","h":"Kirkatwadi on Sinhagad Road: koyta gang allegedly strikes again, residents in fear","s":"Residents of Kirkatwadi on Sinhagad Road are in fear after a fresh attack allegedly involving the koyta gang, and those accused in an attack in the area last month are said to have been released within a few days.","k":"Kirkatwadi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T11:59:22+05:30","g":["Kirkatwadi","Sinhagad Road","Koyta gang","Pune"],"b":"Another attack allegedly involving the koyta gang has left local residents in fear in Kirkatwadi on Sinhagad Road, where panic is said to have returned.\nLast month, a person was seriously attacked in the area. The accused in that case are said to have been released within a few days.\nThe latest attack is said to involve the same group.","i":"","a":["Kirkatwadi"]},{"u":"pune/pimple-gurav-atm-thief-allegedly-sprays-camera-takes-cash.html","h":"Pimple Gurav ATM thief allegedly sprays camera, takes ₹20.30 lakh","s":"Sangvi Police have registered a case against an unidentified person; ₹20.30 lakh in cash was allegedly stolen from a Bank of Maharashtra ATM.","k":"Pimple Gurav","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T11:48:08+05:30","g":["Pimple Gurav","Pimpri-Chinchwad","ATM","Sangvi Police","Bank of Maharashtra"],"b":"A thief allegedly sprayed paint on the CCTV camera of a Bank of Maharashtra ATM in Shwetayan Colony, Pimple Gurav, Pimpri-Chinchwad, in the early hours of Wednesday, 18 November, so the crime would not be recorded.\nThe thief then allegedly used a gas cutter to break open the machine and stole ₹20.30 lakh in cash. About ₹20,30,800 was taken within a few minutes before the thief fled.\nSangvi Police have registered a case against an unidentified person and launched an investigation to trace the accused. Police are examining the available evidence to identify and arrest the thief.","i":"","a":["Pimple Gurav"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fursungi-boy-allegedly-hacked-to-death-by-four-minors.html","h":"Fursungi: 17-year-old boy allegedly hacked to death with machetes by four minors","s":"Four minors aged between 16 and 17 years have been detained and arraigned before the Juvenile Justice Board, and a murder case has been registered over a 17-year-old boy allegedly hacked to death in Fursungi.","k":"Fursungi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T11:36:51+05:30","g":["Fursungi","Pune","Juvenile Justice Board","Arms Act"],"b":"Four minors allegedly hacked a 17-year-old boy to death with machetes near railway tracks in Fursungi, Pune district, at around 8.30 pm on Tuesday.\nThe spot is on the road connecting the Saswad railway station to Sanket Vihar in Bhekrai Nagar. Police said the four minors struck the boy's head, face and both hands with machetes, leading to his death, following an old dispute.\nThe four minors, aged between 16 and 17 years, have been detained and arraigned before the Juvenile Justice Board. Police said there were no CCTV cameras at the spot, and a forensic team was called to the scene.\nA murder case was registered on a complaint by the boy's 22-year-old sister, and charges under the Arms Act and the Maharashtra Police Act were also invoked. Inspector Amol More of the Fursungi police station said police are trying to ascertain the exact reason behind the past dispute and the sequence of events immediately before the attack.","i":"illustration-58fccee9b3","a":["Fursungi","Phursungi"]},{"u":"pune/packed-pmpml-e-bus-seen-tilting-dangerously-on-road.html","h":"Playing with passengers’ lives? Packed PMPML e-bus seen tilting dangerously on road","s":"A PMPML electric bus leaning to one side in a viral video has prompted serious questions about public transport safety in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad.","k":"PMPML e-bus","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T11:25:41+05:30","g":["PMPML","Electric bus","Public transport safety","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"In a video viral on social media, an overcrowded PMPML electric bus operating on Route 372 (Megapolis) is seen tilting dangerously to one side while moving.\nThe bus, registration number MH 12 RN 8063, is seen leaning precariously instead of running upright, sparking suspicion of a technical snag or suspension failure.\nThe packed bus carried a large number of passengers, and it posed a serious accident risk to commuters inside the bus and to other motorists on the road.\nThe video has raised serious questions over public transport safety in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad. Citizens have urged the administration to take immediate cognisance and investigate the lapse, and have questioned whether PMPML authorities and private contractors are conducting regular maintenance and safety inspections.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/wakad-4-drivers-booked-after-viral-reel-of-dangerous-car-stunts.html","h":"Wakad: 4 drivers booked after viral reel of dangerous car stunts","s":"Four car drivers were booked after a stunt video became viral on social media.","k":"Wakad","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-19T11:12:35+05:30","g":["Wakad","Hinjawadi Police","Mumbai–Bengaluru Highway","Viral reel"],"b":"Hinjawadi Police booked four car drivers late on Tuesday, 17 November, over a viral reel of dangerous stunts on the Mumbai–Bengaluru Highway at Wakad.\nThe drivers allegedly swerved their cars across the busy highway in front of Tip Top Hotel and recorded videos on 29 October at around 1:30 pm. The video became viral on social media.\nOne of the cars was allegedly being driven without a registration number plate.\nPolice constable Ashok Athare of the Hinjawadi Traffic Division filed the complaint and said the drivers endangered not only their own lives but also the safety of other road users. Hinjawadi Police are investigating the case.","i":"","a":["Wakad","Vakad"]},{"u":"pune/pune-district-all-13-tehsils-under-drought-first-time-54-years.html","h":"Pune district: all 13 tehsils under drought for first time in 54 years","s":"Vaibhav Tambe, district agriculture officer, said crop-loss assessments have started in the Maval and Mulshi tehsils, and officials say vegetable prices may shoot up.","k":"Pune district","c":"City","t":"2026-11-19T11:00:57+05:30","g":["Pune","Pune drought","Vegetable prices","Farmers","Maval","Mulshi"],"b":"With Maval and Mulshi, two tehsils missing from the initial list of drought-affected areas, all 13 tehsils of Pune district are under drought for the first time in 54 years.\nThe state government has directed the district agriculture office to carry out crop-loss assessments in Maval and Mulshi. With the two, all 13 tehsils of the district, a combined cultivable area of roughly 5 lakh hectares, face acute aridity for the first time since 1972.\n“Barring some pockets of Haveli tehsil, the entire district is now drought affected,” said Vaibhav Tambe, district agriculture officer.\nTambe said crop-loss assessments have started across Maval and Mulshi.\nOfficials said scores of farmers have scaled back sowing, and some are even abandoning water-intensive crops such as sugarcane, fruit and certain vegetables. A senior agriculture department official said the problem may worsen by February, when a shortage of water for agriculture is likely.\nVegetable prices may shoot up, officials say. Officials fear the situation in Marathwada, combined with the aridity in Pune district, could put additional pressure on vegetable arrivals in urban markets, including Pune and Mumbai, and they foresee an unprecedented increase in vegetable prices in the coming months, particularly of leafy vegetables.\nA senior official at Pune’s APMC market said price escalation of all vegetables is bound to happen and that so far, supply is holding because of water availability in the district.","i":"illustration-a4dc6f6879","a":["Maval","Mawal","Maval taluka","Mulshi","Mulshi taluka"]},{"u":"pune/maharera-rejects-goel-ganga-excuses-orders-oc-possession-two-bavdhan-duplexes.html","h":"MahaRERA rejects Goel Ganga’s excuses, orders OC and possession of two Bavdhan duplexes","s":"Goel Ganga Developments LLP must hand over lawful possession of two Ganga Utopia duplexes in Bavdhan within 60 days of securing an Occupancy Certificate, MahaRERA has directed.","k":"Bavdhan duplexes","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-19T10:28:02+05:30","g":["Goel Ganga","Ganga Utopia","Bavdhan","Occupancy Certificate"],"b":"The Maharashtra Real Estate Regulatory Authority (MahaRERA) has ordered Goel Ganga Developments LLP to obtain the mandatory Occupancy Certificate (OC) for two luxury duplexes at its Ganga Utopia project in Bavdhan, rejecting its excuses for the delayed possession.\nThe developer has been directed to hand over lawful possession within 60 days of securing the OC, and to compensate the buyer for the delay.\nThe order came on a complaint by a homebuyer who had invested approximately ₹1.39 crore in the two duplex units. The developer, which collected nearly 95% of the consideration, allegedly failed to secure the necessary approvals and offered possession without the mandatory OC.\nGoel Ganga obtained a part OC for other units in Building E1 in April 2025, but the revised sanctioned plan and OC for the two duplexes remained pending.\nDuring the proceedings, the developer pointed to a dispute with the original landowner, Marvel Omega Builders Pvt Ltd, the landowner’s alleged non-cooperation, insolvency proceedings and disruptions caused by the Covid-19 pandemic. MahaRERA refused to accept these explanations as grounds for denying the buyer his statutory rights.\nMahaRERA Member II Ravindra Deshpande passed the order. Goel Ganga Developments LLP’s key partners are Subhash Sitaram Goel, Anurag Subhash Goel and Gunjan Subhash Goel.","i":"illustration-aa072f91dc","a":["Bavdhan","Bawdhan","Bavdhan Budruk"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-bans-rockets-aerial-firecrackers-across-city-till-25-november.html","h":"PMC bans rockets, aerial firecrackers across city till 25 November","s":"Following a sharp rise in fire incidents during Diwali, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) has prohibited rockets and other aerial firecrackers until 25 November across the city.","k":"PMC aerial firecracker ban","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-19T10:17:04+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Firecrackers","Diwali"],"b":"On Wednesday, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) banned the use of rockets and other aerial firecrackers across the city until 25 November.\nThe prohibition follows a sharp rise in fire incidents during Diwali.","i":"illustration-ba970c7d7a","a":[]},{"u":"pune/massive-timber-market-fire-bhawani-peth-45-shops-6-houses-dispute-suspected.html","h":"Massive Timber Market fire in Bhawani Peth damages 45 shops, 6 houses; dispute between 2 individuals suspected","s":"Four families affected by the Timber Market fire in Bhawani Peth have been shifted to a shelter at Transit Camp, No. 8 Colony, and the Pune Fire Brigade's first team reached the spot at 2.09 am.","k":"Bhawani Peth","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-19T10:03:56+05:30","g":["Timber Market","Bhawani Peth","Pune fire"],"b":"A massive fire that broke out around 2.05 am on Wednesday, November 18, at Timber Market near Jai Vallabh School in Bhawani Peth has damaged around 45 shops, six houses and a vehicle.\nA dispute between two individuals is suspected to have triggered the fire. A senior official, speaking on condition of anonymity, said that one of them allegedly set the place on fire in anger following the dispute. The exact cause of the fire and the alleged role of the individuals involved are yet to be officially confirmed.\nThe first team of the Pune Fire Brigade reached the spot at 2.09 am. With the wooden material, the fire spread rapidly.\nNearly 150 firefighters and around 10 officers brought the blaze under control within two hours. They had 31 firefighting vehicles, including fire tenders and water tankers from the Pune Municipal Corporation, Pune Cantonment and PMRDA, along with four JCB machines. Residents were evacuated, and four affected families have been shifted to a shelter at Transit Camp, No. 8 Colony.\nMayor Manjusha Nagpure, Standing Committee Chairman Shrinath Bhimale and House Leader Ganesh Bidkar visited the site. Fire officials said the operation received support from the police, the 108 ambulance service, MSEDCL and local residents.\nThe Pune District Collector's office has been informed to conduct a panchnama to assess the damage. The extent of the financial losses is yet to be assessed.","i":"","a":["Bhavani Peth","Bhawani Peth"]},{"u":"pune/pune-crowd-nabs-three-alleged-phone-thieves-bhosari-bus-stop.html","h":"Crowd nabs three alleged phone thieves at Bhosari bus stop near Pune Station","s":"Police Inspector Dasharath Govindrao Taledwar is investigating FIR 0315/2026, registered by Bundgarden police against three men accused of stealing a commuter’s phone.","k":"Pune Station","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-18T13:24:19+05:30","g":["Pune Station","Bundgarden","Phone theft","Bhosari bus stop"],"b":"People nearby caught two of three men accused of stealing a commuter’s phone at the Bhosari bus stop near Pune Station; the third, who had run off and got into an auto-rickshaw, was caught too.\nThe commuter, Kariya Khuplal Rajbhar, 50, told police that at about 4.30 am on 17 November, as he boarded a crowded bus to Bhosari at the bus stop by the Tukaram Sheth Shinde parking lot, Pune Station, his Realme C61 phone was taken from his back pocket. He was returning from the wedding of his friend Shivram’s son in Hyderabad.\nOn finding the phone gone, he got off the bus, saw three men running and shouted “Thief! Catch them!”\nThe three were handed over at the Pune Railway Station police chowky. They gave their names as Nadeem Kasim Bagmar, 38, Shahrukh Rahimuddin Momin, 32, and Wasim Wajidali Ansari, 37.\nThe FIR says Rajbhar’s phone was found in Momin’s right pocket and four more phones, two Samsung, one Oppo and one Itel, were found under the driver’s seat of the rickshaw. The FIR says the three told police they had stolen the phones from passengers’ back pockets at the Bhosari bus stop. Police seized the five phones and the rickshaw, which are valued together at ₹1.6 lakh.\nBundgarden police booked the three on 17 November in FIR 0315/2026 under BNS sections 303(2) (theft) and 3(5) (common intention). Inspector Shashikant Bharat Chavan registered the case, and Police Inspector Dasharath Govindrao Taledwar is investigating.","i":"illustration-bd4f06bb52","a":["Bund Garden"]},{"u":"pune/kondhwa-vehicles-park-four-five-lanes-opposite-sheetal-petrol-pump.html","h":"Kondhwa: vehicles park in four to five lanes opposite Sheetal Petrol Pump where signboard permits one","s":"Local shopkeepers are demanding fines for violators and strict enforcement of parking rules where vehicles occupy four to five lanes opposite Sheetal Petrol Pump in Kondhwa.","k":"Kondhwa","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-18T13:13:43+05:30","g":["Pune","Kondhwa","Sheetal Petrol Pump","parking","traffic congestion"],"b":"Despite a signboard that permits parking in only one lane, motorists continue to park across four to five lanes opposite Sheetal Petrol Pump in Kondhwa. The parking is causing traffic congestion and affecting nearby businesses.\nLocal shopkeepers say multi-lane parking, vehicles left parked for hours and the lack of traffic enforcement make it difficult for customers to reach their shops. Repeated complaints to the authorities have brought no concrete action, they say.\nThe shopkeepers are demanding strict enforcement of parking rules, fines for violators and better traffic management so that customers can reach local businesses.","i":"","a":["Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-youth-allegedly-duped-lakh-fake-japan-visa-racecourse-job.html","h":"Pune youth allegedly duped of ₹4.15 lakh with fake Japan visa, promised racecourse job","s":"A man from Kondhwa allegedly sent a Pune youth a PDF of a fake visa, and PSI Bagade is investigating a case registered by Wanawadi police.","k":"Job fraud","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-18T13:01:01+05:30","g":["Job fraud","Visa fraud","Wanawadi police","Kondhwa"],"b":"Wanawadi police have registered a case against the accused, a man from Kondhwa, over a youth from Pune being allegedly duped of ₹4.15 lakh on the promise of a job at a racecourse in Japan.\nThe accused allegedly collected the money on the pretext of arranging a Japanese visa and later sent the youth a PDF of a fake visa.\nThe youth verified the document and found it was counterfeit, which is how the fraud came to light.\nPSI Bagade is conducting further investigation.","i":"illustration-4cbf9f1edd","a":["Kondhwa","Kondhawa","Kondhwa Budruk","Kondhwa Khurd","Kondhwa Bk"]},{"u":"pune/pune-maval-fda-seizes-edible-oil-raid-avenue-supermarts-facility.html","h":"Maval: FDA seizes ₹50 lakh edible oil in raid on Avenue Supermarts facility","s":"Edible oil valued at ₹50,27,893 and suspected to be substandard and misbranded was seized in the FDA’s Pune Division campaign ‘Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra’.","k":"Maval","c":"City","t":"2026-11-18T11:54:42+05:30","g":["Pune","Maval","FDA","Edible oil","Food Safety"],"b":"The Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration seized 20,085 litres of edible oil worth ₹50.27 lakh in a raid on 17 November at the Avenue Supermarts Limited facility at Gat No. 113, Ambi village, Maval taluka.\nThe stock was valued at ₹50,27,893 and was suspected to be substandard and misbranded under the Food Safety and Standards Act.\nNine samples of different edible oil products were collected and sent to a laboratory. The products were refined sunflower oil, physically refined rice bran oil, kachi ghani mustard oil, and cold-pressed mustard and groundnut oils.\nThe products sampled included brands such as Aadhar, Fortune, Patanjali and Saffola, in pouches, bottles and jars.\nThe FDA’s Pune Division carried out the action as part of its ‘Safe Food, Safe Maharashtra’ campaign. A team led by Assistant Commissioner D. S. Salunkhe conducted the inspection and seizure.\nPune Division Joint Commissioner (Food) Shrikant Karakale said further legal action would be initiated after the laboratory reports are received.","i":"","a":["Maval","Mawal","Maval taluka"]},{"u":"pune/two-men-booked-102-g-mephedrone-near-jj-garden-camp.html","h":"Two men booked after Crime Branch finds 102 g of mephedrone near JJ Garden in Camp","s":"Parvez Jafar Shaikh, 35, and Nabeel Nurmohammad Shaikh, 34, are booked over mephedrone valued at ₹3,07,800, which police say was kept for sale.","k":"Camp","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-18T11:42:30+05:30","g":["Pune","Camp","Mephedrone","NDPS Act","Lashkar police"],"b":"Crime Branch's Anti-Narcotics Squad 1 found 102 g of mephedrone (MD) on two men near JJ Garden in Camp, and the two were booked.\nThe FIR says Pune City Police's Anti-Narcotics Squad 1 stopped Parvez Jafar Shaikh, 35, and Nabeel Nurmohammad Shaikh, 34, on two white Activa scooters at about 6.40 am on 17 November, on the public road opposite Clover Centre, near JJ Garden in Camp.\nPolice say 49 g 35 mg of MD was found on Parvez Jafar Shaikh and 53 g 25 mg on Nabeel Nurmohammad Shaikh, kept for sale. Seized along with the drug, valued at ₹3,07,800, were three mobile phones and the two scooters, ₹4,77,800 in all.\nAccording to the FIR, the two said they had got the MD for sale from Abrar Shaikh alias Bengali Babu of Kondhwa and a mobile number holder, Chandrakant, of Yerawada.\nPolice Havaldar Tushar Salunkhe brought in Umesh Ganesh Kakade and Sudhakar Limbraj Dhurgude as panch witnesses. Amruta Darade, the officer on the forensic mobile van, examined the powder at the spot.\nPSI Yogesh Kotkar led the team of Police Havaldars Sarde (6607), Jadhav (7554), Jadhav (5903), Salunkhe (6456) and Lonkar (8386) and Police Amaldar Gund (8878). He searched the two and drew up the panchnama. Senior Police Inspector Trupti Sonawane, in charge of the squad, was present for the search.\nLashkar police's night-round officer, PSI Swati Bharad, came to the spot with Police Havaldars Marane (684) and Ukirde (7728).\nPolice Havaldar Atul Madhukar Kshirsagar of the Anti-Narcotics Squad 1, Crime Branch, lodged the complaint. Inspector Maruti Bhimsen Khedkar registered the case at Lashkar police station (FIR 0269/2026) on 17 November under sections 8(c), 22(c) and 29 of the NDPS Act. PSI Swati Bharad is investigating.","i":"illustration-7d82ebaca6","a":["Pune Camp","Camp","Pune Cantonment area"]},{"u":"pune/marunji-worker-23-dies-in-fall-from-fourth-floor.html","h":"In Marunji, worker, 23, dies in fall from fourth floor of under-construction building","s":"Police allege that a 23-year-old worker who died in a fall was forced to work without safety gear, and a case of culpable homicide not amounting to murder was registered on Monday.","k":"Marunji","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-18T11:31:52+05:30","g":["Marunji","Hinjewadi","Worker safety","Culpable homicide"],"b":"A 23-year-old worker died in a fall from the fourth floor of an under-construction building in Marunji, where on Saturday he had climbed up to fix a crane trolley without any safety gear.\nA police officer said he lost his balance while fixing the trolley, fell and died of severe head injuries. Hinjewadi police identified him as a resident of Dange Chowk.\nPolice alleged that the builder and contractor forced him to undertake the work without safety gear. A case of culpable homicide not amounting to murder was registered against the builder and contractor on Monday.","i":"illustration-648be21bae","a":["Marunji","Hinjawadi","Hinjewadi","Hinjwadi","Hinjawadi Phase 1","Hinjawadi Phase 2","Hinjawadi Phase 3","Hinjewadi Phase 1","Hinjewadi Phase 2","Hinjewadi Phase 3"]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-cardiac-patient-made-to-walk-spicejet-wheelchair.html","h":"Pune airport: cardiac patient made to walk after SpiceJet failed to provide pre-booked wheelchair","s":"A 52-year-old cardiac patient's son had requested wheelchair assistance while booking the Pune-to-Patna tickets on 5 November.","k":"Pune airport","c":"City","t":"2026-11-18T11:20:33+05:30","g":["Pune airport","cardiac patient","wheelchair assistance","Patna"],"b":"A 52-year-old cardiac patient, travelling with his wife from Pune to Patna on SpiceJet flight SG-646 scheduled for 16 November, was made to walk through Pune airport after SpiceJet failed to provide his pre-booked wheelchair.\nOn 5 November, while booking the tickets, the couple's son had requested wheelchair assistance for his father. The flight was rescheduled to 8.10 pm, kept being delayed through the night, departed around 2 am and landed in Patna at about 4 am.\nThe family was asked to wait at the airport. The son said that after nearly 40 minutes an official from a third-party ground handling agency assured them a wheelchair would be arranged inside the terminal, escorted the couple there, seated them near the check-in counter and disappeared.\nWith no help forthcoming, the couple completed check-in, walked to the first floor for security screening and reached the security hold area on their own.\n“Leaving a cardiac patient without pre-booked wheelchair assistance is unacceptable. The airline and airport staff should have ensured the promised facility was provided,” the son said.\nThe son added that the couple run a hostel in Patna that stayed locked because they could not reach on time, causing financial losses.\nA query to a SpiceJet spokesperson on the wheelchair lapse remained unanswered.","i":"illustration-86fb067cf9","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-ask-pmc-tall-iron-mesh-old-mundhwa-bridge.html","h":"Pune police ask PMC for tall iron mesh on old Mundhwa bridge after 4 suicide deaths","s":"Police are following up with the PMC on tall iron mesh for either side of the old Mundhwa bridge, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Zone VII) Abhinash Kumar said.","k":"Old Mundhwa bridge","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-18T11:09:56+05:30","g":["Pune","Mundhwa","PMC","Pune Police","Iron mesh"],"b":"Pune police have asked the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) for tall iron mesh and other security measures on the old Mundhwa bridge to prevent suicides, and a police team has inspected the bridge and met PMC officials.\nFour suicide deaths occurred at the bridge in the past three months. The team visited after recording the series of suicides at the site.\nAbhinash Kumar, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Zone VII), said the police request is for tall iron mesh on either side of the bridge, and that police are following up with the PMC.\n“The iron mesh or other protective nets cannot stop suicide, but these can certainly save some lives in the future,” he said.\nBhaskar Mahadik, ward officer of the PMC’s Dhole Road office, said the ward office and the road department will carry out a site inspection and the work to place such nets will be speeded up.","i":"illustration-cc9d70a25b","a":["Mundhwa","Mundhawa"]},{"u":"pune/dhankawdi-fda-orders-food-site-shut-over-unhygienic-conditions.html","h":"Dhankawdi: FDA orders food site supplying Shankar Maharaj Math annachhatra shut over unhygienic conditions","s":"An operator preparing food for a community kitchen has been directed to stop food preparation and business activities, and Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration officials say the operator held no valid licence or registration.","k":"Dhankawdi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-18T10:26:52+05:30","g":["FDA","Shankar Maharaj Math","Food safety","Dhankawdi"],"b":"The Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has ordered shut, over unhygienic conditions, a food preparation facility supplying meals for the annachhatra (community kitchen) associated with Shri Sadguru Shankar Maharaj Math in Dhankawdi. FDA Food Safety Officer K. L. Sonkamble inspected the food site near the Math on Monday, November 16.\nAccording to FDA officials, food was being prepared under extremely unhygienic conditions. The operator preparing food for the annachhatra did not hold a valid licence or registration under the Food Safety and Standards Act, according to FDA officials.\nThe FDA also said the food preparation was being carried out on space adjacent to the Math that is allegedly encroached.\nUntil the deficiencies are rectified and the necessary licence or registration is obtained, the operator has been directed to stop food preparation and business activities immediately.\nAs the food was being distributed to devotees as prasad, FDA officials collected samples and sent them to a laboratory for analysis. Further action will be decided after the test results arrive.\nFDA Joint Commissioner (Food) Shrikant Karkale confirmed the inspection findings and said the necessary action would follow the laboratory report.","i":"illustration-b2570e3e9a","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-timber-market-fire-ganj-peth-more-than-50-shops.html","h":"Major fire at Pune’s Timber Market in Ganj Peth: more than 50 shops estimated affected","s":"Around 150 fire personnel took part and 27 fire tenders were deployed at a major fire at shops dealing in wood and timber goods in Ganj Peth; no injuries are known so far.","k":"Timber Market","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-18T10:15:43+05:30","g":["Timber Market","Ganj Peth","Pune Fire Brigade","Fire"],"b":"A major fire at shops dealing in wood and timber goods near Jai Vallabh School in Pune’s Timber Market area of Ganj Peth is estimated to have affected more than 50 shops; it broke out at around 2.05 am on Wednesday, 18 November.\nThe Pune Fire Brigade deployed 27 fire tenders, including one vehicle each from the Pune Cantonment Fire Brigade and the PMRDA Fire Brigade.\nChief Fire Officer Ganesh Sonune and Deputy Chief Fire Officer Vijay Bhilare led around 10 officers and about 150 fire personnel who took part.\nFirefighters worked from all four sides to keep the flames from spreading to adjoining residential buildings. They brought the blaze under control after nearly two hours, and cooling operations were still under way at 6.55 am.\nThe police, the 108 ambulance service, MSEDCL, local residents and the PMC’s Vehicle Depot and Water Supply Department helped in the operation.\nNo injuries are known so far. The exact cause of the fire is yet to be ascertained.","i":"","a":["Ganj Peth","Mahatma Phule Peth"]},{"u":"pune/pune-approach-road-used-by-500-families-now-dirt-track-awaits-repair.html","h":"Tarabaug–Sopan Baug approach road used by 500 families is now a dirt track, still awaiting repair","s":"PMC Additional Commissioner Aarti Patil confirmed that tendering for resurfacing the Tarabaug–Sopan Baug approach road is underway.","k":"Tarabaug–Sopan Baug","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-18T10:03:10+05:30","g":["Tarabaug","Sopan Baug","PMC","Road repair"],"b":"Around 500 families in Tarabaug–Sopan Baug are still waiting for repair of their approach road, which has turned into a dirt track and remained in poor condition despite repeated complaints and assurances from civic authorities.\nPMC officials inspected the site on May 23, 2026, and outlined steps to begin the work. Local corporator Prashant Jagtap assured residents that the process would be expedited. Residents say no visible progress has been made on the ground since February 2026.\nSchoolchildren, senior citizens, domestic workers, labourers and delivery personnel find daily commuting difficult. Water tankers and emergency vehicles also struggle on the road. Residents say it turns slippery with mud and slush in the monsoon, while dry weather brings dust clouds, loose stones and an uneven surface.\nResidents are demanding immediate temporary repairs, proper drainage and dust control, a firm timeline for permanent resurfacing, and regular monitoring of the road.\nAarti Patil, PMC Additional Commissioner, confirmed that the tendering process for resurfacing the road is underway. The PMC Central Road Department is handling the work. Officials indicated the tender process could begin in the last week of December, with a permanent solution expected after the monsoon.","i":"illustration-90f16c3a66","a":["Sopan Baug"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-tax-row-dhangekar-alleges-500-crore-loss-court-order.html","h":"PMC tax row: Dhangekar alleges over ₹500 crore loss, corporation says it followed court order","s":"Former MLA Ravindra Dhangekar has questioned how the reported tax arrears of Gandhi Lawns in Kothrud were reduced from ₹26 crore to less than ₹1 crore; the Pune Municipal Corporation says a court order and applicable rules governed its decision.","k":"PMC tax row","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-18T09:51:51+05:30","g":["Ravindra Dhangekar","Gandhi Lawns","PMC","Pune"],"b":"Former MLA Ravindra Dhangekar has alleged irregularities in the tax assessment and collection department of the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) and accused officials of granting illegal concessions to defaulters, causing losses of more than ₹500 crore to Pune residents.\nThe irregularities he has alleged relate to the tax dues of Gandhi Lawns in Kothrud. He questioned how Gandhi Lawns' reported tax arrears of ₹26 crore were reduced to less than ₹1 crore.\nThe officials he accused are Deputy Commissioner (Tax Assessment) Ravi Pawar and Additional Commissioner Omprakash Divate. He demanded a high-level inquiry into cases approved since Pawar took charge and into the roles of both officials.\nThe PMC has rejected the claims of wrongdoing. It says its decision followed a court order and applicable rules.\nIn its clarification, the PMC said the annual rateable value (ARV) of Gandhi Lawns, initially fixed at ₹23.86 lakh in 2000, was reduced to ₹12.27 lakh after an objection hearing.\nThe property owner appealed to the Small Causes Court in Pune. In 2007 the court set aside the assessment and sent the matter back to the corporation for a fresh hearing and decision.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/pune-bjym-sit-in-against-rohit-pawar-allegations-chief-minister-fadnavis.html","h":"BJYM sit-in in Pune against MLA Rohit Pawar’s allegations on Chief Minister Fadnavis","s":"BJYM office-bearers and workers joined a thiyya andolan organised by the Bharatiya Janata Yuva Morcha, Pune city, against MLA Rohit Pawar’s allegations about Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis.","k":"BJYM sit-in","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T20:43:55+05:30","g":["Pune","BJYM","Rohit Pawar","Devendra Fadnavis","Sit-in protest"],"b":"In Pune, the Bharatiya Janata Yuva Morcha (BJYM) staged a sit-in against the allegations MLA Rohit Pawar has made about Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis.\nBJYM, Pune city, organised the sit-in (thiyya andolan) to protest the allegations and to put forward its stand against them. BJYM office-bearers and workers joined the protest.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/bawankule-responds-to-rohit-pawar-allegations.html","h":"Bawankule to Rohit Pawar: ‘Travelling on a plane doesn’t mean having ties with the plane company’","s":"BJP leader Chandrashekhar Bawankule has answered Rohit Pawar’s allegations, saying travelling on a plane does not mean having ties with the plane company.","k":"Maharashtra","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T20:10:30+05:30","g":["Chandrashekhar Bawankule","Rohit Pawar","Ajit Pawar","Maharashtra"],"b":"The allegations raised by Rohit Pawar drew a response from BJP leader Chandrashekhar Bawankule, who, speaking to the media, replied: “Travelling on a plane doesn’t mean having ties with the plane company.”\nThe remark comes amid the political debate in Maharashtra over the Ajit Pawar plane crash and the aircraft company.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/world-record-pune-455-cakes-cookies-india-heritage.html","h":"World record in Pune: 455 cakes and cookies on India’s heritage","s":"A display of 75 cakes and 380 hand-piped royal icing cookies stood for all 28 states and eight Union Territories.","k":"World record","c":"City","t":"2026-11-17T19:49:00+05:30","g":["Pune","World record","Cakes and cookies","Royal icing"],"b":"A display of 455 cakes and cookies held on 16 November at The Orchid Hotel, Baner-Balewadi, has been certified a world record by the World Book of Records, London.\nPune artist Prachi Dhabal Deb and 36 artists from across India set the record. The record is for the largest display of cakes and cookies celebrating the cultural heritage of every Indian state and Union Territory.\nOf the 455 edible creations, 75 were cakes made by the 36 participating artists and 380 were hand-piped royal icing cookies made by Prachi Dhabal Deb, a Pune-based royal icing and heritage artist. Together they represented all 28 states and eight Union Territories through regional traditions, festivals, architecture, art forms and cultural symbols.\nPrachi Dhabal Deb curated and organised the display. The artists came from cities including Pune, Mumbai, Bengaluru, Jaipur, Hyderabad, Vadodara, Kolkata, Lucknow, Agra, Gurugram and New Delhi.\nPavneet Kaur (IAS), Additional Municipal Commissioner, Pune Municipal Corporation, attended as Chief Guest and said such initiatives help preserve cultural heritage while making it relevant to contemporary audiences.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/kunjirwadi-five-injured-luxury-bus-rams-parked-tempo-traveller.html","h":"Kunjirwadi: Five injured as speeding luxury bus rams parked Tempo Traveller on Pune–Solapur highway","s":"Three transgender persons in a Tempo Traveller were injured and two others suffered minor injuries; Loni Kalbhor police have registered a case against a luxury bus driver.","k":"Kunjirwadi accident","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-17T19:37:58+05:30","g":["Pune","Kunjirwadi","Pune–Solapur highway","Loni Kalbhor police"],"b":"A speeding luxury bus travelling from Hyderabad towards Mumbai rammed a Tempo Traveller parked at the roadside at Kunjirwadi on the Pune–Solapur highway around 4:30 am on Monday, 16 November, injuring five people.\nThe bus hit the Tempo Traveller hard from behind, in front of Hotel Satkar Grand Lodge at Kunjirwadi in Haveli taluka.\nThree transgender persons in the vehicle were injured and two others suffered minor injuries. The injured were taken straight to a private hospital in Kunjirwadi for treatment. The Tempo Traveller was also badly damaged.\nAccording to police, the complainant had brought seven transgender persons from Miraj in his Force Motors Tempo Traveller to a gathering at Vrindavan Mangal Karyalaya in Theur. Having arrived early, he had stopped in front of the lodge to ask about a room, and went in with two of them while the other five stayed in the vehicle.\nThe complainant alleges that the bus driver ignored traffic rules and drove at high speed. Loni Kalbhor police have registered a case against the bus driver under the Motor Vehicles Act and the relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, and are investigating further.","i":"illustration-e40268c14e","a":["Loni Kalbhor"]},{"u":"pune/bhide-bridge-completely-closed-vehicles-until-december-31-pedestrian-bridge.html","h":"Bhide Bridge to be completely closed to vehicles until December 31 for pedestrian bridge","s":"Pune Metro announced the closure of Bhide Bridge to vehicles to ensure public safety, and the road through the Mutha riverbed will stay open.","k":"Bhide Bridge","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T19:15:33+05:30","g":["Bhide Bridge","Mutha River","Pune Metro","Deccan Gymkhana"],"b":"From 6 am on November 19 until December 31, 2026, Bhide Bridge over the Mutha River will be completely closed to vehicles for the construction of a pedestrian bridge above the existing bridge.\nThe pedestrian bridge will connect Deccan Gymkhana Metro Station with the Peth areas. It is expected to make metro access easier for residents of Narayan Peth, Shaniwar Peth and the areas around Laxmi Road, and for students travelling to educational institutions in the area.\nThe road running through the Mutha riverbed will remain open during the closure. Commuters have been advised to use Lakdi Bridge, Balgandharva Bridge or Z Bridge instead.\nPune Metro announced the restriction to ensure public safety during the work, and has appealed to citizens to plan their journeys accordingly. Metro authorities said the pedestrian bridge would be completed as soon as possible and expressed regret over the inconvenience.","i":"illustration-50401ccf64","a":["Deccan Gymkhana","Deccan"]},{"u":"pune/pune-water-cut-returns-19-november-entire-city-supply-shut-every-thursday.html","h":"Pune water cut returns 19 November: entire city's supply shut every Thursday","s":"Pune Municipal Corporation's weekly water cut, first introduced on 15 October and suspended on 5 and 12 November for Diwali, returns from Thursday, 19 November, with the entire city's supply shut every Thursday; residents have been advised to store enough water in advance.","k":"Pune water cut","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T19:04:48+05:30","g":["Pune water cut","PMC","Pune water supply"],"b":"From Thursday, 19 November 2026, the Pune Municipal Corporation will again shut the entire city's water supply every Thursday.\nThe weekly water cut returns after being suspended for two weeks, on 5 and 12 November, because of Diwali. With the festive period over, the civic body has decided to reinstate the schedule.\nThe PMC first introduced the weekly shutdown on 15 October. It cited lower-than-usual water storage and the need to manage available water in view of possibly reduced rainfall in future.\nResidents have been advised to store enough water in advance and use it judiciously.","i":"illustration-dd264f511b","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pcmc-reclaims-60-per-cent-encroached-amenity-plots.html","h":"PCMC reclaims 60% of encroached amenity plots, aims to clear rest within a month","s":"Of PCMC's 60 encroached amenity plots, Moshi has 18, Charholi 13 and Sangvi 10, across around 25 acres in 11 villages.","k":"PCMC amenity plots","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T18:53:24+05:30","g":["PCMC","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Moshi","Encroached plots","Amenity plots"],"b":"Of the 60 amenity plots of the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC), all of which had been encroached on, 60 per cent have been reclaimed, and the corporation aims to clear the rest within a month.\nThe plots cover around 25 acres across 11 villages in the city. Moshi has the most, with 18 encroached plots, followed by Charholi with 13 and Sangvi with 10.\nOn land reserved for gardens, playgrounds, schools, water tanks, crematoriums, bus stations, community halls, parking and dispensaries, unauthorised sheds, permanent structures and commercial units had come up.\nMunicipal Commissioner Vijay Suryawanshi said the remaining plots will be reclaimed within a month, after which bamboo trees will be planted on the land.\nHe warned encroachers on the remaining plots to remove their illegal structures on their own; otherwise, the corporation will demolish the structures and file FIRs against them.\nLand mafias and political leaders have allegedly taken over the plots, and the encroachments allegedly enjoy the patronage of a local MLA, a former standing committee chairman, sitting corporators and some influential residents. Hotels, garages, shops and other commercial establishments have been set up on the plots, and their operators are said to be collecting rents running into lakhs of rupees every month.\nThe PCMC's Land and Estate Department prepared the list of encroached plots, following which the drive was started.","i":"illustration-22ef719acd","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/nine-more-sinhgad-institutions-temporary-govt-control-bombay-high-court.html","h":"Nine more Sinhgad institutions under temporary govt control after Bombay High Court directive","s":"Nine more Sinhgad Technical Education Society institutions will have administrators till May 9, 2027, or earlier if students are accommodated in nearby schools.","k":"Sinhgad institutions","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T18:41:54+05:30","g":["Sinhgad Technical Education Society","STES","Bombay High Court","Pune"],"b":"In an order issued on November 13, the state education department has appointed administrators to nine more institutions run by the Sinhgad Technical Education Society (STES), after a Bombay High Court directive.\nThe administrators will continue till May 9, 2027, or till the students are accommodated in nearby schools, whichever is earlier. They have been appointed to ensure that students' education is not affected by the institution's administrative and financial crisis.\nThe order was issued by Mahesh Palkar, director of education (secondary and higher secondary), under section 3(1) of the Maharashtra Educational Institutions (Management) Act, 1976.\n“It is necessary to appoint administrators to ensure the proper functioning of the schools, prevent any academic loss to students, and facilitate their adjustment in nearby schools before the commencement of the next academic year,”\nthe order states\nThe nine institutions are Sinhgad Spring Dale School, Ambegaon; Sinhgad Springdale Public School, Vadgaon; Sinhgad City School, Kondhwa; Sinhgad College of Arts, Commerce and Science at Narhe, Ambegaon and Kondhwa; Sinhgad Public School, Kusgaon, Lonavla; RMD Springdale Secondary School, Warje; and Springdale Secondary School, Karvenagar-Erandwane.\nEarlier, the Pune divisional deputy director of education had ordered withdrawal of recognition of the nine institutions from May 1, 2027. The Bombay High Court's November 10 order vacated the interim protection granted against the department's action and directed it to either take over the institutions or accommodate the students in other schools.\nThe latest order is part of a series of interventions against the Sinhgad group amid complaints of unpaid teachers' salaries, non-compliance with court directions and disruption of academic activities. The higher education department had earlier taken over the management of seven colleges run by the trust for three years, while administrators were also directed to take charge of 25 technical institutions.","i":"illustration-4bfbb0acb7","a":[]},{"u":"pune/supriya-sule-slams-pmc-over-undri-rmc-plants.html","h":"Supriya Sule slams PMC over Undri RMC plants: “Stop playing with citizens’ health”","s":"Supriya Sule, an NCP (Sharadchandra Pawar) MP, alleges that dust from Ready-Mix Concrete plants in Undri has severely affected local air quality, and wants the plants shut for good.","k":"Undri RMC plants","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T18:03:34+05:30","g":["Supriya Sule","Undri","RMC plants","PMC","Pune"],"b":"NCP (Sharadchandra Pawar) MP Supriya Sule has slammed the Pune Municipal Corporation over alleged violations by Ready-Mix Concrete (RMC) plants in Undri: “Stop playing with citizens’ health”. She demanded that the plants be permanently shut down.\nShe questioned the corporation’s inaction despite the municipal commissioner’s personal inspection of the area. Sule alleged that dust from the plants has severely affected local air quality, exposing residents to respiratory health risks.\nShe also said plant operators had allegedly dumped cement into a stormwater drain and blocked it. She said the drain remains blocked despite the issue being brought to the commissioner’s attention, causing waterlogging on the road and dangerous conditions, particularly for two-wheeler riders.\nSule pointed to the lack of action despite months of follow-up. She has urged the PMC commissioner and the Maharashtra Pollution Control Board (MPCB) to permanently shut down the RMC plants posing risks to public health, and has also demanded immediate restoration of the blocked drain and a survey, demarcation, deepening and cleaning of the nearby lake.","i":"","a":["Undri"]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-removes-just-78-illegal-hoardings-in-seven-months.html","h":"Pune: PMC removes just 78 illegal hoardings in seven months, seven ward offices remove none","s":"Seven of the Pune Municipal Corporation's 15 ward offices removed no unauthorised hoardings, and the Nagar Road ward office removed the most, 22 illegal hoardings.","k":"Illegal hoardings","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T17:52:37+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Illegal hoardings","Pune Municipal Corporation"],"b":"Between April 1 and November 4, 2026, the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) removed just 78 illegal hoardings across Pune, and seven of its 15 ward offices removed none, in figures from its sky-sign and licensing department.\nThe seven ward offices that did not remove a single unauthorised hoarding in that time are Shivajinagar-Ghole Road, Kothrud-Bavdhan, Dhankawadi-Katraj-Ambegaon, Sinhagad Road, Warje-Karvenagar, Vishrambaugwada and Kasba-Bhawani Peth.\nThe Nagar Road ward office took the most action, removing 22 illegal hoardings. Dhole Patil and Kondhwa-Undri removed five each, Aundh-Baner three and Bibwewadi one.\nIn the same seven months, the civic body removed 15,464 banners, 5,853 posters, 3,323 flags, 3,284 kiosks and 192 flex boards.\nThe PMC requires every hoarding to have permission, display an authorised licence number and the advertising agency's name, and renew its licence every year. Several hoardings are allegedly being put up in violation of these rules.","i":"illustration-e752e07848","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-fortuner-stolen-from-koregaon-bhima-found-in-visakhapatnam.html","h":"Fortuner stolen from Koregaon Bhima found in Visakhapatnam after 13 months","s":"A Fortuner stolen in just four and a half minutes has been driven back to Shikrapur police station, across four states.","k":"Koregaon Bhima","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T17:42:03+05:30","g":["Pune","Koregaon Bhima","Shikrapur","Visakhapatnam","Fortuner"],"b":"A Fortuner parked outside its owner's office on the night of 16 October 2025 and stolen from Koregaon Bhima 13 months ago has been found in Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh.\nThe SUV belongs to a former sarpanch of Koregaon Bhima in Shirur taluka. It was stolen in just four and a half minutes in the early hours. The investigation found that it was being used with a fake number plate copied from another vehicle of a prominent leader.\nShikrapur police had registered a case against unknown thieves on the owner's complaint. One suspect was detained during the investigation, but the car could not be traced.\nPolice in Visakhapatnam noticed the fake plate while checking a suspicious car and traced the original owner through its chassis number. Shown the car over a video call, he confirmed it was his from a torn seat cover inside.\nOn the instructions of Inspector Chandrashekhar Yadav of Shikrapur police station, the owner and police head constables Vishwambhar Waghmare and Ajit Ingawale flew to Visakhapatnam and completed the legal process in five days. They drove the car back to Shikrapur police station in 26 hours straight, across four states.","i":"illustration-1e444a9017","a":["Koregaon Bhima","Bhima Koregaon","Shikrapur"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-took-dhayari-land-original-owners-still-billed-property-tax.html","h":"PMC took Dhayari land and paid in TDR, but original owners still billed property tax","s":"Credence Realtors transferred 1,052.65 sq m of a 1,300 sq m Dhayari plot permanently to the Pune Municipal Corporation and TDR was granted, yet the original owners were sent a bill for ₹7,05,694.","k":"Dhayari","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T17:31:29+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Property tax","Dhayari","TDR"],"b":"Original owners are still being billed property tax on land the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) took over and paid for in TDR, with bills for four years of tax arrears being sent even after the land was developed.\nThe PMC takes over citizens' land for development plan reservations and road widening, and pays for it in TDR, but has left the property tax records in the original owners' names. The bills expose a lack of coordination between the PMC's land acquisition, construction and property tax departments.\nIn Dhayari, 1,052.65 sq m of a 1,300 sq m plot belonging to Credence Realtors was earmarked for a 30-metre DP road and the OM-41 reservation. Credence Realtors transferred it permanently to the PMC by a registered deed on 19 October 2022. The PMC's name went on the 7/12 extract, and TDR was granted under DRC no. 006055.\nOn 13 July 2023 the owners applied to the Sinhagad Road ward office to have the tax charged only on the remaining 247.35 sq m. No action followed, nor after written complaints to the Municipal Commissioner on 20 February and 19 May 2025. Instead, the original owners were sent a bill for ₹7,05,694.\nTwice, after a site inspection and document checks, proposals to cut the tax were prepared and signed by senior officials, but the file then went missing. There is a demand for an inquiry into whether such files are lost or made to disappear, and for action.","i":"illustration-c3583b648a","a":["Dhayari","Dhayri","Dhayarigaon"]},{"u":"pune/pmc-commissioner-joint-crackdown-police-fc-road-hawkers.html","h":"PMC Commissioner announces joint crackdown with police on FC Road hawkers","s":"PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram rejected allegations of extortion (hafta) and political pressure, and assured uniform action against encroachments across Pune.","k":"FC Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T17:20:51+05:30","g":["FC Road","PMC","Pune Police","Encroachments","Hawkers"],"b":"PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram said PMC and Pune Police will launch a joint, end-to-end crackdown on encroachments on Fergusson College (FC) Road, after discussions with the Police Commissioner.\nThe announcement followed protests by ruling corporators over rampant encroachments on the road.\nHe said FC Road is a strict ‘No-Hawkers Zone’ where footpaths must remain free for pedestrians. He also said PMC’s encroachment department alone lacks adequate manpower to stop hawkers returning the next day, making joint police-civic profiling of every stall operator essential.\nHe rejected allegations of extortion (hafta) and political pressure. He said the entire city matters equally to him beyond VIP areas like FC Road, and assured uniform anti-encroachment action across Pune.\nA local corporator from Ward 12 displayed photographs and copies of past FIRs filed against repeat offenders. The corporator said encroachers often return within half an hour of routine drives, and urged the administration to deliver permanent results rather than “video-only” token action.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-airport-fastags-likely-to-be-made-mandatory-for-vehicles-entering-premises.html","h":"FASTags likely to be made mandatory for vehicles entering Pune airport premises","s":"Under a proposed arrangement, vehicles entering Pune airport premises that exceed a 15-minute limit will be charged a ₹500 penalty deducted from the owner's FASTag account, with enforcement scheduled from the first week of December.","k":"Pune airport","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T17:10:20+05:30","g":["FASTag","Pune airport"],"b":"AeroMall, which manages traffic at Pune airport, said on Monday that FASTags are likely to be made mandatory for vehicles entering the premises.\nThe move is aimed at further reducing congestion on the airside and eliminating delays at the exit gates. The rule on time-bound entry and exit is scheduled to be strictly enforced from the first week of December.\nUnder the proposed arrangement, a vehicle that exceeds the 15-minute limit will be charged a ₹500 penalty. The amount will be deducted automatically from the owner's FASTag account, so motorists need not stop at the exit gate to pay in cash or digitally.\nY S Rajput, vice president of AeroMall, said vehicle owners would be informed before the penalty is deducted. Rajput said the cashier at the exit gate would tell the owner about the violation, the gate would open and the penalty would be deducted from the FASTag account.\nA motorist who believes a penalty was wrongly imposed can contest it through AeroMall's helpline, 9226089640, its WhatsApp number, or by email at complaint@aeromallpune.com. If an investigation finds the penalty was wrongly imposed, the amount will be refunded.\nAn awareness campaign is under way and no penalties are being imposed yet. Two electronic display boards that will flash images of vehicles overstaying the permitted time have been installed and are undergoing trial runs.\nSeparately, Bharat Taxi, launched in Pune by Union home minister Amit Shah on Sunday, has informed that it is preparing to set up a permanent kiosk on AeroMall's first floor by the end of November.","i":"illustration-0db8d77a54","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-way-cleared-500-traffic-wardens-pmc-commissioner-lifts-stay.html","h":"Pune: Way cleared for 500 traffic wardens as PMC commissioner lifts stay","s":"An inquiry into complaints about the appointment of 500 traffic wardens in Pune found no solid evidence of malpractice, and the appointment process will now resume.","k":"PMC traffic wardens","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T16:59:44+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Traffic wardens","Naval Kishore Ram"],"b":"PMC Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram has lifted the stay on the appointment of 500 traffic wardens in Pune, and the way is cleared for them.\nThe commissioner had stayed the work on 1 October and ordered an inquiry after complaints of irregularities in the appointment process. Deputy Commissioner (Vigilance) Prasad Katkar and Deputy Commissioner (Security) Tushar Babar examined the contractor's eligibility, documents and financial transactions.\nThe inquiry report found no solid evidence of malpractice. The commissioner then held a hearing and lifted the stay.\nThe standing committee had approved a proposal to spend about Rs 17 crore over a year on the wardens. The work was given to a firm without a tender process.\nThe PMC health department had earlier blacklisted the firm over major lapses in supplying it manpower. The firm was later taken off the blacklist, which had raised questions over the appointments.\nBefore the stay, 225 wardens had been recruited, and 120 of them were on duty during Ganeshotsav.\nThe appointment process will now resume, with wardens provided where the traffic police ask for them. Their attendance is planned to be monitored online.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pimpri-chinchwad-cyber-police-bust-alleged-dubai-based-racket-12000-sim-cards.html","h":"Pimpri-Chinchwad Cyber Police bust alleged Dubai-based racket over 12,000 SIM cards, seven arrested","s":"A 26-year-old resident of Nigdi Pradhikaran is among seven arrested over an alleged SIM card supply network, and police have registered a case under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.","k":"Cyber Police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T16:49:08+05:30","g":["Pimpri-Chinchwad","Cyber fraud","SIM cards","Cyber Police"],"b":"Pimpri-Chinchwad Cyber Police have arrested seven people over an interstate network, with links to Dubai and Chinese nationals, that allegedly supplied up to 12,000 SIM cards to Dubai fraudsters.\nBetween 10,000 and 12,000 SIM cards were allegedly procured and supplied for cybercrime operations. The police registered a case, CR No. 42/2026, under Sections 318(4), 317(2), 61(2) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.\nPolice identified a 26-year-old resident of Nigdi Pradhikaran as the main accused, who allegedly ran the network from Dubai with Chinese nationals. After a Look Out Circular and Interpol coordination, Assistant Police Inspector Pravin Swami and his team apprehended him at Mumbai airport. His passport shows he allegedly travelled to Dubai 25 to 30 times.\nAlso arrested are a bank account holder from Chikhali and his associate from Akurdi, two alleged SIM card suppliers in Mumbai, and two men who allegedly procured SIM cards from suppliers and routed them to the main accused in Dubai.\nPolice say the SIM cards were obtained in the names of genuine customers visiting outlets for new connections, who were told their OTP had expired, the server was unavailable or the SIM card had not been activated. The cards were then allegedly handed over to associates for money, and used for cyber fraud calls, fake applications, linking bank accounts and email IDs under false names.\nPolice are now examining the data linked to the SIM cards to establish how many cyber fraud cases they were used in and whether others were involved. Further investigation is underway, said Rohidas Pawar, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Crime), Pimpri-Chinchwad.","i":"","a":["Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/supriya-sule-await-ajit-pawar-crash-probe.html","h":"Supriya Sule: ‘Maharashtra deserves the truth’, await Ajit Pawar crash probe","s":"NCP (SP) MP Supriya Sule has appealed for sensitivity from political parties and the media over a plane crash that killed former Deputy CM Ajit Pawar.","k":"Supriya Sule","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T16:37:55+05:30","g":["Supriya Sule","Ajit Pawar","Plane crash","Baramati"],"b":"Speaking in Pune on Tuesday, NCP (SP) MP Supriya Sule said the Maharashtra Government must address the questions and doubts surrounding the plane crash that killed former Deputy CM Ajit Pawar, and urged people to await the probe.\nShe said Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis had demanded a transparent and time-bound inquiry before Union Home Minister Amit Shah, and that the truth must come out before the people of Maharashtra.\n“Therefore, let us wait for the report,” she said.\nOn Rohit Pawar’s presentation and allegations about the crash, Sule said she had not watched his entire press conference as she had been in Delhi. She said she would speak to him to understand the details, including his demand for an FIR and an investigation into the role of the aircraft operator.\nShe said civil aviation is a Central subject and the competent authorities should take an appropriate decision.\n“The person who died in this accident was the man who held our family together. My elder brother is gone,” she said, appealing to political parties and the media to approach the matter with sensitivity.\nSule also met the Pune District Collector over drought, water availability and traffic. She said farmers in the Baramati Lok Sabha constituency who have not received the ₹5,000 assistance should visit the Collector’s office and register their names.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/bhor-police-patil-found-dead-suspected-sharp-weapon-attack.html","h":"Ghorepadal-Sangvi Budruk: Bhor police patil found dead in suspected sharp-weapon attack","s":"Who attacked a village police patil in Bhor taluka, and why, is not yet known, and Rajgad Police are examining a possible land dispute among other angles.","k":"Bhor taluka","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T16:27:11+05:30","g":["Bhor","Police patil","Rajgad Police","Pune"],"b":"A suspected sharp-weapon attack at Ghorepadal-Sangvi Budruk in Bhor taluka, Pune district, on Monday evening, November 16, left a village police patil dead.\nHe was found lying injured in a field at around 5.30 pm with severe head injuries, said to have been caused by a sharp-edged weapon resembling a sickle. He had also suffered major blood loss.\nRelatives and villagers took him to a nearby private hospital, and doctors there declared him dead after examining him.\nRajgad Police reached the spot soon after receiving information, inspected it and sent the body for a post-mortem examination.\nWho attacked him, and why, is not yet known. A possible land dispute is among the angles being examined, though the motive has not been confirmed. Police are also looking into an earlier personal dispute or other reasons.","i":"illustration-34c47d17b7","a":["Bhor","Bhor taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-pmc-acts-against-encroachments-on-fc-road.html","h":"PMC acts against encroachments on Pune’s FC Road","s":"The Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) carried out the action against encroachments on FC Road, Pune, on 17 November.","k":"FC Road","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T16:14:58+05:30","g":["Pune","FC Road","PMC","Encroachments"],"b":"On 17 November, PMC took action against encroachments on Pune's FC Road.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/ms-dhoni-retires-as-ipl-player-will-mentor-csk-from-2027.html","h":"MS Dhoni retires as IPL player, will mentor CSK from 2027","s":"MS Dhoni, Chennai Super Kings’ most-capped cricketer with 272 appearances, ends his IPL playing career and will be Team Mentor from IPL 2027.","k":"IPL retirement","c":"City","t":"2026-11-17T16:04:24+05:30","g":["MS Dhoni","CSK","Chennai Super Kings","IPL"],"b":"Mahendra Singh Dhoni, the former Chennai Super Kings captain, has announced his retirement from the Indian Premier League as a player ahead of the 2027 season and will be the franchise’s Team Mentor.\nChennai Super Kings confirmed that the wicketkeeper-batter will begin a new chapter with the franchise as Team Mentor from IPL 2027.\nDhoni ends his IPL playing career as CSK’s most-capped cricketer, with 272 appearances, and their second-highest run-scorer, with 5,314 runs.\nUnder his captaincy, CSK won five IPL titles (2010, 2011, 2018, 2021 and 2023), the joint-most by any captain, and a record two Champions League T20 trophies.\nCSK co-owner N. Srinivasan paid tribute to Dhoni’s nearly two-decade association with the team. Srinivasan said Chennai will always remain Dhoni’s home.\n“There is no CSK without MS Dhoni. In 2008, I insisted that Dhoni should be part of CSK... It turns out that’s the best decision I took.”\nCSK co-owner N. Srinivasan","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/three-new-cars-allegedly-driven-dangerously-near-wakad-biker-narrow-escape.html","h":"Three new cars allegedly driven dangerously on highway near Wakad; biker has a narrow escape","s":"Citizens have demanded strict action against those driving three new cars that a viral video shows speeding alongside each other at extremely close distances.","k":"Wakad","c":"City","t":"2026-11-17T15:43:13+05:30","g":["Wakad","Mumbai-Bengaluru Highway","Katraj-Dehu Road bypass","Pune"],"b":"A viral video on social media shows a biker's narrow escape between three new cars that were allegedly driven dangerously during a photoshoot on the Mumbai-Bengaluru Highway near Wakad.\nThe incident took place on the Katraj-Dehu Road bypass near Wakad, where the cars were allegedly involved in risky driving manoeuvres.\nThe video shows the three cars speeding alongside each other at extremely close distances, while a biker on a two-wheeler narrowly makes his way through a dangerously narrow gap between them.\nThe incident could have caused a serious accident and put other commuters at risk. Citizens have expressed outrage and demanded strict action against the car drivers.","i":"","a":["Wakad","Vakad"]},{"u":"pune/moshi-woman-9-month-old-baby-missing-kidnapping-case-registered.html","h":"Moshi woman and 9-month-old baby missing; kidnapping case registered on husband's complaint","s":"Anyone who knows where the missing Moshi woman or her baby may be can contact MIDC Bhosari Police Station, which has registered a kidnapping case.","k":"Moshi","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T15:32:14+05:30","g":["Moshi","Missing woman","MIDC Bhosari","Kidnapping case"],"b":"MIDC Bhosari Police Station has registered a kidnapping case over a 27-year-old woman and her 9-month-old baby, who have been missing from Moshi since 15 November.\nThe case is against an unknown person under Section 140(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, on the husband's complaint. Police Sub-Inspector R. B. Pansare is investigating.\nOn the day she went missing, the couple had a minor argument and the husband left the house in anger. He returned around 5:30 pm to find neither his wife nor the baby at home.\nThe woman's mother and grandmother, who were in the house at the time, said she had left with the baby. The family searched among relatives and in the neighbourhood but found no trace of either of them. Her mobile phone is also missing.\nThe husband suspects that an unknown person may have lured her away.\nThe woman is about 5 feet 2 inches tall, of medium build and fair complexion, with long hair and black eyes. She was last seen wearing a dark red dress and a mangalsutra with a small gold-coloured pendant.\nAnyone with information about the woman or the child can contact MIDC Bhosari Police Station.","i":"illustration-00c082373e","a":["Moshi"]},{"u":"pune/lonavala-police-sub-inspector-allegedly-caught-accepting-20000-bribe-acb-trap.html","h":"Lonavala police sub-inspector allegedly caught accepting ₹20,000 bribe in ACB trap","s":"A police sub-inspector attached to Lonavala Rural Police Station allegedly accepted ₹1.30 lakh from a complainant on several earlier occasions to dilute the charges and help the complainant’s brother secure bail, and demanded a further ₹30,000.","k":"Lonavala ACB trap","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T15:21:35+05:30","g":["Lonavala","Anti-Corruption Bureau","ACB trap","Mapro Garden"],"b":"On Monday, 16 November, a Pune Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) trap at a food court near Mapro Garden in Lonavala allegedly caught Police Sub-Inspector Natha Ramkishan Kekan, 38, accepting a ₹20,000 bribe in the presence of independent witnesses.\nKekan, attached to Lonavala Rural Police Station, was investigating a case registered at that station against the complainant’s brother under Sections 109(2), 352 and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS). On several earlier occasions, he had allegedly accepted ₹1.30 lakh from the complainant to dilute the charges and help the brother secure bail.\nKekan allegedly demanded a further ₹30,000 on 14 November to help the brother in chapter proceedings, assist during the rest of the investigation and ensure the chargesheet was filed early. Unwilling to pay more, the complainant approached the Pune ACB on 16 November.\nDuring a verification, Kekan allegedly acknowledged having received money earlier, then demanded ₹20,000 and agreed to accept it.\nThe details are as stated by the Pune Anti-Corruption Bureau.","i":"illustration-4c29cb6f5f","a":["Lonavala","Lonavla"]},{"u":"pune/pune-ghod-dam-major-action-sand-mafia-17-boats-destroyed-gelatin-blasts.html","h":"Ghod Dam: major action on sand mafia, 17 boats destroyed in gelatin blasts","s":"A preliminary estimate puts the machinery of sand thieves destroyed in the Ghod Dam blasts at about ₹1.5 crore; Shirur Tehsildar Balasaheb Mhaske and Shrigonda Tehsildar Sachin Dongre led the action.","k":"Ghod Dam","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T15:10:51+05:30","g":["Ghod Dam","Shirur","Shrigonda","sand mafia","Pune"],"b":"The revenue department blew up 17 boats of sand mafia in gelatin blasts in Ghod Dam. Revenue teams from Shirur and Shrigonda talukas entered the dam in an automated boat at around 10 am on Monday, 16 November.\nThe boats were 8 mechanical boats and 9 fibre boats of sand mafia who were stealing sand with mechanical boats in the backwaters of Ghod Dam at Chinchani. Ghod Dam at Chinchani is a lifeline for Shirur and Shrigonda talukas.\nSensing the action, the sand thieves tried to hide their mechanical boats within the limits of Chinchani-Gunat village, but the administration chased them and blew up all the boats with gelatin.\nShirur Tehsildar Balasaheb Mhaske and Shrigonda Tehsildar Sachin Dongre led the action. Nimone Circle Officer Nandkumar Kharat and Circle Officer Rajendra Dhage of the Shrigonda revenue team took part along with village revenue officers.\nA preliminary estimate puts the sand thieves' machinery destroyed at about ₹1.5 crore.","i":"","a":["Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-slips-out-top-10-cleanest-cities-swachh-survekshan-pimpri-chinchwad.html","h":"Pune slips out of top 10 cleanest cities in Swachh Survekshan; Pimpri-Chinchwad stays No. 1 in Maharashtra","s":"In Swachh Survekshan 2025–26, Pune ranked 12th among cities with a population of over 10 lakh, down from eighth in 2024–25 and sixth in the survey before that.","k":"Swachh Survekshan","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T15:00:10+05:30","g":["Swachh Survekshan","Pune","Pimpri-Chinchwad","PMC","PCMC"],"b":"Pune has slipped out of the top 10 cleanest cities in Swachh Survekshan 2025–26, ranking 12th nationally among cities with a population of over 10 lakh, and Pimpri-Chinchwad has stayed No. 1 in Maharashtra.\nThe Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) ranking is down from eighth place in 2024–25 and sixth in the survey before that. Among cities with a population of over one lakh, Pune ranked 27th.\nPune stood 18th among 50 cities in the clean air survey, despite receiving ₹281 crore for pollution control.\nThe Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation (PCMC) has kept its first position in Maharashtra among cities with a population of over 10 lakh. In New Delhi, it received the award from President Droupadi Murmu, recognising the efforts of sanitation workers, civic planning and citizen participation.","i":"illustration-3478d2f24c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-shirur-police-constable-arrested-after-allegedly-fleeing-with-95000-bribe.html","h":"Shirur police constable arrested after allegedly fleeing with ₹95,000 bribe, case documents","s":"A 45-year-old police constable posted at Shirur Police Station, who allegedly took a ₹95,000 bribe from a complainant, was remanded to police custody until 20 November by the Special Court (Additional Sessions Judge) in Shirur.","k":"Shirur","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T14:49:16+05:30","g":["Shirur","Anti-Corruption Bureau","ACB","Bribe"],"b":"A 45-year-old police constable posted at Shirur Police Station, who allegedly fled with a ₹95,000 bribe and case documents, was arrested on 16 November by the Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB), Pune.\nHe allegedly took a bribe from a complainant in exchange for helping him in a criminal case registered at Shirur Police Station and ensuring that he was not arrested. He had allegedly first demanded ₹1 lakh.\nDuring a verification operation on 30 September, the ACB established that he called the complainant to the Takali Haji Police Outpost and demanded ₹1 lakh in the presence of an independent witness. The amount was negotiated down to ₹95,000.\nDuring the trap that followed, he allegedly accepted ₹95,000 from the complainant in the presence of witnesses. After sensing the ACB team, he fled the spot with the bribe money and the documents of the criminal case registered against the complainant.\nA case was registered against him at Shirur Police Station under Section 7 of the Prevention of Corruption Act and Section 238 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS). After remaining at large, he was arrested at around 11.25 am at the Shirur Municipal Council premises, in an operation led by Police Inspector Suhas Hattekar of the ACB, Pune.\nThe Special Court (Additional Sessions Judge) in Shirur remanded him to police custody until 20 November. Further investigation is under way.","i":"illustration-95f1c57700","a":["Shirur","Shirur taluka","Shirur town","Ghodnadi"]},{"u":"pune/rohit-pawar-seeks-cbi-probe-ajit-pawar-crash-fadnavis-vsr-owner.html","h":"Ajit Pawar crash: Rohit Pawar seeks CBI probe, questions Fadnavis’s links with VSR owner","s":"NCP (Sharadchandra Pawar) MLA Rohit Pawar alleged that a picture he said was taken in Jaipur on November 21, 2024 shows close personal and social ties between Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis and the owners of VSR Ventures.","k":"Ajit Pawar crash","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T14:38:33+05:30","g":["Rohit Pawar","Ajit Pawar","CBI probe","VSR Ventures","Baramati"],"b":"NCP (Sharadchandra Pawar) MLA Rohit Pawar on Monday demanded a Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) inquiry into the January 28 crash near the Baramati airstrip that killed former Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar and four others.\nHe also questioned Chief Minister (CM) Devendra Fadnavis’s ties with VK Singh, owner of VSR Ventures, the company that operated the Learjet 45 that crashed.\nAddressing a press conference, Pawar displayed a picture of Fadnavis. The picture, he said, was taken in Jaipur on November 21, 2024, during the wedding celebrations of VK Singh’s son. He alleged that it showed close personal and social ties between the Chief Minister and the company’s owners.\n“I am not saying that the Chief Minister is involved with the accident. But VK Singh is certainly involved in this,” Pawar said.\nPawar said no First Information Report (FIR) had been registered in the case. He alleged that the state government had paid about Rs 168.92 crore to the company for its services since the accident. He appealed to Deputy Chief Minister Sunetra Pawar and her sons, Parth and Jay, to press for a CBI investigation.\nState BJP Chief Spokesperson Navnath Ban dismissed the allegations as low-level politics and a bid for publicity. He said VSR has provided services to political parties and state governments since 2013 and that several leaders have travelled in its aircraft.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-rickshaw-cab-operators-strike-23-november.html","h":"Maharashtra rickshaw, cab operators to strike on 23 November","s":"Dr Baba Kamble, president of the Maharashtra Transport Federation, chaired the Alandi meeting at which rickshaw and taxi unions decided on a statewide strike.","k":"Maharashtra strike","c":"City","t":"2026-11-17T14:27:21+05:30","g":["Pune","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Maharashtra","Rickshaw strike","Bike taxi"],"b":"Rickshaw and cab operators across Maharashtra will hold a one-day strike on 23 November, with major cities including Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad taking part.\nThe strike is to protest pending demands and the alleged illegal operation of bike taxis. The unions are demanding action against app-based bike taxi companies operating without proper authorisation, and renewal of permits.\nOperators have also raised concerns over unfair competition, inadequate enforcement and the impact on traditional transport services.\nThe strike was decided at a joint meeting of rickshaw and taxi unions in Alandi, chaired by Dr Baba Kamble, president of the Maharashtra Transport Federation.","i":"illustration-04faee5b95","a":["Alandi","Alandi Devachi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-burst-pipeline-near-talab-masjid-wastes-thousands-of-litres.html","h":"Burst pipeline near Talab Masjid wastes thousands of litres of drinking water","s":"Residents of Capricorn Green Park say the main drinking water pipeline in their locality has been leaking for several days and the road in the area has been in a pathetic condition for two years.","k":"Talab Masjid","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T14:15:20+05:30","g":["Talab Masjid","Capricorn Green Park","PMC","Drinking water"],"b":"Thousands of litres of potable water are flowing onto the road every day from a leaking main drinking water pipeline near Talab Masjid in Pune, residents of Capricorn Green Park say.\nThe residents are from Capricorn Green Park, behind the HP petrol pump near Talab Masjid. They say the main drinking water pipeline in their locality has been leaking for the past several days.\nThey also say the road in the area has remained in a pathetic condition for the past two years, and that repeated complaints seeking repairs have been ignored.\nAngry at the waste of clean water while the city grapples with water shortages, the residents have urged the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) to repair both the damaged pipeline and the road immediately.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/kamla-nehru-hospital-stretcher-allegedly-used-for-construction-debris.html","h":"Kamla Nehru Hospital stretcher allegedly used for construction debris; PMC fines contractor ₹25,000","s":"Contractor Tejdarshan Infra Pvt Ltd, appointed to renovate and modernise Kamla Nehru Hospital, has paid a ₹25,000 penalty over the alleged use of a patient stretcher to carry construction debris, and the civic administration has warned of stricter action should such violations recur.","k":"Kamla Nehru Hospital","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T14:04:21+05:30","g":["Pune","PMC","Kamla Nehru Hospital","Tejdarshan Infra"],"b":"Contractor Tejdarshan Infra Pvt Ltd has been fined ₹25,000 by the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) after a patient stretcher at Kamla Nehru Hospital was allegedly used to transport construction debris.\nThe stretcher was meant for shifting patients between hospital departments. The matter came to light after it was found being used to carry construction waste.\nTejdarshan Infra has been appointed to renovate and modernise the hospital. The hospital is attached to the civic body's Bharatratna Atal Bihari Vajpayee Medical College.\nThe PMC's building department initiated penal action against the contractor. Building department head Bipin Shinde confirmed the action and said the administration had warned the contractor against repeating such practices.\nThe civic administration has warned of stricter action if such violations recur. The contractor has paid the penalty.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/man-allegedly-attacks-two-wheeler-rider-machete-chikhali-cctv.html","h":"Man allegedly attacks two-wheeler rider with machete near Sane Chowk in Chikhali, caught on CCTV","s":"A two-wheeler rider attacked with a machete near Sane Chowk in Chikhali escaped with his life; the rider has not yet filed a formal complaint at Chikhali Police Station, and Chikhali Police have launched an investigation.","k":"Chikhali","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T13:53:41+05:30","g":["Chikhali","Machete attack","CCTV","Chikhali Police","Sane Chowk"],"b":"A two-wheeler rider escaped with his life after a local goon allegedly attacked him with a machete around 9 pm on Monday near Sane Chowk in Chikhali, Pimpri-Chinchwad.\nThe rider was passing through the area. The entire incident was caught on CCTV cameras.\nThe victim has not yet filed a formal complaint at Chikhali Police Station. Chikhali Police have taken cognisance of the incident, launched an investigation and begun efforts to identify and trace the accused.","i":"","a":["Chikhali","Chikhli"]},{"u":"pune/pune-fc-road-encroachments-bjp-corporators-protest-own-administration.html","h":"FC Road encroachments: BJP corporators protest against their own administration at PMC general body meeting","s":"Ganesh Bidkar, Leader of the House, repeatedly tried to pacify BJP corporators who refused to back down in a protest against their own administration.","k":"FC Road","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-17T13:42:43+05:30","g":["FC Road","BJP","PMC","Encroachments"],"b":"Corporators of the ruling BJP, including Ravindra Salegaonkar, protested with placards against their own administration over encroachments on FC Road at the Pune Municipal Corporation's general body meeting.\nThey alleged that entire footpaths and half the road on FC Road have been encroached upon, leaving no space for pedestrians. They accused the administration of taking only token action on Mondays while ignoring violations on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays.\nSalegaonkar had also alleged earlier this week that enforcement squads were collecting hafta from street vendors. Fellow BJP corporator Nivedita Ekbote said the allegation needs serious examination and promised strict action against illegal occupations.\nThere was high tension at the meeting. Leader of the House Ganesh Bidkar repeatedly tried to pacify the protesting corporators, who refused to back down.\nCongress leaders Arvind Shinde and Prashant Jagtap sarcastically congratulated the BJP corporators for questioning their own administration, taking a jibe at the ruling party.\nThe commotion briefly paused when the Mayor returned to the chair, but the heated debate over the administration's alleged inaction continued.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/baner-police-arrest-21-year-old-allegedly-posing-as-ias-officer.html","h":"Baner police arrest 21-year-old for allegedly posing as IAS officer, cheating housing society of Rs 35 lakh","s":"Police estimate that members of a Pune housing society lost around Rs 35 lakh, and a complaint alleges a 21-year-old used forged signatures to start online banking on the society’s account.","k":"Baner","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-17T13:31:37+05:30","g":["Baner","Pune","Housing society","IAS officer","Baner police"],"b":"A 21-year-old who lives near Balewadi High Street in Baner has been arrested by Baner police for allegedly posing as an IAS officer to cheat a Pune housing society of about Rs 35 lakh. He lives in a co-operative housing society.\nPolice say telling residents he had cleared the UPSC exam and become an IAS officer helped him win their trust.\nAccording to the complaint, he promised residents he would sell the society’s unsold flats through a lottery. Several people allegedly paid him money believing the offer was genuine. He was serving as the society’s chairman at the time.\nThe complaint alleges that, without the members’ knowledge, he used forged signatures of a society member and the complainant to start an online banking facility on the society’s account. He then allegedly took a loan of Rs 10 lakh against a Rs 37 lakh deposit held in the society’s account.\nHe also allegedly broke the society’s fixed deposit and moved the money into his personal account. Police estimate that society members lost around Rs 35 lakh.\nBaner police registered a case on the basis of the complaint. The investigation is still on.","i":"illustration-51622f3095","a":["Baner"]},{"u":"pune/aundh-road-car-crashes-into-divider-major-accident-said-to-be-averted.html","h":"Car crashes into divider on Aundh Road in Pune, major accident said to be averted","s":"The cause of a car’s crash into a road divider on Aundh Road in Pune, and whether anyone was hurt, are yet to be confirmed.","k":"Aundh Road","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-17T13:20:16+05:30","g":["Aundh Road","Pune","Road accident"],"b":"A major accident is said to have been averted on Aundh Road in Pune, where a car crashed into a road divider.\nThe front of the car was damaged in the impact, as video from the spot shows.\nWhether anyone was injured, and what exactly caused the collision, are yet to be confirmed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-35000-court-employees-indefinite-strike-work-may-halt.html","h":"Maharashtra: 35,000 court employees on indefinite strike from 17 November, work may halt","s":"A Group C association of court employees called an indefinite strike after a pay-hike proposal stayed pending for 22 months; earlier protests with black ribbons and then a mass leave brought no settlement.","k":"Court strike","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-17T13:08:06+05:30","g":["Court strike","Maharashtra","Pune District and Sessions Court"],"b":"35,000 court employees across Maharashtra are on an indefinite strike from 17 November, called by the Group C association of the Maharashtra State Judicial Employees Federation, and court work may come to a halt.\nThe president and secretary of the Pune District Judicial Employees Group C Association said employees of the Pune District and Sessions Court will join the strike. They cited short staffing, a rising number of cases, work pressure, and pay that does not match the nature of the work. The employees have resolved to keep the strike going until their demands are met.\nThat Group C association called the strike after a proposal for a pay hike had stayed pending for 22 months. Earlier protests, working with black ribbons and then a mass leave, brought no settlement of the demands.\nLawyers say litigants may bear the brunt. With courts already carrying a large backlog, hearings may be delayed and pending cases may rise further.\nComing just as courts reopen after the long Diwali vacation, the strike may hit the filing of new suits, the registration of applications, obtaining certified copies of orders and carrying out bail orders.\nA lawyer at the District and Sessions Court urged the government to settle the employees' demands at once.","i":"illustration-7a931bb634","a":[]},{"u":"pune/nigdi-scrap-warehouse-fire-alert-residents-prevent-major-disaster.html","h":"Nigdi scrap warehouse fire; alert residents prevent major disaster","s":"Timely alertness by residents helped avert a major disaster in a fire at a scrap warehouse.","k":"Nigdi fire","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-17T12:56:09+05:30","g":["Nigdi","Pimpri-Chinchwad","scrap warehouse","fire"],"b":"Thanks to the timely alertness of residents, a fire at a scrap warehouse in Nigdi, Pimpri-Chinchwad, was brought under control.\nThe fire had caused concern among local residents; their alertness helped prevent a major disaster.","i":"","a":["Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/pune-container-truck-overturns-dive-ghat.html","h":"Container truck overturns at Dive Ghat in Pune","s":"A container truck lay overturned across a road at Dive Ghat, and the exact cause, details of any injuries and the extent of traffic disruption are yet to be confirmed.","k":"Dive Ghat","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-17T11:25:43+05:30","g":["Dive Ghat","Container truck","Pune"],"b":"A container truck overturned at Dive Ghat in Pune at around 1 AM on Tuesday, November 17, and lay across the road.\nOther vehicles were present at the scene. The exact cause of the accident, details of any injuries and the extent of traffic disruption are yet to be confirmed.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-akurdi-zepto-delivery-executive-killed-truck-allegedly-reverses.html","h":"Akurdi: Zepto delivery executive, 28, killed as truck allegedly reverses into motorcycle","s":"Nigdi police are investigating a case against a container truck driver, a 28-year-old native of Aurangabad in Bihar, filed on a complaint by the father of a Zepto delivery executive who died in Akurdi.","k":"Akurdi","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-17T11:13:16+05:30","g":["Pune","Akurdi","Nigdi","Zepto","Bajaj Auto"],"b":"A 28-year-old Zepto delivery executive was killed in Akurdi at around 11:30 pm on Saturday, after a container truck hit his motorcycle on the Nigdi-Pune stretch of the Grade Separator Road, in front of Bajaj Auto.\nThe victim, a resident of Nigdi, was riding from Nigdi towards Pimpri to make Zepto deliveries. Police said the driver allegedly reversed the container truck without checking for traffic behind him, and the motorcycle, coming from behind, crashed into the container.\nHe suffered severe injuries to his head, both hands and both legs, and died at the spot. Police said the driver allegedly fled without stopping to help the injured man or arranging medical assistance.\nOn a complaint filed by the victim's father, Nigdi police have registered a case against the container driver, a 28-year-old native of Aurangabad in Bihar, and are investigating. No arrest has been reported so far.","i":"illustration-7d1ccb2933","a":["Akurdi","Nigdi","Nigdi Pradhikaran","Pradhikaran"]},{"u":"pune/pune-alternate-day-water-supply-likely-delayed-pmc-plans-discussions.html","h":"Pune’s shift to alternate-day water supply after Diwali likely delayed as PMC plans further discussions","s":"Pune’s water quota is 13 TMC, against the 21 TMC that the Pune Municipal Corporation initially demanded for the current year.","k":"Pune water supply","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-17T10:42:04+05:30","g":["Pune water supply","PMC","Khadakwasla dam","Water cuts"],"b":"Pune’s shift to alternate-day water supply after Diwali is likely to be delayed, as the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) plans to seek further discussions with the Irrigation Department over the city’s allocated water quota of 13 TMC.\nThe PMC’s group leaders from all political parties were to meet on November 16 to discuss the proposed cuts, but the meeting was postponed. The matter is expected to be taken up at the next meeting on November 17.\nA decision will be taken after discussions involving the Irrigation Department, PMC officials and representatives of all political parties.\nMayor Manjusha Nagpure said the existing 13 TMC allocation was inadequate and that further water cuts would require detailed discussions with the Irrigation Department and political representatives.\nThe PMC had initially demanded 21 TMC for the current year. The Irrigation Department sanctioned 11.33 TMC and, following objections from citizens, allocated an additional 1.70 TMC, taking the total quota to 13 TMC.\nThe Khadakwasla dam system held 21.74 TMC on November 16, 2026, against 27.78 TMC on the same date in 2025, a deficit of 6.04 TMC.\nThe existing 10% cut continues: the PMC has clarified that water supply will remain suspended across the city every Thursday, and citizens have been advised to plan their water consumption accordingly.","i":"illustration-c8a398b031","a":[]},{"u":"pune/rural-pune-cng-price-hiked-per-kg-101-50.html","h":"Rural Pune CNG price rises ₹1 per kg to ₹101.50","s":"CNG prices in rural Pune are going up ₹1 per kg to ₹101.50, and Torrent has implemented the hike.","k":"Rural Pune CNG","c":"Business","t":"2026-11-16T20:50:12+05:30","g":["Pune","CNG","CNG price","Rural Pune"],"b":"The Petrol Dealers Association, Pune has announced a ₹1 per kg rise in Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) prices in rural Pune, effective from midnight on November 16, that is, 12 am on November 17.\nAfter the revision, the CNG price will be ₹101.50 per kg.\nTorrent has implemented the hike. Its team will visit CNG stations to help put the revised rates in place.","i":"illustration-e5bb928ad3","a":[]},{"u":"pune/maharashtra-bans-school-admission-interviews-tests-screening-donations.html","h":"Maharashtra bans school admission interviews, tests, screening and donations for Nursery, KG and Class I seats","s":"Schools in Maharashtra that violate the Standard Operating Procedure on admissions could face administrative or penal action, and officials are required to send monthly compliance reports.","k":"School admissions","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T20:33:32+05:30","g":["Maharashtra","School admissions","Nursery","Directorate of Primary Education","Maharashtra Navnirman Vidyarthi Sena"],"b":"Maharashtra bans interviews, written or oral admission tests, screening and donations for Nursery, KG and Class I seats, under a four-page Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) that the Directorate of Primary Education issued on November 16.\nThe SOP prohibits interviews of children and parents, written or oral admission tests and any form of screening. Schools cannot demand documents beyond those prescribed by the government. Donations, capitation fees and unauthorised charges are also prohibited.\nThe directive bars discrimination on grounds of caste, religion, language, gender, social or economic background, or parents’ educational qualifications. Where applications exceed available seats, schools must follow a transparent lottery.\nThe rules apply to schools across Maharashtra, including those run by minority communities, irrespective of medium of instruction. Education officials and inspectors are to inspect schools, scrutinise admission records, fee structures and lottery records, and promptly investigate complaints.\nSchools violating the rules may face administrative or penal action. Officials must submit monthly compliance reports.\nThe directive follows a campaign by the Maharashtra Navnirman Vidyarthi Sena (MNVS), which approached Primary Education Director Sharad Gosavi on October 26.\nThe MNVS had flagged schools allegedly demanding parents’ income details, Income Tax Returns and educational certificates, and cited complaints of intermediaries allegedly demanding up to ₹7 lakh for admissions. It has demanded an independent investigation into the alleged network of agents and middlemen.\n“Education is a child’s right. Parents cannot be forced to disclose their financial status or pay lakhs of rupees to secure admission,” said Dhananjay Vijay Dalvi, Pune city president of the MNVS.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-net-set-phd-holders-indefinite-sit-in-vacant-professor-posts.html","h":"Pune: NET-SET, PhD holders on indefinite sit-in over 5,012 vacant assistant professor posts","s":"The NET-SET, PhD Holders Struggle Committee, Maharashtra State, claimed that universities have not prepared the score sheets needed to recruit assistant professors for aided colleges, and alleged that appointing professors on a Clock Hour Basis violates University Grants Commission guidelines.","k":"Higher Education","c":"City","t":"2026-11-16T20:19:25+05:30","g":["NET-SET","Struggle Committee","Assistant professors","Higher Education","Maharashtra"],"b":"NET-SET, PhD holders began an indefinite sit-in in Pune on Monday, outside the office of the Director of Higher Education on Senapati Bapat Road, over 5,012 assistant professor posts that are still vacant.\nThe NET-SET, PhD Holders Struggle Committee, Maharashtra State, alleged that nine months after the state government issued a Government Resolution (GR) to recruit 5,012 assistant professors in aided colleges across the state, not a single appointment has been made. It claimed that universities have not prepared even the score sheets needed to start the recruitment, bringing the process to a standstill.\nThe committee also alleged that appointing professors on a Clock Hour Basis (CHB) violates University Grants Commission (UGC) guidelines. Its state coordinator said that CHB teachers, appointed for nine months on paper, often receive an honorarium for barely six months, as it is stopped during the Diwali vacation, the summer vacation and the examination period.\nThe state coordinator said a petition challenging the CHB system, filed before the Aurangabad Bench in 2023, is awaiting a decision.\nThe committee demands equal pay for equal work and an end to the CHB system. It also demands the recruitment completed immediately and transparently, and a clear GR on assessing professors' workload under NEP 2020. It says such a GR would help protect nearly 33,000 aided professor posts across Maharashtra.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-signal-timers-blank-police-say-pmc-not-paid-bills.html","h":"Pune signal countdown timers go blank; police say PMC had not paid electricity bills on time","s":"Deputy Commissioner of Police (Traffic) Sandeep Bhajibhakre says the pending electricity bills of the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) have now been paid.","k":"Pune traffic signals","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T20:07:42+05:30","g":["Pune traffic signals","Countdown timers","PMC"],"b":"At several major Pune traffic signals the red, yellow and green lights still work, but the countdown timers have gone blank.\nThe digital countdown indicators are blank at Swargate, Alka Chowk, Bibwewadi, Laxmi Narayan Chowk, Mitramandal Chowk and Lal Mahal Chowk. Signals along Pune RTO Road, Pune Railway Station Road and several other stretches are also affected.\nCommuters are left guessing how long they must wait. They say the missing timers make it hard to anticipate signal changes, particularly during peak hours, and raise the chance of motorists jumping signals.\nAn autorickshaw driver at Swargate said that at certain junctions traffic police regulate traffic by hand while CCTV cameras keep monitoring vehicles, and drivers often receive online-generated challans.\nSandeep Bhajibhakre, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Traffic), said several signals stopped working properly because the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) had not paid electricity bills on time. He said the pending bills have now been paid, some signals are also quite old, and the police have coordinated with PMC officials to restore the systems.","i":"illustration-e97685345c","a":[]},{"u":"pune/kasarwadi-pool-equipment-worth-lakhs-allegedly-stolen-before-opening.html","h":"Kasarwadi swimming pool: equipment worth lakhs stolen days before opening","s":"CCTV cameras, lights, showers and taps were among the items allegedly stolen from a Kasarwadi swimming pool days before its planned opening for citizens.","k":"Kasarwadi","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T19:56:48+05:30","g":["Kasarwadi","Swimming Pool","PCMC","Theft"],"b":"In a major theft, thieves allegedly cut through the metal security boundary of the Bharat Ratna Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Swimming Pool in Kasarwadi on November 9, days before the pool's planned opening for citizens, and stole equipment worth lakhs.\nThe items allegedly stolen include CCTV cameras, electrical wires, MCBs, lights, bathroom fittings, showers and taps. Two cricket bats from a nearby academy were also allegedly stolen.\nSecurity guards were deployed in all three shifts, yet the theft came to light only on November 12. The incident has raised questions over the safety of municipal properties.\nThe PCMC Sports Department has assured further action, including a police complaint and an inquiry into the security arrangements.","i":"illustration-6b5ade9ad1","a":["Kasarwadi"]},{"u":"pune/hawkers-case-supreme-court-orders-pcmc-commissioner-suryavanshi.html","h":"Hawkers’ case: Supreme Court orders PCMC Commissioner Vijay Suryavanshi to appear in person","s":"Labour leader Kashinath Nakhate has petitioned the Supreme Court, through the Maharashtra Feriwala Kranti Mahasangh with senior advocate Colin Gonsalves, over action against hawkers in the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation area.","k":"Hawkers’ case","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-16T19:44:38+05:30","g":["Supreme Court","PCMC","Street Vendors Act","Hawkers","Pimpri-Chinchwad"],"b":"A Supreme Court bench of Justice Vikram Nath and Justice Aparesh Kumar Singh has ordered PCMC Commissioner Vijay Suryavanshi to appear in person at the hawkers’ case hearing on 17 November.\nThe Supreme Court will hear on 17 November a petition over the action against hawkers in the Pimpri-Chinchwad Municipal Corporation area and the implementation of the Street Vendors Act. Suryavanshi had also had to appear in court on 13 October 2026.\nLabour leader Kashinath Nakhate filed the petition through the Maharashtra Feriwala Kranti Mahasangh, with senior advocate Colin Gonsalves.\nThe federation says a 2022 PCMC survey recorded 19,792 vendors, including pavement sellers, handcart owners and stall holders, but they were not given hawker certificates and identity cards on time.\nIt alleges that vendors’ goods were being seized without meetings of the town vending committee and without proper implementation of the law. It says the action continued in some wards even though the Supreme Court had earlier stayed it, and has also told the court that disabled vendors are suffering from the action.\nAccording to the federation, the legal fight has won state government approval for the town vending committee, and the hawker certificates and identity cards pending for four years are now being handed out; thousands of vendors who paid the ₹1,400 fee have received certificates.\n“The order for the commissioner to appear in person is serious notice of this issue. This is happening for the first time in the history of the corporation,” Nakhate said, adding that the struggle will go on until hawkers get legal protection, a rightful place, certificates and a chance to do business with dignity.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/kothrud-aap-criminal-case-hilledge-alleged-hill-excavation.html","h":"Kothrud: AAP calls for criminal case against Hilledge Realty and Developers over alleged hill excavation","s":"The Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) says the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) earlier issued Hilledge Realty and Developers LLP a stop-work notice, but stopping the work alone is not enough.","k":"Kothrud","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T19:33:43+05:30","g":["Kothrud","PMC","Aam Aadmi Party","Hill excavation"],"b":"Over alleged unauthorised excavation at Sutardara in Kothrud, the Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) has called on the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) to file a criminal case against Hilledge Realty and Developers LLP, and to carry out an immediate Electronic Total Station (ETS) survey.\nAAP alleged in a representation to the municipal commissioner that a hill in the Biodiversity Park (BDP) and hilltop area of Survey No. 113 had been cut without permission, causing significant environmental damage.\nAAP said the PMC had earlier issued the developer a stop-work notice and ordered excavation using JCB machinery to stop. The party said stopping the work alone was not enough and called for legal action against those responsible for damaging the hill.\nAAP wants the survey to measure the quantity of excavated minor minerals. It also sought the suspension of any officials found to have supported or allowed the alleged unauthorised work.\nAAP also wants a detailed report on the number of trees cut at the site, and the developer directed to plant new trees equivalent in total age to those removed.\nRaviraj Baban Kale, state president of AAP’s Maharashtra youth wing, urged the municipal commissioner to intervene and take strict action. Kale also sought written details on the land survey, the extent of excavation, the status of permissions and an assessment of the environmental damage.","i":"","a":["Kothrud"]},{"u":"pune/pune-phone-hacks-cost-11-residents-about-76-lakh-in-15-days.html","h":"Phone hacks cost 11 Pune residents about ₹76 lakh in 15 days","s":"A fake ‘APK’ file, once installed on a phone, lets fraudsters divert its calls and bank OTPs to another number.","k":"Phone hacks","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-16T19:18:46+05:30","g":["Phone hacks","APK files","Wagholi","Pune"],"b":"Phone hacks have cost 11 Pune residents about ₹76 lakh in 15 days, with fraudsters hacking the phones and taking remote access to them.\nThe victims are from Swargate, Wagholi, Lohegaon, Kondhwa, Kothrud, the airport area and Bharati Vidyapeeth.\nThe bait is a message about an RTO e-challan, an unpaid gas bill or free movies, with a link on WhatsApp or SMS to a fake ‘APK’ file. Once it is installed, the fraudsters get access to the phone, divert its calls and bank OTPs to another number, and empty the bank accounts.\nIn Wagholi, a hacker took over the phone of a woman accountant at a company's office, deleted the number of a director's brother and saved his own number under that name. He then asked her on WhatsApp to transfer ₹16 lakh to a bank account, and she sent it, taking it as the brother's message. A case has been registered at Wagholi police station.\nOther cases: ₹12 lakh through an APK file and ₹7.5 lakh through remote access in Lohegaon; ₹8.7 lakh taken from a woman's phone in the airport area; ₹6.81 lakh from a businessman through a fake e-challan app in Swargate; ₹6.25 lakh and ₹3.5 lakh in Bharati Vidyapeeth; ₹6 lakh from a senior citizen in Kondhwa.\nSenior Police Inspector Swapnali Shinde of the Pune City Cyber Police Station has asked citizens not to click any unknown link received on WhatsApp or SMS, and especially not to download files with the ‘.apk’ extension.\nDownload apps only from the Play Store or App Store, check RTO challans and gas bills only on the official website or app, and if you suspect your phone is hacked, switch off the internet and change your bank and UPI passwords at once.","i":"illustration-80ed72160b","a":["Wagholi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-firefighter-climbs-bsnl-tower-in-camp-to-bring-down-man.html","h":"Firefighter climbs BSNL tower in Camp, brings down man who threatened to end his life","s":"A man who threatened to end his life from a mobile tower in Camp was rescued with support from driver Sachin Pawar, Rohit Ranpise, team leader Asif Shaikh, Abhijit Ghumthakar and Ajit Dabde.","k":"Camp","c":"City","t":"2026-11-16T19:03:37+05:30","g":["Camp","BSNL","Pune Cantonment Fire Brigade","Pune"],"b":"Firefighter Mahendra Mahamuni brought down a man who had threatened to end his life on a mobile tower at the BSNL office on Tarapore Road in Pune’s Camp area, opposite the ISKCON Temple.\nThe Pune Cantonment Fire Brigade received an emergency call on 101 and a team rushed to the spot. When repeated attempts by firefighters to persuade the man from the ground failed, Mahamuni climbed the tower himself.\nMahamuni kept speaking to the man as he approached, calmed him and gradually convinced him to come down safely.\nDriver Sachin Pawar, Rohit Ranpise, team leader Asif Shaikh, Abhijit Ghumthakar and Ajit Dabde supported the rescue. The reason for the man’s distress has not been made known.","i":"illustration-6682a8379d","a":["Pune Camp","Camp","Pune Cantonment area"]},{"u":"pune/ajit-pawar-crash-rohit-pawar-calls-fadnavis-alleged-muffler-man.html","h":"Ajit Pawar crash: Rohit Pawar calls CM Fadnavis alleged ‘Muffler Man’","s":"Allegations by NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar against Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis have put the Ajit Pawar plane crash investigation in the political spotlight again.","k":"‘Muffler Man’","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-16T18:50:27+05:30","g":["Rohit Pawar","Devendra Fadnavis","Muffler Man","Ajit Pawar"],"b":"At a press conference in Mumbai, NCP (SP) MLA Rohit Pawar called Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis the alleged ‘Muffler Man’, answering questions about the plane crash that claimed the life of former Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar.\nRohit Pawar alleged that Fadnavis had a role in protecting VSR Ventures and V.K. Singh. He also pointed out that Fadnavis had attended a wedding in Jaipur.\nThe allegations have brought the Ajit Pawar plane crash investigation back into the political spotlight.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-commuters-try-to-rush-blockades-chandani-chowk-amit-shah-visit.html","h":"‘For how long shall we wait?’ Commuters try to rush blockades at Chandani Chowk as Amit Shah visits","s":"Near Chandani Chowk in Pune, road blockades stopped traffic during Amit Shah’s visit; a video shows commuters on two-wheelers arguing with police officers at the barricades.","k":"Chandani Chowk","c":"City","t":"2026-11-16T18:38:19+05:30","g":["Chandani Chowk","Amit Shah","Commuters","Road blockades"],"b":"Commuters tried to rush through road blockades near Chandani Chowk in Pune during Amit Shah’s visit, and a video shows them arguing with police officers at the barricades.\nRoad blockades stopped traffic, and the commuters were asking, “For how long shall we wait?”\nThe video shows commuters on two-wheelers at the barricades as riders try to push past.","i":"","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-ravet-illegal-pavana-water-extraction-detected-tanker-operators-warned.html","h":"Illegal Pavana water extraction detected in Ravet, tanker operators warned","s":"Illegal extraction of water from the Pavana River in Ravet was detected by the Water Resources Department, which has warned tanker operators and builders of legal action.","k":"Pavana River, Ravet","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T17:10:10+05:30","g":["Pavana River","Ravet","Pimpri-Chinchwad","Water Resources Department"],"b":"The Water Resources Department has detected illegal extraction of water from the Pavana River in Ravet, and a team led by Executive Engineer Kiran Deshmukh inspected the site. It was detected amid water shortages and alternate-day supply in Pimpri-Chinchwad.\nOperators were allegedly pumping river water into a nearby well, then filling tankers and selling it to builders and private establishments for commercial use. The team found an unauthorised pipeline connected to the well.\nThose involved have been directed to remove the equipment and dismantle the illegal pumping arrangements. The Water Resources Department has warned tanker operators and builders of legal action if unauthorised extraction continues.","i":"illustration-498312071c","a":["Ravet"]},{"u":"pune/ambegaon-pump-employee-allegedly-assaulted-refusing-petrol-bottle.html","h":"Ambegaon pump employee allegedly assaulted for refusing petrol in bottle","s":"Three men allegedly abused, assaulted and threatened to kill a petrol pump employee who refused to dispense petrol into an empty bottle, and Ambegaon Police have registered a case.","k":"Ambegaon","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-16T16:39:34+05:30","g":["Ambegaon","Petrol pump","Ambegaon Police","Pune"],"b":"An employee at Beldare Petrol Pump in Pune’s Ambegaon area was allegedly assaulted by three men between 2 pm and 3 pm on November 15, 2026, after he refused to dispense petrol into an empty bottle, citing safety regulations.\nAccording to the complaint, the men arrived on a two-wheeler and demanded petrol in a bottle. When the employee refused and asked them to use another dispensing point, an argument broke out. The men allegedly abused him, assaulted him and threatened to kill him.\nAmbegaon Police have registered a case under relevant provisions of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), and further investigation is underway. Police have also initiated preventive legal action to maintain peace in the area.","i":"illustration-5355841610","a":[]},{"u":"pune/suspected-gas-blast-shree-sant-gadge-maharaj-vasahat-koregaon-park.html","h":"Suspected gas blast at Shree Sant Gadge Maharaj Vasahat in Koregaon Park","s":"Details of a suspected gas blast on South Main Road in Koregaon Park are awaited.","k":"Koregaon Park","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-16T15:58:54+05:30","g":["Gas blast","Koregaon Park","Pune"],"b":"Shree Sant Gadge Maharaj Vasahat on South Main Road in Koregaon Park, Pune, was the site of a suspected gas blast.\nDetails on the cause of the blast, casualties and property damage are awaited.","i":"","a":["Koregaon Park","KP","Koregaon Park Annexe"]},{"u":"pune/pune-coep-flags-slow-mula-riverfront-work-100th-regatta.html","h":"COEP flags slow Mula riverfront work ahead of 100th Regatta in 2028","s":"COEP Technological University officials said they are yet to receive a response from the Municipal Commissioner and City Engineer they wrote to six months ago.","k":"COEP Regatta","c":"Civic","t":"2026-11-16T15:36:06+05:30","g":["COEP","Regatta","Mula river","Riverfront Development"],"b":"Ahead of the 100th edition of its iconic annual Regatta, set for 2028, COEP Technological University has raised concerns over how slowly Riverfront Development (RFD) work is moving along the Boat Club side of the Mula river.\nFinal preparations are slated to begin by March 2027.\nThe rugged and incomplete stretch on the COEP side is hampering year-round student rowing practice, although the opposite Sangamwadi bank has undergone visible beautification.\nUniversity officials said they wrote to Municipal Commissioner Naval Kishore Ram and City Engineer Aniruddha Pawaskar six months ago, offering alumni backing and seeking civic support, and are yet to receive a response.\nRFD Superintending Engineer Bipin Shinde said multiple coordination meetings have already been held with COEP. The Central Water and Power Research Station (CWPRS) has been appointed to verify river cross-sections after this year's water-level rise, to ensure any construction does not cause waterlogging inside the campus.","i":"illustration-b55f45fd34","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-fadnavis-asks-shah-expedite-ajit-pawar-plane-crash-probe.html","h":"‘Accident or something more?’: Fadnavis asks Shah to expedite Ajit Pawar plane crash probe","s":"Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis said Union Home Minister Amit Shah had assured him he would try to expedite the investigation into the plane crash that killed Ajit Pawar.","k":"Ajit Pawar crash probe","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-16T15:25:25+05:30","g":["Ajit Pawar","Devendra Fadnavis","Amit Shah","Baramati","Pune"],"b":"Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis said people wanted to know whether the plane crash that killed former Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar was an accident or whether something more lay behind it, and urged Union Home Minister Amit Shah on Monday, 16 November, to expedite the probe. He was speaking at the unveiling of Ajit Pawar's bust at the Pune Zilla Parishad headquarters, and urged that the findings be made public at the earliest.\nFadnavis said he had personally requested Shah to intervene, and that Shah had assured him he would look into the matter and try to expedite the process.\n“Nearly eight, nine, 10 months have passed, and a major investigation is underway with people and teams from America and various countries assisting in the probe. But the confusion in the minds of the common people of Maharashtra must be cleared,” Fadnavis said.\nShah unveiled the bust, and the main entrance gate of the Pune Zilla Parishad headquarters was named after Ajit Pawar.\nAjit Pawar died on 28 January 2026, when a Learjet 45 carrying him from Mumbai to Baramati crashed while attempting to land near Baramati airport. All five people aboard died.\nThe Aircraft Accident Investigation Bureau's preliminary report of 28 February flagged poor visibility, inadequate navigational and weather facilities at the airport, faded runway markings and loose gravel, and did not establish any foul play. The final report is still awaited.","i":"","a":["Baramati","Baramati city","Baramati taluka"]},{"u":"pune/pune-court-life-term-burkegaon-man-axes-wife-to-death.html","h":"Burkegaon man, drunk on suspicion, axes wife to death; Pune court awards life term","s":"A Pune sessions court has given a Burkegaon man life imprisonment instead of the death penalty for killing his wife, ruling that the case did not fall under the ‘rarest of rare’ category.","k":"Burkegaon","c":"Courts","t":"2026-11-16T14:54:47+05:30","g":["Burkegaon","Pune court","Life imprisonment","DNA analysis"],"b":"In a judgment delivered on November 7, 2026, a Pune sessions court sentenced a 53-year-old Burkegaon man to life imprisonment for killing his wife with an axe on July 23, 2024.\nAdditional Sessions Judge H M Bhosale also imposed a fine of ₹10,000, with three months of rigorous imprisonment in default.\nAccording to the prosecution, the man repeatedly questioned his wife’s character and frequently ill-treated her under the influence of alcohol. The murder came to light when the couple’s daughter reached the house at around 12.30 pm, after her mother did not answer calls or report for work.\nShe found her mother lying in a pool of blood with a bloodstained axe nearby. The man was allegedly sleeping in the same room. When she woke him, he allegedly told her that he had killed her mother with the axe.\nThe woman was declared dead at Sassoon Hospital. The post-mortem found 16 external injuries, including wounds to her head, neck and back.\nBlood on the man’s shirt matched her DNA profile. So did bloodstains on the axe, on the woman’s blouse and in samples from the scene. DNA analysis played a crucial role in the conviction.\nThe defence claimed the man was outside the house at the time. The court rejected this, relying on the daughter’s testimony, the forensic evidence and other circumstances. It ruled that the case did not fall under the ‘rarest of rare’ category and awarded life imprisonment instead of the death penalty.\nAdditional Public Prosecutor N P Konghe represented the prosecution.","i":"illustration-9ee302bb38","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-bj-medical-college-student-missing-four-months-parents-dark-diwali.html","h":"Pune: BJ Medical College student missing four months, parents spent a dark Diwali","s":"The father of a missing first-year BJ Medical College student has accused a few students of ragging his son; Bund Garden police say they “could not find any evidence of harassment”.","k":"Missing student","c":"City","t":"2026-11-16T14:43:51+05:30","g":["Pune","Kharadi","BJ Medical College","Missing student"],"b":"A first-year BJ Medical College student from Kolhapur who vanished on July 18 after leaving a friend’s residence in Kharadi is still missing four months on, and his parents have spent a dark Diwali.\nHis father said the student’s friends told the family he was being bullied and discriminated against because he came from a village, while most of his batchmates were from the city. The father has accused a few students of ragging his son and filed a complaint at the Bund Garden police station.\nSenior Inspector Santosh Pandhare of the Bund Garden police station said police recorded statements from the student’s hostel roommates and batchmates, the faculty and the students the family accused of ragging, but “could not find any evidence of harassment.”\nA missing person’s complaint has been lodged at the Kharadi police station. Senior Inspector Sanjay Chavan of the Kharadi police station said teams were sent to Goa, Nashik and Beed.\nThe student’s phone was last traced within the jurisdiction of the Uruli Kanchan police station, and police learnt he had boarded a train heading toward Solapur, but the cameras at Daund railway station were not operational, so the lead was lost. His details have been uploaded to the national grid.\nDr Eknath Pawar, dean of BJ Medical College, said the college has been cooperating with the police, does not tolerate ragging or bullying, and has a robust complaint redressal mechanism.","i":"illustration-99e6cd7f11","a":["Kharadi"]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-form-20-member-team-fix-26-accident-black-spots.html","h":"Pune police form 20-member team to fix 26 accident black spots","s":"Traffic signals, blinkers and rumble strips are among the immediate measures, and pedestrian bridges and flyovers among the long-term ones, for 26 accident black spots.","k":"Accident black spots","c":"Accidents and fires","t":"2026-11-16T14:33:11+05:30","g":["Pune police","Black spots","Navale Bridge","Katraj-Dehu Road Bypass","Accidents"],"b":"Pune police formed a 20-member special team about a month ago to fix 26 accident black spots on the Katraj-Dehu Road Bypass, the Pune-Solapur Highway, the Pune-Nagar Highway and other city roads.\nThe black spots claimed 226 lives in three years. Police classify a location as a black spot after five or more accidents there.\nNavale Bridge on the Mumbai-Bengaluru highway is the deadliest, with 26 fatal accidents between 2024 and 2026; 17 of them came in 2025 alone. Perne Phata on the Pune-Ahmednagar highway recorded 16, and Kadamvak Vasti on the Pune-Solapur highway 15.\nTo study recurring fatal crashes and recommend fixes, the team conducts joint inspections with the PMC, the state PWD, NHAI and local police stations.\nImmediate measures include traffic signals and blinkers, rumble strips, filling potholes, rerouting traffic, regulating heavy vehicles and correcting road levels. Long-term measures include widening roads, pedestrian bridges and flyovers.\nSpecial attention is being paid to the Katraj-Dehu Road Bypass, with the aim of cutting accidents by at least 20% to 30% over the next couple of years, Deputy Commissioner of Police (Traffic) Sandip Bhajibhakre said.","i":"illustration-a647f73700","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-faraskhana-police-fly-two-accused-kolkata-flight-cost-questioned.html","h":"Faraskhana police fly two accused from Kolkata to Pune; flight cost questioned","s":"Faraskhana police flew two people accused in separate cases from Kolkata to Pune, and who decided on a flight when rail was available remains an open question.","k":"Faraskhana police","c":"Crime","t":"2026-11-16T14:22:38+05:30","g":["Faraskhana police","Kolkata","Pune","flight cost"],"b":"Two accused who fled Pune for Kolkata after cases were registered were detained there and flown back to Pune by Faraskhana police.\nThe two are accused in separate cases that Faraskhana police were investigating. In the first case, 17 kg of silver jewellery and silver bars worth ₹40.90 lakh were stolen from a jeweller’s shop in Ganesh Peth. A craftsman at the shop was suspected. The shop owner checked CCTV footage, which showed him leaving the shop with a large bag around dawn.\nIn the second case, 1,850 grams of pure gold was taken from a Raviwar Peth jeweller on the pretext of making ornaments and was allegedly never returned, an embezzlement of about ₹2.59 crore. A case was registered against the accused and his manager.\nOn learning the two were in Kolkata, a team of one police officer and three personnel went in pursuit of them.\nQuestions are now being raised over the cost of the air travel, whether senior officers had given permission, and whether administrative approval was obtained. The investigation team is understood to have said it flew at the last minute because it missed its train.\nWho decided on a flight when rail was available, how much it cost and whether it was paid from government funds remain open questions, as does whether senior police officers will order an inquiry into the expense.","i":"illustration-b9deaa5cc1","a":[]},{"u":"pune/pune-police-detain-congress-worker-facebook-post-amit-shah-visit.html","h":"Pune Police detain Congress worker over Facebook post as Amit Shah visits","s":"A Congress worker detained by Pune Police over a Facebook post was taken into custody by Airport Police as a security measure.","k":"Amit Shah visit","c":"Politics","t":"2026-11-16T14:12:01+05:30","g":["Pune Police","Amit Shah","Ajit Pawar","Congress","Facebook post"],"b":"During Union Home Minister Amit Shah’s Pune visit, Pune Police detained a Congress worker over a Facebook post in which he demanded that Shah first get a case registered over the accident involving the late Deputy Chief Minister Ajit Pawar, and only then unveil his statue.\nShah was due to unveil the statue of the late Ajit Pawar at the Pune Zilla Parishad.\nAirport Police took the worker into custody as a security measure. The police have not said anything further about the detention, and whether he has since been released is not yet clear.","i":"","a":[]}]});window.__pvIdx&&window.__pvIdx();
